    { key = "E1z8", text = "[E1z8] (QoL 0.7.20: the boxes moved to a Change column at the far right, Rating shows the rating as text, and the ability lists are one nested line per ability: E1z20.) (QoL 0.7.15; Stat Calculator columns, Xaya 2026-11-05: \"do multiple columns: for cleaner presentation * Stat || Current Value || Pt Value || etc\") Open the character window with the Stat Calculator on, Stats tab, panel at its default size (QoL > Character Toolkit > Panel > Layout > Reset size). |cffffd100Expect:|r under each section header (Primary stats, Secondary stats, Tertiary stats, Offense, Defense) a grey column head |cffffd100Stat ... Current value ... Pt value|r (Secondary and Tertiary also |cffffd100Rating|r over the boxes). Primary stats: Agility, its box, your Agility under Current value; \"» Attack power\": the attack power under Current value and 1.00 (attack power per Agility) under Pt value; \"» Armor\": the armor under Current value, under Pt value your mastery text's percent / 100 (0.90 for 89.7%), and under the line in grey \"89.7% of Agility, mastery\"; \"» Abilities (per 100)\": the ability list in grey on its own line, every ability readable, nothing cut off; Stamina \"» Health\": your health and the health per Stamina (21.20 in your screenshot) under Pt value. No \"(1 = ...)\" inside any value; every value's right edge lines up under \"Current value\" and every Pt value under \"Pt value\". Critical Strike: your rating in the box, the percent, \"46.0 / 1%\" (your figure) under Pt value; \"» Parry\": +X%, \"N / 1%\", \"before DR\" under it. Drag the panel's bottom-right corner out to about twice the width. |cffffd100Expect:|r a |cffffd100Note|r head appears right of Pt value and every grey note moves up beside its line in that column; drag it back narrow: the notes go back under their lines. Nothing overlaps or is cut at any width; also at text size 16 (Panel > Layout > Text size). Hover the name Agility, then one of its \"»\" lines. |cffffd100Expect:|r the same tooltip both times, with \"» Attack power  +N  (1 = 1.00)\". Hover Agility in Blizzard's character window stat list. |cffffd100Expect:|r the XayaUI block has \"» Armor  +N  (1 = 0.90); 89.7% of Agility, mastery\". Gear tab: click your helm's icon, pick a helm from your bags. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"What it changes\" has the same column head (no Rating) and its lines use it, \"now -> then\" on one line where it fits; |cffffd100Summary|r is a table, Gear || Character || Elsewhere, one row per stat. Screenshot please, narrow and wide." },
    { key = "E1z11", text = "[E1z11] (QoL 0.7.19; one item level per slot, Xaya's report of 2026-11-05 \"character pane is broken\") Settings as in her report: Blizzard UI Reskin > Character Pane: Character Reskin on, Clean window off, Item level on each slot on, Enchants beside the slots on; QoL > Character Toolkit on with Slot Overlays ticked. Open the character window (C). |cffffd100Expect:|r XayaUI draws one item level per slot, at the slot's bottom edge, in its upgrade-track colour; none on the shirt or the tabard (the shirt's \"1\" is gone); no small \"1S\" / \"2S\" on a slot whose sockets all hold a gem (those were the \"15\" / \"25\"). If a second number still shows (the large one across the middle of the icon in her screenshot), type |cff88ccff/xui reskin status|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r a line \"Text on the slots that is not XayaUI's (N): Head 334 (FrameName); ...\" naming the frames that draw it: that is another addon (her stat column's Defense / Offense / Ratings sections are not Blizzard's or XayaUI's either). Report the names it prints, or \"No other text on the slot buttons\" if it says that. Untick Item level on each slot: XayaUI's number goes; anything left is the other addon's. Tick it again. Then untick Gems and sockets beside the slots. |cffffd100Expect:|r the toolkit's orange \"1S\" shows only on a slot with an empty socket (a gem-less socket), nowhere else. Tick it again: the \"1S\" goes (the sockets show it instead, E1z13)." },
    { key = "E1z12", text = "[E1z12] (QoL 0.7.22: the enchant shows its own name without \"Enchant <slot> - \" and, with the wider window, sits between the slot and the model: E1z40, E1z44.) (QoL 0.7.19; enchant labels wrapped, Xaya 2026-11-05: \"correctly word wrap enchant lines\") Same settings, character window open, mouse away from the model. |cffffd100Expect:|r beside each enchanted slot, toward the model, the whole enchant name in green on up to three lines (e.g. \"Enchant Helm - / Empowered Rune of / Avoidance\"), no \"...\" and no word cut in half; \"No enchant\" in orange on a ticked slot without one; the left column's labels stay left of the window's middle and the right column's right of it, each within its own slot's height, none touching another; the weapons' labels sit under the side columns (left of the main hand, right of the off hand) and do not cover the weapon slots. The \"Ancient Hash'ey Battle Art: ...\" label is green like the others (it was purple: the game colours that line itself). Move the mouse onto the model: the zoom / rotate buttons appear at its top. |cffffd100Expect:|r the head row's label (and the hands row's, if it has one) hides while the buttons show; no label sits on a button; move the mouse away: the label is back. Open the stats pane (the arrow at the bottom right) and close it: the labels do not move. Report any label that is cut, overlaps something, or is hard to read; a screenshot please. Turn Enchants beside the slots off: every label goes." },
    { key = "E1z13", text = "[E1z13] (QoL 0.7.22: the sockets are rows under the enchant, bigger, with the gem's name: E1z43.) (QoL 0.7.19; gems and sockets, Xaya 2026-11-05: \"show gem sockets and gems socketed\") Blizzard UI Reskin > Character Pane: |cffffd100Expect:|r a new tick box \"Gems and sockets beside the slots\" (on) under Enchants beside the slots. Character window open. |cffffd100Expect:|r beside every slot whose item has sockets (neck and rings at least), 7 px from the slot toward the model, one small square per socket stacked down the slot's side: the gem's own icon in a filled socket, the game's empty-socket frame in an empty one; under the main hand / off hand if a weapon has a socket. Hover a gem. |cffffd100Expect:|r the gem's tooltip (its name and stat). Hover an empty socket: \"Prismatic Socket\" (or \"Empty socket\"). Compare with the item's own tooltip: the same gems in the same order. Socket a gem into an empty socket (or swap a ring): the squares follow within a moment. Untick the box: the squares go, nothing else moves. If you are on a Timerunning character, the game's own socket display shows there too: report it (two sets of sockets)." },
    { key = "E1z20", text = "[E1z20] (QoL 0.7.20; Stat Calculator, Xaya 2026-11-05: \"put the input box on the far right under a new column \"Change\"\", \"\"abilities with your number\" should be renamed to \"Ability Scaling\"\", \"ability names should be nested under abilities\") Open the character window with the Stat Calculator on, Stats tab, panel at its default size (QoL > Character Toolkit > Panel > Layout > Reset size). |cffffd100Expect:|r Primary stats' grey head reads |cffffd100Stat ... Current value ... Pt value ... Change|r; Secondary and Tertiary stats' read |cffffd100Stat ... Rating ... Current value ... Pt value ... Change|r; Offense and Defense have no Change. Every box is the last thing on its row, at the panel's right edge under |cffffd100Change|r, clear of the Pt value beside it: Agility's box holds your Agility (2616 in your screenshot) and Agility's number sits under Current value; Critical Strike reads \"Critical Strike ... 535 ... 22.63% ... 46.0 / 1% ... [535]\" (your rating under Rating as plain text, the box under Change); the same for Haste, Mastery, Versatility, Avoidance, Leech, Speed and the All ratings box. Under \"» Abilities (per 100)\" each ability is its own line, indented one step further than the \"»\" lines, with its number under Current value (Sigil of Spite +1,115, Fel Devastation +1,100, Fiery Brand +670, Fracture +444 in your screenshot, in that order); no comma list anywhere. Haste: under \"» Abilities (their text names Haste)\" one ability per line with \"N s recharge\" under Current value where it has charges. Click Agility's box, type your Agility + 4 (2620 in your screenshot), press Enter. |cffffd100Expect:|r a line |cffffd100» Ability Scaling|r (no \"Abilities with your number\" anywhere, also not in the hover) with each ability on its own indented line and \"now -> then\" in green under Current value (Sigil of Spite 38,524 -> 38,569 ...). Type 200 more than your crit rating in Critical Strike's box, press Enter. |cffffd100Expect:|r Rating still shows your own rating, the box shows what you typed, Current value \"now -> then\". Clear both boxes: back to yours. Hover the name Agility. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"» Abilities (per 100)\" then one indented line per ability with its number; the hover covers the row up to the box, and clicking the box still puts the cursor in it. Hover Agility in Blizzard's character window stat list. |cffffd100Expect:|r the same indented ability lines in the XayaUI block. Drag the panel's corner out to about twice the width. |cffffd100Expect:|r a |cffffd100Note|r head between Pt value and Change, the boxes still at the far right. Text size 16 and the narrowest panel: nothing overlaps or is cut, every box still usable (you can click it and type). Report any name that wraps onto two lines at the default size (by the offline estimate \"Critical Strike\" may). Gear tab: compare a helm with more Agility. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"What it changes\" has no Rating and no Change head, and shows \"» Ability Scaling\" with the abilities nested under it. Screenshot please, default and wide, with a number typed." },
    { key = "E1z41", text = "[E1z41] (QoL 0.7.22; the background, Xaya 2026-11-05: \"the current invisible background is not good\") Character Reskin on, Clean window off. Open and close the character window three times. |cffffd100Expect:|r every time a solid dark background behind the whole window (the slots, the model area, the stat list and the added width): the game world does not show through. Tick Clean window, open and close it three times again. |cffffd100Expect:|r the same solid background with a thin border, no stone frame or portrait, the stat list on the theme's pane colour. Drag Background opacity to 50%, then 100%. |cffffd100Expect:|r a little see-through at 50%, fully solid at 100%. Change XayaUI's theme (Settings > Theme). |cffffd100Expect:|r the window's background follows it. Untick Character Reskin. |cffffd100Expect:|r Blizzard's own window back, its normal width." },
    { key = "E1z43", text = "[E1z43] (QoL 0.7.22; gems, Xaya 2026-11-05: \"gemstone display is much too small and doesn't show the gem name socketed\") Character Reskin on with Gems on. |cffffd100Expect:|r under each slot's enchant one row per socket: the gem's icon (about a third of a slot icon; a little smaller on a crowded slot such as a ring with an enchant and two gems) and the gem's name in white; an empty socket shows \"Prismatic Socket\" (or its type) in orange with the empty socket frame. Hover a gem's row. |cffffd100Expect:|r the gem's own tooltip. If a gem shows its icon but no name, wait a moment or reopen the window. |cffffd100Expect:|r the name fills in. No \"1S\" / \"2S\" marks on the slots." },
    { key = "E1z44", text = "[E1z44] (QoL 0.7.22; hover, Xaya 2026-11-05: \"hovering over the enchant name ... should also allow you to see what the enchant does\", \"embellished items should be hoverable so you can read what the embellishment does\") Hover a ring's enchant line (\"Eyes of the Eagle\"). |cffffd100Expect:|r a tooltip with the game's line (\"Enchanted: Enchant Ring - Eyes of the Eagle\") and \"Effect text not given by the game.\" (the game does not hand an addon the enchant's effect text: please tell us if the slot's own item tooltip shows more for it). Hover the legs' line. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Enchanted: +41 Agility/Strength & +27 Armor\" and nothing more. On an embellished item |cffffd100Expect:|r a light-blue line \"Embellished (n/2)\" (n = how many you wear); hover it: \"Unique-Equipped: Embellished (2)\", the item's Equip line as the game shows it, \"n of 2 embellished items worn.\" Tell us if an embellished item shows no such line (it is found by the word \"Embellished\" in the item's tooltip). Click and shift-click a slot right next to its lines. |cffffd100Expect:|r the slot works as always (the lines take the mouse only over themselves)." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-look-4", { title = "2. Looks and layout (no effect on use) (4 of 6)", order = 200.04, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "E1z21", text = "[E1z21] (QoL 0.7.21; Stat Calculator, Xaya 2026-11-05: default width \"can be increased to cleanly fit all columns with default selected user font up to 450px\"; the Rating cell \"should show alongside the +/- stat amount\") QoL > Character Toolkit > Panel > Layout > Reset size, then open the character window with the Stat Calculator on, Stats tab, default text size. |cffffd100Expect:|r the panel is 450 wide (was 380); every column head, every stat name (\"Critical Strike\" included) and \"» Abilities (per 100)\" sit on one line; nothing is cut. Type 172 more than your crit rating into Critical Strike's box, press Enter. |cffffd100Expect:|r the Rating cell reads your rating and the change, e.g. \"528 +172\", on one line; type less than yours: \"528 -28\"; clear the box: only your rating. The Note column now appears from a panel about 584 wide (was 540). A width you had dragged the panel to before is kept, so Reset size first. Screenshot please, with a number typed." },
    { key = "E1z47", text = "[E1z47] (QoL 0.7.23; Min / Max, Xaya: \"two configured sizes -- one smaller and one larger (NOT full screen, just longer) -- as well as the free resize option in the bottom corner\") |cffffd100Expect:|r a |cffffd100Max|r button left of the panel's close X; click it: the panel grows to the larger height (760 to start) and the button reads |cffffd100Min|r; click it: back to 440. Drag the bottom-right corner while large: it resizes freely, and Max / Min then give that height for the large size. QoL > Character Toolkit > Panel > Layout: Smaller height / Larger height move the two heights; Reset size puts back the width and both heights." },
    { key = "E1z48", text = "[E1z48] (QoL 0.7.23; Character Stats, Xaya: \"combine primary, secondary, and tertiary stats into one major section under the name \"Character Stats\"\") Stat Calculator > Stats. |cffffd100Expect:|r two headers, |cffffd100Character Stats|r then |cffffd100Stat Weights|r. Inside Character Stats: Core Stats with Primary (your primary stat, Stamina), General (Health, your resource, Global cooldown, Movement speed), Offensive (Attack Power / Spell Power, Attack Speed, Weapon DPS, Damage, Critical strike effectiveness), Defensive (Armor, Dodge, Parry, Block); then Secondaries, Tertiaries, Gear Summary (Gear || Character || Elsewhere). No All ratings line; no Durability or Repair anywhere (Stats, Gear, a clicked slot); the Gear tab has Equipped and Compare only. Resource: on a Mana / Energy / Focus spec the total and a generation rate; on a builder (Fury, Rage, Runic Power...) its maximum and no rate; on a Death Knight both Runic Power and Runes (one rune's recharge time, read while a rune recharges; tell us the number it shows against the rune bar). Critical strike effectiveness: with a ring enchant such as Eyes of the Eagle, \"+2%\" per such text, \"read from item text\"; hover it for the item lines it came from. Tell us if your client's text is worded differently (nothing found although an item says it)." },
    { key = "E1z51", text = "[E1z51] (QoL 0.7.24; spell columns and the button, Xaya: \"Spell Name (spell id underneath) || % PSV (underneath each entry show \"1 agility = {value}\") || Talent Modifiers\"; \"remove \"usable now\" from spirit bomb\"; \"a centered button that is no more than 250px wide\") |cffffd100Expect:|r the |cffffd100Refresh spell data|r button above \"- Active spells\", centred, a clear button (border, lights up on hover), at most 250 px wide; click it: the list reads again. Under the header a column head |cffffd100Spell Name || % PSV || Talent Modifiers || Computed Value|r (QoL 0.7.24, her \"Fourth column - computed Value\"); each spell: its name with \"Spell ID: N\" under it, \"N% of attack power\" in % PSV with \"1 Agility = N\" (your primary stat) under it, the talents that name it in Talent Modifiers (\"none\" otherwise), its number (38,011) in Computed Value; nothing else in the table (no Value column, no note or \"Entered\" line). Spirit Bomb (and every other spell) has no \"Usable now\" line. Drag the panel narrow and wide and try text sizes 8 and 16: nothing overlaps or runs out of its column." },
    { key = "E1z52", text = "[E1z52] (QoL 0.7.24; equipped selection and slot names, Xaya: \"selecting an item ... should highlight the box ... clicking it again should deselect it\"; \"ring slot #1, ring slot #2, trinket slot #1, trinket slot #2 ... main-hand and off-hand\") Stat Calculator > Gear. |cffffd100Expect:|r click your first ring: its icon gets a coloured frame and the section reads \"Compare: Ring slot #1\"; click it again: the frame goes and the comparison clears. The second ring: \"Ring slot #2\"; trinkets \"Trinket slot #1 / #2\"; weapons \"Main-hand\" / \"Off-hand\". With two rings equipped and an item picked, the \"Replacing\" / \"Replace instead\" lines name \"Ring slot #1\" / \"Ring slot #2\"." },
    { key = "E1z53", text = "[E1z53] (QoL 0.7.24; bag items as icons, several at once, Xaya: \"compare item sublist should be icons like the equipped gear display ... compare items should support multi-item selection and display\") With a ring slot selected and two or three rings in your bags. |cffffd100Expect:|r the bag rings as icons with their item level under each (best first); hover: the game's item tooltip. Click one: its box is framed and its name appears in the Item box; click a second and a third: all framed, the Item box shows the last; the Changes table has a column for each (Equipped || ring A || ring B || ring C). A fourth lets the first go. Click a framed one: it is let go and its column disappears. Typing an item ID in the box and pressing Enter still adds that item. On a narrow panel (or text size 16) fewer columns show and a line says how many more are picked." },
    { key = "E1z60", text = "[E1z60] (QoL 0.7.24; the wider character window, Xaya 2026-11-06: \"Push to 380px before stats pane and request feedback confirmation\") Character Reskin on with its default settings (Blizzard UI Reskin > Character Pane; |cffffd100Extra width|r now goes from 0 to 300 and starts at 42). Open the character window, stats pane closed, then open. |cffffd100Expect:|r 380 px wide without the stats pane (Blizzard's is 338) and 582 with it (Blizzard's 540); the model whole and centred. At 380 only about 18 px is left between each slot column and the model, so |cffffd100no enchant, embellishment or gem block is drawn beside the head, neck, shoulders, chest, wrists, waist, legs, feet or rings|r (they never cover the model or its camera buttons); only the two weapons' blocks show, under the side columns. Set |cffffd100Extra width|r to 240: every block is back, whole. Please tell us how 380 looks and what you want next (her feedback, REQUEST-LOG #56)." },
    { key = "E1z61", text = "[E1z61] (QoL 0.7.24; gem icons, her answer \"16 px\") |cffffd100Extra width|r 240. |cffffd100Expect:|r gem and empty-socket icons beside the slots 16 px (one more than 14, against the game's own 11 px); on a ring with an enchant and two sockets they drop to 12 px so the block fits its slot's height. Hover a gem: its tooltip." },
    { key = "E1z62", text = "[E1z62] (QoL 0.7.24; embellishments, Xaya: \"put Embellished - Name: ______ and a line break before the description\"; \"pane line says embellished (2/2): name — the rest goes in tooltip\") |cffffd100Extra width|r 240, an embellished item on. |cffffd100Expect:|r beside it a light-blue line \"Embellished (1/2): <the item's name>\" ((2/2) when you wear two, on each). Hover it: \"Embellished - Name: <the item's name>\", then on the next line its effect as the game words it (its Equip / Use line), nothing else. Tell us if the game's tooltip names the embellishment itself somewhere (the name shown is the item's: no documented call names the embellishment)." },
    { key = "E1z70", text = "[E1z70] (QoL 0.7.28; REQUEST-LOG #60 / #62, her answer \"Titles centred over columns\") Stat Calculator > Stats at its default width (Panel > Layout > Reset size), text size 11; scroll to |cffffd100Stat Weights|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the heads read |cffffd100Stat || Rating (P / %) || PPP || DR Threshold || T/L Rating|r, each whole on one line (no \"...\", no wrap inside \"Rating (P / %)\"), each centred over its column; every number starts at its column's left edge; the T/L cell is two lines, \"T: 1,430\" then \"L: 12.2\" under it. Drag the panel to 760: Influences gets its own column, heads still whole." },
    { key = "E1z71", text = "[E1z71] (QoL 0.7.28; #60 / #62 \"New value with sign\") Stats tab: type 2800 in Agility's Change box (or 200 more than yours) and press Enter. |cffffd100Expect:|r no \"now -> then\" anywhere; Agility's Current value is your number (2,616) with |cffffd100+2,800|r under it in the theme's accent colour; hover Attack power in Agility's Influences: its value, then the new one with + under it. Type a number lower than yours: the line under reads with a |cffffd100-|r. Clear the box: the lines under go away." },
    { key = "E1z72", text = "[E1z72] (QoL 0.7.28; #60 / #62 \"Both lists\") With the number from E1z71 still typed. |cffffd100Expect:|r no \"» Abilities (per 100)\" and no \"» Ability Scaling\" on the Stats tab, nor in Agility's hover, nor in the character window's Agility tooltip." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-look-5", { title = "2. Looks and layout (no effect on use) (5 of 6)", order = 200.05, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "E1z73", text = "[E1z73] (QoL 0.7.28; #60 / #61 / #62 \"Spells tab -> Ability Scaling\", \"Only stats that change the number\") The tabs read |cffffd100Stats || Gear || Ability Scaling|r (the tab you had open last time opens again). Open Ability Scaling (Configure spell data if asked). |cffffd100Expect:|r no \"Refresh spell data\" line under the Spell Name head in Active spells, Active offensive spells or Active defensive spells (the centred button above stays); the fourth head reads |cffffd100Computed Value|r in full; under each damage or healing spell's percents a line \"Versatility: +N%\", and \"Mastery: +N%\" only on spells your mastery's text names (or their school); no crit or haste line. With a number typed on the Stats tab (Agility, Versatility or Mastery), the first Computed Value shows the new value with its sign under it in the accent colour. Tell us whether the numbers match what the spell does in game (an estimate: it assumes the description already counts versatility and mastery)." },
    { key = "E1z74", text = "[E1z74] (QoL 0.7.28; #63 / #65 \"bucket bar ... indentations follow sub- and sub-sub- nesting rules\") Stats tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r Primary, General, Offensive and Defensive each a thin band in the theme's accent colour across the pane with the name on it; every stat (Agility, Health, Attack Power, Critical Strike ...) one step in from the band; every line under a stat one more step in; nothing out of line. Say if you want another colour or step." },
    { key = "E1z75", text = "[E1z75] (QoL 0.7.28; #64 / #65 \"provide all three visual options ... volunteer more\") Stats tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r |cffffd100Gear Summary|r is the first section, above Character Stats, drawn as |cffffd100Split bars|r (one bar per stat in its colour, as long as your rating; the solid part from gear, the lighter part from elsewhere; \"544 (gear 489 +55)\" at its end). Panel > Layout > |cffffd100Gear Summary style|r: try |cffffd100Stat tiles|r, |cffffd100One stacked bar|r, |cffffd100Columns|r, |cffffd100Gear share|r and |cffffd100Table|r; each draws inside the pane, numbers whole. Please tell us which one to keep as the default." },
    { key = "E1z76", text = "[E1z76] (Replaced in QoL 0.7.40 by E1z195: skip. The column is Modifies; \"from Agility\" is a row under the stat.) (QoL 0.7.28; #66 / #67 \"Names only, values on hover\", \"Same Influences column\") Stats tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r the heads read |cffffd100Stat || Current value || Pt value || Influences || Change|r (Rating too over Secondaries / Tertiaries), none cut; Agility's row lists |cffffd100Attack power, Dodge, Armor|r in Influences, Stamina's |cffffd100Health|r, Attack Power's |cffffd100from Agility|r (and |cffffd100from Mastery|r where your mastery gives attack power); no \"»\" or \"From Agility\" rows under the stats any more. Hover a name: its value, its Pt value, and with a typed number the new value. At the default width the Influences column is narrow (names may wrap); say whether the default width should grow." },
    { key = "E1z77", text = "[E1z77] (QoL 0.7.28; #68 \"gear pane request for gear highlight dropped\") Gear tab: click your main hand. |cffffd100Expect:|r its box gets a clear frame in the theme's accent colour, thicker than the quality border, over the icon's edges; pick one, then two items in the Compare list: each picked one has the same frame; click one again: its frame goes." },
    { key = "E1z78", text = "[E1z78] (QoL 0.7.28; REQUEST-LOG #69 / #71, her answer \"Over the model\") Character Reskin on, |cffffd100Extra width|r 42 (the default: 380 / 582 wide). Open the character window. |cffffd100Expect:|r every slot that has an enchant, embellishment or gem shows its block again (head, neck, shoulders, chest, wrists, waist, legs, feet, both rings, both weapons); the ones beside the model run over its sides, as at Blizzard's width; the gem icons are 16 px (12 where a block is tight); hover a row for its whole text. Set |cffffd100Extra width|r to 240: the blocks sit beside the model, off it. (This replaces E1z60's \"no block is drawn beside the head ...\".)" },
    { key = "E1z83", text = "[E1z83] (QoL 0.7.33; Insivius via Xaya: \"Text breaks if you make the window wider and then bring it back down\"; her answer \"Fix + diagnostic\") QoL > Character Reskin on, Enchants and Gems beside the slots on, Wider window on. Open the character window with the stats pane open. Set Extra width to 240, then back to 42 (the window stays open). Then close and open the stats pane (the arrow at the window's bottom right). |cffffd100Expect:|r after each change the enchant, embellishment and gem lines are the same as when the window was first opened at that width: nothing wraps short, nothing runs over the slots or past its band. Then type |cff88ccff/xui reskin status|r and send the |cffffd100Size change|r line (it says whether the game gave different positions right after the change than a frame later: that settles the cause). If the text still breaks, a screenshot and that line please." },
    { key = "E1z92", text = "[E1z92] (QoL 0.7.36; REQUEST-LOG UI-39, Xaya 2026-11-06: \"put talent modifiers before % PSV for clarity / spell names should be collapsible and there should be divider lines between each ability to segmenrt more clearly / put the numbers to left-align to be closer to their %PSV calculations\") Stat Calc > Ability Scaling, Active spells. |cffffd100Expect:|r the columns read Spell Name || Talent Modifiers || % PSV || Computed Value; the Computed Value numbers start at the left of their column, next to the percents; a thin line between two spells. Each spell name starts with \"- \"; click a spell's row: it folds to \"+ <name>\" alone; click it again: it opens. Close and reopen the panel: a folded spell stays folded. Screenshot please." },
    { key = "E1z196", text = "[E1z196] (QoL 0.7.40; REQUEST-LOG #89, her words \"compare item selection should also have a clear highlight for selections\"; walkthrough \"Stat Calculator: the picked compare item is highlighted\") Gear tab: click your second trinket (Trinket slot #2), then a trinket in the icon row under |cffffd100Compare: Trinket slot #2|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the picked trinket gets the same frame as the equipped one: 3 px, the theme's accent colour, all round, over the icon. Pick a second ring from a ring slot's list: both picked rings framed. Click a picked one again: its frame goes. (Cause found: the bags' links use a named quality colour, \"||cnIQ4:\", which the item reader cut off, so the picked item never matched its icon.)" },
    { key = "E1z197", text = "[E1z197] (QoL 0.7.40; REQUEST-LOG #90, her words \"+/- signs should be in () to the right of the compared values -- set the number values to left-align to make space\"; walkthrough \"Stat Calculator: Changes shows (+/-) beside each number\") Gear tab: compare an item with different secondary stats. |cffffd100Expect:|r in |cffffd100Changes|r every number starts at its column's left edge and, for each picked item, its difference follows on the same line in brackets, e.g. |cffffd1001,405 (-12)|r, green when better, orange when worse; no difference on a line under the number. DR threshold's \"crosses N\" and True / lost's \"L N\" stay under their numbers. With three items picked at the default width, two columns may show side by side with \"1 more picked: drag the panel's corner wider ...\" (the bracketed numbers need the room); drag the panel wider: all three." },
    { key = "E1z198", text = "[E1z198] (QoL 0.7.40; REQUEST-LOG #91, her words \"name, class, and spec not needed on stat calculator. Instead, set this section to display currently equipped ilvl and on the right side max ilvl (in bags)\"; reading taken: max = the game's overall item level; walkthrough \"Stat Calculator: header shows equipped and max item level\") Open the Stat Calculator. |cffffd100Expect:|r above the tabs one line: |cffffd100Equipped <equipped item level>|r on the left, |cffffd100Max (bags) <item level>|r on the right; no name, spec, class or class colour. Hover the character window's item level: the Max (bags) number is the game's overall (higher) one, Equipped the equipped one. Drag the panel to its narrowest: both still on one line, apart." },
    { key = "E1z199", text = "[E1z199] (QoL 0.7.40; REQUEST-LOG B2, reading taken: the \"% / rating\" toggle removed in all three places; walkthrough \"Stat Calculator: no % / rating toggle\") |cffffd100Expect:|r no \"Show: %\" / \"Show: rating\" button in the panel's title row; clicking Critical Strike opens or folds its lines and never switches a percent to a rating; QoL > Character Toolkit > Panel > Layout has no |cffffd100Rating lines|r, Your numbers has no |cffffd100Reset line flips|r (Clear all stays)." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-look-6", { title = "2. Looks and layout (no effect on use) (6 of 6)", order = 200.06, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "F5", text = "[F5] Switch |cffffd100XayaUI Bonus Features|r off, relog. |cffffd100Expect:|r no notepad, no panels, plain tooltips, no Bonus Features tab; |cff88ccff/xui notes|r says Bonus Features is switched off." },
    { key = "F7", text = "[F7] (Bonus 0.6.11, Options 0.6.40) Bonus Features tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r the left pane reads Data Panels (a tick box left of its name), Tooltips (no box), Utilities (no box) with Calculator (no box) and Notepad (a tick box) under it; no Notepad entry of its own at the top. Select Tooltips, then click Notepad's box. |cffffd100Expect:|r the Notepad box shows on screen, Tooltips stays open on the right, no noticeable pause. Click it again: the notepad hides. Show it with |cff88ccff/xui notes|r, close it with its x. |cffffd100Expect:|r Notepad's tick box follows each time (within a moment). Tick Data Panels' box. |cffffd100Expect:|r the panels you have switched on show; untick it: all panels hide. Hover that box. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Enable Data Panels\" and the master-switch explanation. Open both pages. |cffffd100Expect:|r no \"Enable Data Panels\" switch on the Data Panels page, no \"Show Notepad\" switch on the Notepad page; the Notepad page's other settings are as before." },
    { key = "F20", text = "[F20] (Bonus 0.6.18; UI-5 / UI-7: \"change the name Custom Data Panels and Bars -- split the two in the options settings to Data Panels / Data Bars\"; her answer: Data Bars (ElvUI-style progress bars) on the roadmap for later, under Blizzard UI Reskin) Bonus Features tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r the first row reads |cffffd100Data Panels|r (hover its tick box: \"Enable Data Panels\"); its page and every panel work as before. No Data Bars row yet (roadmap RM-DATABARS)." },
    { key = "G1", text = "[G1] Blizzard UI Reskin > Esc Menu (Options 0.6.38): switch the look on, press Esc. |cffffd100Expect:|r XayaUI's look on the Game Menu; every button does what its label says (Options, Shop, Log Out, Exit Game, Return to Game)." },
    { key = "G1b", text = "[G1b] (Options 0.6.38, Chat 0.6.13, Reskin 0.6.1, QoL 0.7.14; Xaya 2026-11-05: \"Take all reskins and put them into a new tab: Blizzard UI Reskin\") Open the settings window. |cffffd100Expect:|r a top tab |cffffd100Blizzard UI Reskin|r after Bonus Features, with Character Pane, Chat Panel and Esc Menu in its left pane; no Chat tab; QoL without Character Reskin. Settings > UI Options > Display: the Menu button (ESC menu) options are still there, with one line saying the Esc menu's look is under Blizzard UI Reskin > Esc Menu (no look options on Display). |cff88ccff/xui chat settings|r, right-clicking a Chat Bar block and |cff88ccff/xui reskin options|r open their pages in the new tab. Open the Settings pages: the tab hides like the other feature tabs." },
    { key = "G2", text = "[G2] Switch |cffffd100XayaUI Blizzard Reskin|r off, relog. |cffffd100Expect:|r Blizzard's Game Menu; the XayaUI button in it still opens the window; the Esc Menu page is gone from the Blizzard UI Reskin tab." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-combat-1", { title = "3. Combat displays (1 of 16)", order = 300.01, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "B10", text = "[B10] A buff rule with an icon display, |cffffd100Duration text|r on, not in a dynamic group (for example Anti-Magic Shell or Power Word: Shield). Cast the buff in combat. |cffffd100Expect:|r the time counts down in combat, in XayaUI's format (|cff88ccff12|r, then tenths such as |cff88ccff4.3|r below 5 s if tenths are on), in the font, size and colour set on the display (before 0.6.3 it was small white text with an |cff88ccffs|r). If it shows |cff88ccff12s|r style instead, |cff88ccff/xuiengine|r must say \"time text in the game's own format\" for that display: report that line." },
    { key = "B11", text = "[B11] The same rule with |cffffd100Stacks|r on, on a buff that cannot stack. |cffffd100Expect:|r no number (before: |cff88ccff0|r or |cff88ccff1|r). On a buff that stacks: the number from 2 stacks up, in combat too." },
    { key = "B12", text = "[B12] The same display with |cffffd100Shield / absorb amount|r on (source \"this aura\" or \"total\"). |cffffd100Expect:|r the amount shows over the engine's icon, in and out of combat. With |cffffd100Abbreviate|r off and |cffffd100Hide when zero|r on, nothing shows when you have no shield. (With both on, a |cff88ccff0|r can show: known game limit, listed by |cff88ccff/xui debug timing|r.)" },
    { key = "B13", text = "[B13] A rule with an icon cue and a separate |cffffd100Text|r cue showing the duration (the #347 shape, no conditions). |cffffd100Expect:|r both show in combat; the Text cue's time is exact (counts down smoothly, no jumps when you recast). |cff88ccff/xuiengine|r ends its summary with \"plus 1 separate time / stack display\"." },
    { key = "B14", text = "[B14] A \"Target Debuff (yours)\" rule (the debuff as its only trigger, not in a dynamic group). Apply the debuff to dummy A, then target dummy B (no debuff), then back to A. |cffffd100Expect:|r the icon disappears at once on B and comes back at once on A, with A's remaining time (before 0.6.3 it could keep showing A's debuff on B)." },
    { key = "B15", text = "[B15] A cooldown rule shown while the spell is |cffffd100not ready|r, with Duration text on. Use the spell in combat. |cffffd100Expect:|r the text counts the cooldown down to 0 (exact), and the global cooldown alone shows no countdown. A spell with charges: the time to the next charge." },
    { key = "B16", text = "[B16] A display with |cffffd100Only while on an action bar|r on: remove the spell from your bars. |cffffd100Expect:|r the display hides, also when the engine draws it." },
    { key = "B17", text = "[B17] |cff88ccff/xui debug timing|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r one line per rule that uses time or stacks, no Lua error." },
    { key = "B18", text = "[B18] Out of combat with a proc or buff on you: |cff88ccff/xui debug auras|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r one line per buff with its ID, stacks and time, and a second line with readable in combat / Cooldown Manager / Blizzard flags; no Lua error. Turn a listed buff on in Blizzard's Cooldown Manager (Tracked Buffs) and run it again: that buff now says \"on and shown\"." },
    { key = "B19", text = "[B19] In combat: |cff88ccff/xui debug auras|r says the game hides aura details right now; |cff88ccff/xui debug auras <an ID from B18>|r still prints that spell's three facts. Paste both outputs into the report (testers with Divine Arbiter or Boiling Blood / Boiling Point: please include those)." },
    { key = "B20", text = "[B20] A dynamic group of 3 or more buff rules (your Active Mitigation group works), Sort = |cffffd100Manual|r. Use the buffs in combat in a different order than the rules. |cffffd100Expect:|r the icons always show in the rule order, with no gaps; a buff that appears takes its place between the others. Then drag one rule to another place in the group (out of combat): the order follows." },
    { key = "B21", text = "[B21] Same group, Sort = |cffffd100Expiration|r, then |cffffd100Important|r, then |cffffd100Name|r, each with and without |cffffd100Reverse|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the order changes accordingly, no Lua error; |cff88ccff/xuiengine|r names the sort. Back to |cffffd100Manual|r: the rule order returns. |cffffd100Save order and reload|r reloads with the order kept." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-combat-2", { title = "3. Combat displays (2 of 16)", order = 300.02, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "B22", text = "[B22] (0.6.7) A dynamic group with Sort = |cffffd100Manual|r and Spacing 4, 3 or more buffs up in combat. |cffffd100Expect:|r the icons are 4 pixels apart, the same as unlocked (0.6.6 put them 8 apart in combat)." },
    { key = "B23", text = "[B23] (0.6.7) Same group, Grow direction |cffffd100Centered row|r. Use the buffs one by one in combat. |cffffd100Expect:|r the row stays centered on the group's position and widens both ways as each buff appears, and closes up when one ends. Unlock the group: the preview shows the same spots." },
    { key = "B24", text = "[B24] (0.6.7) Grow direction |cffffd100From anchor point, rows|r, then set This group's anchor point to TOPRIGHT, then BOTTOMLEFT, then BOTTOM. |cffffd100Expect:|r TOPRIGHT: icons start at the group's top right and grow left; BOTTOMLEFT: start bottom left, grow right, new rows above; BOTTOM: centered on the bottom middle. In combat the icons stay on those spots as buffs come and go. Also try |cffffd100From anchor point, columns|r." },
    { key = "B25", text = "[B25] (0.6.8) Unholy, Death and Decay in the Cooldown Manager's Tracked Buffs, Insivius's rule (Death and Decay ready AND its buff 188290 / 434034 missing, loaded in combat; Condition 1: buff AND charges == 2 shows a texture and plays a sound). In combat with both charges, not standing in it: |cffffd100Expect:|r the texture shows and the sound plays; step into it: they stop; with one charge: they stay off. |cff88ccff/xui debug status|r in combat shows the rule's buff answer coming from \"CDM tracked buff of the rule's spell 43265\"." },
    { key = "B26", text = "[B26] (0.6.9) Insivius's Death and Decay rule (2 charges from Death's Echo). In combat, use one charge and step out of it: |cffffd100Expect:|r the texture and sound do NOT fire until the second charge is back (0.6.8 fired right after the cast). Use both: nothing until both are back. |cff88ccff/xui debug status|r in combat shows the cooldown line \"charges (max 2): ...\" with how the count was found." },
    { key = "B27", text = "[B27] (0.6.9) A rule on a spell with 3 charges (|cff88ccffdocs/reference/charges.md|r), condition \"charges == 2\", the spell in Blizzard's Cooldown Manager: use one charge in combat. |cffffd100Expect:|r TRUE at 2, FALSE at 1 and 3. Without the spell in the Cooldown Manager: unknown below full (the rule does not fire), exact again at full or 0." },
    { key = "B28", text = "[B28] (0.6.11) A \"missing debuff\" rule: Target Debuff (yours), State \"Debuff is NOT on the unit\", the DEBUFF's ID (Sigil of Flame 204598), the ability (204596) in Blizzard's Cooldown Manager Tracked Buffs, Cooldown Manager spell ID left blank. In combat: |cffffd100Expect:|r TRUE when the debuff is not on your target, FALSE while it is (before 0.6.11 it stayed unknown unless the Cooldown Manager spell ID was typed in)." },
    { key = "B30", text = "[B30] (XayaUI 0.6.12) Recycle Bin, rules: delete a rule that has cues and a condition (right-click > Delete). |cffffd100Expect:|r the prompt ends \"It goes to the Recycle Bin for 7 days\"; the rule is gone from the sidebar and its icon / sound no longer fire; Rules > Recycle Bin lists it as \"Rule. Deleted <time>; removed for good in 6 days\". Restore. |cffffd100Expect:|r it is back in its group with its cues and condition, and works." },
    { key = "B31", text = "[B31] (XayaUI 0.6.12) Recycle Bin, groups: (a) delete a group on its own: its rules move up one level; Restore: the group is back and the rules are inside it again. (b) delete a group WITH contents (nested group, a few rules): one bin item (\"Group with its contents: N rule(s), 2 group(s)\"); Restore: everything back where it was. (c) multi-select 3 rules and press Delete: three items. |cffffd100Expect:|r as described, no Lua error." },
    { key = "B32", text = "[B32] (XayaUI 0.6.12) Recycle Bin settings: set \"Keep deleted items for\" to 36 hours, |cff88ccff/reload|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the setting stays. Empty Recycle Bin. |cffffd100Expect:|r a confirmation first, then the page says the bin is empty and the chat says how many items were removed." },
    { key = "B33", text = "[B33] (XayaUI 0.6.13, decision D2) Game-played aura sound: on a rule with a Buff / Aura trigger (for example a proc buff such as Boiling Point 1265968, or any buff of yours) and a Sound cue with a sound FILE (not a [Game] kit), open the Sound cue, tick \"Let the game play this sound on the aura itself\", leave Ambience. |cffffd100Expect:|r the pane's last line turns green: \"The game plays this sound when the aura is gained (aura ..., channel Ambience)\". Fight a training dummy until the buff procs. |cffffd100Expect:|r the sound plays in combat, once per proc (not twice). Set the game's Ambience volume to 0. |cffffd100Expect:|r the sound stops; other sounds still play. |cff88ccff/reload|r, proc it again. |cffffd100Expect:|r still once, not twice. Report \"plays / does not play / plays twice\" with the aura ID: this is the first in-game check of AddAuraSound for an ordinary aura." },
    { key = "B34", text = "[B34] (XayaUI 0.6.13) Spell Glows trigger: add a trigger \"Spell Glows (proc highlight)\" with a spell that a proc lights (Frost Death Knight: Howling Blast 49184 with Rime; Frost Mage: Flurry 44614 with Brain Freeze) and a Sound cue. |cffffd100Expect:|r the row's \"Right now\" line reads true only while the button glows, out of combat and on a training dummy (in combat); the sound plays when the glow starts." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-combat-3", { title = "3. Combat displays (3 of 16)", order = 300.03, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "B35", text = "[B35] (XayaUI 0.6.13) Proc glow standing in for a hidden buff: a rule with Buff / Aura = Rime 59052 (or Brain Freeze 190446), present, and a Sound cue; do NOT track the buff in the Cooldown Manager. Out of combat, get the proc twice (or with the Dev Assist probe running, see section J). Then fight a dummy. |cffffd100Expect:|r after the two sightings |cff88ccff/xui debug status|r shows the rule's buff answer \"proc glow on Howling Blast (49184; pairing seen in game)\" while the button glows in combat, and the rule fires. Before the two sightings it reads unknown in combat. If it ever reads present while the buff is NOT on you, report it with the aura ID." },
    { key = "B36", text = "[B36] (XayaUI 0.6.13) Tier Set Pieces Worn: add the trigger, leave Set ID 0, \"Pieces worn >= 4\". |cffffd100Expect:|r the pane lists the sets you wear with their IDs and piece counts; Right now is true with 4 or more pieces on. Take one tier piece off. |cffffd100Expect:|r false at once." },
    { key = "B37", text = "[B37] (XayaUI 0.6.13) Per-rule combat line: open a rule with a Buff / Aura trigger whose buff is not in the Cooldown Manager. |cffffd100Expect:|r at the top of the Triggers tab, \"In combat: 1 of N triggers may read UNKNOWN (Buff / Aura)\". Add the buff to Tracked Buffs, reopen the rule. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"every trigger XayaUI can judge is readable\"." },
    { key = "B38", text = "[B38] (XayaUI 0.6.13) Engine performance guard: type |cff88ccff/xuiengine|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the last line names \"Blizzard's aura containers ... ms\" and \"all of XayaUI ... ms\" (or \"no reading yet\"). If you ever saw \"performance guard\" turn the engine off before, |cff88ccff/reload|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the engine draws again, and |cff88ccff/xuiengine|r notes the old trip was undone." },
    { key = "B39", text = "[B39] (XayaUI 0.6.13) A spell you do not have: make a rule with the built-in Cooldown trigger on a talent you have NOT picked, state \"Fully ready\", and a Sound cue. |cffffd100Expect:|r it never fires; |cff88ccff/xui debug status|r says \"spell not known (talent or specialization)\". Pick the talent. |cffffd100Expect:|r it fires when the spell is ready." },
    { key = "B40", text = "[B40] (XayaUI 0.6.13, decision D1) A buff that is not up: a rule \"Buff / Aura present\" on a buff you do not have, plus a condition \"Buff / Aura: seconds left <= 2\" listing a Sound cue. |cffffd100Expect:|r no sound while the buff is missing (before 0.6.13 it played: the missing buff counted as 0 seconds left)." },
    { key = "B41", text = "[B41] (XayaUI 0.6.14) Cues fire from the triggers unless a condition decides them: a rule with a Buff / Aura trigger and two Sound cues, no conditions. Get the buff. |cffffd100Expect:|r both sounds once. Add Condition 1 (IF stacks >= 3, or any check that is false now) whose THEN lists only cue 1. |cffffd100Expect:|r the Cues tab says cue 1 \"Fires while Condition 1 is true\" and cue 2 \"Fires with the rule's triggers\"; get the buff again: only cue 2 plays. Switch Condition 1 off. |cffffd100Expect:|r cue 1 reads \"Silent\" and stays silent. Switch the whole rule off. |cffffd100Expect:|r neither cue plays (before 0.6.14 they still did)." },
    { key = "B42", text = "[B42] (XayaUI 0.6.15, #333; tester without Xaya's art folders, e.g. Insivius) Open a Texture cue > \"Or pick art\". |cffffd100Expect:|r no blank rows: the [Graphics] and [Bar Fills] entries are gone, the game's own art is listed, and your own XayaUI_Media pictures are listed. Xaya: the same list shows all of them. If blank rows remain, report it: the game then does not report missing files through SetTexture, and the fix needs another route." },
    { key = "B43", text = "[B43] (Options 0.6.12, #352) Open any settings page where a dropdown sits alone on its row (for example a cue's \"Channel for the game's copy\", or Load > a single dropdown). |cffffd100Expect:|r the dropdown is one column wide (about half the pane), never stretched across the whole row; a dropdown with long options is as wide as its longest option." },
    { key = "B44", text = "[B44] (XayaUI 0.6.16 / Options 0.6.12, #286) With the addon's own look on: the Debug console tray's Clear / Copy, the \"Play all N sounds at once?\" Yes / No, the console window's buttons (|cff88ccff/xui console|r, \"Select all\" in a copy box) and a group's X / Y position popup buttons. |cffffd100Expect:|r every one is flat (dark box, gold text), none in Blizzard's red. |cff88ccff/xuiskin|r (look off) and reopen: Blizzard's buttons return." },
    { key = "B45", text = "[B45] (XayaUI 0.6.16, #99) Add a Target Debuff (yours) trigger. |cffffd100Expect:|r the labels read \"Cooldown Manager ID\" and \"Unlit icon in combat\" in full (not \"Cooldown M...\"); hovering each shows the full explanation." },
    { key = "B46", text = "[B46] (XayaUI 0.6.17 / Options 0.6.13, #336) Quit the game fully and start it again (a new file, |cff88ccffMedia\\UI\\xui_blank.tga|r, is found only at game start), then open a Texture cue > \"Or pick art\". |cffffd100Expect:|r every row's name starts at the same place, with the picture centred in a column two icons wide (narrow and wide pictures alike); the closed box shows only a small picture, no empty gap before it." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-combat-4", { title = "3. Combat displays (4 of 16)", order = 300.04, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "B47", text = "[B47] (XayaUI 0.6.18 / Options 0.6.14, #319) On a Paladin (any class but Death Knight): a rule with Load = |cffffd100Always load|r, Class row ticked with Death Knight chosen. |cffffd100Expect:|r a tick box \"Always load: only this class\" on the Class row; unticked, the rule loads (as before). Tick it. |cffffd100Expect:|r the rule no longer loads on the Paladin (|cff88ccff/xui debug status|r says \"Always load, only this class\"); it loads on a Death Knight. Switch the mode to Match ALL. |cffffd100Expect:|r the tick box disappears (the Class row counts anyway). Group version: a group set to Always with Class = Death Knight on its Load tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Always load: only this class\" under the Class list; ticked, the group's rules stay off on the Paladin." },
    { key = "B48", text = "[B48] (XayaUI 0.6.19, #260) A rule with a Buff / Aura trigger, one Icon cue drawn by the engine (|cff88ccff/xuiengine|r lists it), and Condition 1 whose THEN lists that cue with \"Desaturate: on\" and Opacity 50%, IF something you can switch (for example a cooldown ready). Out of combat and on a training dummy: |cffffd100Expect:|r the icon shows only while the condition is true, grey and half transparent then; when the condition turns false the icon hides; with the condition switched to something the game hides in combat (stacks), the icon stays hidden in combat. Take the cue out of the condition's THEN: |cffffd100Expect:|r it shows whenever the aura is up, in its own colours." },
    { key = "B49", text = "[B49] (XayaUI 0.6.19, #334) A Sound cue with a [Game] sound: set \"This cue's volume\" to 30% and test. |cffffd100Expect:|r this cue alone is quieter; other game sounds and the channel volume are unchanged. Pick a sound file instead. |cffffd100Expect:|r the slider is greyed out and its tooltip says why." },
    { key = "B50", text = "[B50] (XayaUI 0.6.20) Settings > Debugging: tick Advanced Debugging. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"XayaUI's messages\" reads \"XayaUI console window\"; type |cff88ccff/xui debug status|r: its lines appear in the console window (it opens), not in chat. Fight a training dummy for a few seconds, leave combat, then Create bug report. |cffffd100Expect:|r a \"Debug record\" section with \"combat start\", rule lines, \"combat end\", \"engine\" lines and \"aura\" lines naming which source answered. |cff88ccff/reload|r, then open |cff88ccffWTF\\Account\\<account>\\SavedVariables\\XayaUI.lua|r: |cffffd100Expect:|r a |cff88ccffdebugRecord|r table with the same lines. Untick Advanced Debugging: |cffffd100Expect:|r messages go back to chat and nothing more is added." },
    { key = "B51", text = "[B51] (XayaUI 0.6.20, Dev Assist installed) With Advanced Debugging on: |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Also run the game-data probe\" is shown and ticked, and |cff88ccff/xuidev probe status|r says ON without typing |cff88ccff/xuidev probe on|r. Untick Advanced Debugging: |cffffd100Expect:|r the probe goes off." },
    { key = "B52", text = "[B52] (XayaUI 0.6.20) A Buff / Aura trigger on Rime (59052) as a Frost Death Knight, the buff NOT in the Cooldown Manager. |cffffd100Expect:|r its In combat line says the Howling Blast glow \"will stand in once XayaUI has seen them agree 2 times (0 so far)\"; after two Rime procs out of combat (or with the buff readable) it says \"present from its proc glow\". A set-bonus aura (any aura listed in |cff88ccffXayaUI/SetBonusAuras.lua|r for your class): |cffffd100Expect:|r the line says it comes from a set bonus, and with too few pieces worn the trigger reads missing in combat." },
    { key = "B53", text = "[B53] (XayaUI 0.6.20, Chat 0.6.7) With Advanced Debugging on and messages going to the console window: Ctrl + right-click a player's name in chat to ignore them. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Ignoring <name> ...\" appears in the console window. Then Create bug report and the console window's Copy. |cffffd100Expect:|r that name appears in neither. Remove them from the Ignore list afterwards. Untick \"Open the console window when a message arrives\", close the window, type |cff88ccff/xui debug status|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the window stays closed; reopen Settings: the box is still unticked." },
    { key = "B54", text = "[B54] (XayaUI 0.6.22) Settings > Debugging with Advanced Debugging on: |cffffd100Expect:|r a \"What to record\" box with 11 switches, each with its cost in grey; Rules, Snapshots, Aura answers, Proc glows, Sounds, Game state, Engine status and Messages ticked; Trigger detail, Displays and Performance unticked. Untick \"XayaUI's messages\", type |cff88ccff/xui debug status|r, then |cffffd100View the debug record|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r no |cff88ccffMessage|r lines after that point; the lines read |cff88ccfftime  Category  what happened|r; the top says what each category means and which are off. Click |cffffd100Light set|r, then |cffffd100Defaults|r: |cffffd100Expect:|r the ticks change accordingly." },
    { key = "B55", text = "[B55] (XayaUI 0.6.22) Tick \"Trigger detail for chosen rules\", pick one rule in \"Rules for trigger detail\", trigger it on and off a few times, then View the debug record. |cffffd100Expect:|r |cff88ccffTrigger|r lines for that rule only, one per change (not one per second), each saying where the aura answer came from or why it does not fire. Tick \"Displays shown and hidden\": |cffffd100Expect:|r one |cff88ccffDisplay|r line when its display appears and one when it goes." },
    { key = "B56", text = "[B56] (XayaUI 0.6.22) Tick \"Performance\", fight a training dummy for 20 seconds, leave combat, View the debug record. |cffffd100Expect:|r |cff88ccffPerf|r lines (cost per second, slowest rules, the game's addon meter) after the combat-end mark, and no perf messages in chat or the console window. Then type |cff88ccff/xui debug perf|r: |cffffd100Expect:|r \"not measuring\" (the record's timer stopped with the combat). Enter a dungeon: |cffffd100Expect:|r a |cff88ccffGame|r line with the instance name, type, difficulty, instance ID and map ID; on a boss pull and kill or wipe, |cff88ccffGame|r lines with the encounter ID and the result." },
    { key = "B57", text = "[B57] (XayaUI 0.6.22) \"What to send\" (shown even with Advanced Debugging off): click the XayaUI.lua box, Ctrl+A, Ctrl+C, paste into File Explorer's address bar after replacing |cff88ccff<YOUR ACCOUNT FOLDER>|r with your account folder (and removing |cff88ccffXayaUI.lua|r at the end). |cffffd100Expect:|r the folder opens and holds XayaUI.lua. Note the account folder's name format (a number such as |cff88ccff12345678#1|r, or something else) in the QA notes: the text says \"often a number\" and that is not confirmed. With Dev Assist installed: |cffffd100Expect:|r a second box for XayaUI_DevAssist.lua. The console window has a |cffffd100What to send|r button with the same text; a bug report ends with it." },
    { key = "B58", text = "[B58] (XayaUI 0.6.24) Needs an addon that brings LibCustomGlow (ElvUI, BigWigs, ...). A rule's Actions tab, During: tick Glow a frame, Glow = this rule's display. For each Glow type (button, pixel, autocast, proc): trigger the rule. |cffffd100Expect:|r the glow of that type on the display. Then pick a red color with the picker's opacity at about 40%. |cffffd100Expect:|r a red, see-through glow (all four types). Pixel: Lines 12, Speed -0.5, Thickness 3, Offset X 5. |cffffd100Expect:|r 12 thicker lines running the other way, shifted right. Autocast: Sparkle groups 6, Sparkle size 150%. |cffffd100Expect:|r more, bigger sparkles. Proc: untick Start flash. |cffffd100Expect:|r the loop starts without the opening flash. Button: no Offset or position settings are shown. If a setting has no effect, note the library version: |cff88ccff/dump select(2, LibStub(\"LibCustomGlow-1.0\"))|r (25 was the version checked)." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-combat-5", { title = "3. Combat displays (5 of 16)", order = 300.05, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "B59", text = "[B59] (Options 0.6.19) Rules > Enabled, pick a group that has displays (e.g. Active Mitigation). |cffffd100Expect:|r the top row reads |cffffd100Group|r, |cffffd100Display|r, |cffffd100Load|r in full, drawn as tabs (the picked one in the selected-tab colors, 2 px apart), not as separate buttons; clicking Load switches to the Load page and Load becomes the picked tab. The buttons below read in full: |cffffd100Delete group|r, |cffffd100Delete with contents|r, |cffffd100+ New rule|r, |cffffd100+ Nested group|r, |cffffd100Enable all|r, |cffffd100Disable all|r (no \"...\"); a button that does not fit moves to the next line instead of running past the pane's right edge. Close and reopen the settings window twice. |cffffd100Expect:|r the buttons keep their full width (they no longer shrink each time)." },
    { key = "B60", text = "[B60] (Options 0.6.20) Rules > Enabled: drag the sidebar's right edge as far left as it goes, then open nested groups 3-4 levels deep (e.g. the Vengeance group > Active Mitigation). |cffffd100Expect:|r after the list redraws, the sidebar widens by itself so the deepest visible names show at least about 10 letters (not \"VD...\", \"A...\"); it never widens past the window's limit; hovering a row shows its full name. Collapse the deep groups. |cffffd100Expect:|r the sidebar stays as wide as it got (it does not shrink by itself)." },
    { key = "B61", text = "[B61] (XayaUI 0.6.25) A rule on a spell with no cooldown of its own that is on the global cooldown (e.g. a builder), Cooldown section State \"Cooldown ready\", a Sound or Icon cue. Out of combat and in combat on a dummy, cast another GCD spell. |cffffd100Expect:|r with Count the global cooldown unticked, the cue stays on through the GCD (as before); ticked, it goes off for the length of the GCD after every cast and comes back when the GCD ends. Same with an added \"Cooldown (any spell)\" trigger row and its own tick box." },
    { key = "B62", text = "[B62] (XayaUI 0.6.26) A rule with a Cooldown on a spell with a long cooldown (30 s or more), State \"On cooldown\", Seconds left \"At most\" 5, a Sound cue. Cast the spell out of combat. |cffffd100Expect:|r the sound plays only in the last 5 seconds of the cooldown, not right after the cast. Repeat on a dummy in combat. |cffffd100Expect:|r the same, give or take the estimate (|cff88ccff/xui debug timing|r shows it); before the first estimate exists, nothing fires (unknown). On a 2+ charge spell: State \"Has a charge\", Charges \"At least\" 2. |cffffd100Expect:|r on only while 2 or more charges are up. On a rule without a Cooldown trigger: the Count the global cooldown / Seconds left / Charges options do not show; Remove on the Cooldown section clears them." },
    { key = "B63", text = "[B63] (XayaUI 0.6.27) A rule on a spell of one school (e.g. a Fire spell), State \"Cooldown ready\", Count a lockout as cooldown ticked, an Icon cue. Get interrupted while casting a spell of that school (a dungeon caster or a PvP partner with an interrupt). |cffffd100Expect:|r the icon goes off for the lockout and comes back when it ends; with the box unticked it stays on. Note whether the lockout is seen in combat." },
    { key = "B64", text = "[B64] (Options 0.6.24) A rule with a Sound cue whose \"Let the game play this sound on the aura itself\" is ticked (on the Sound cue's own pane). Add another cue to the rule (Cues tab, + Icon or + Sound), then open the Sound cue again. |cffffd100Expect:|r the new cue is added and both panes open, no Lua error. If an old core folder is installed by mistake, the Sound cue's pane shows a red line asking to copy every XayaUI folder again and restart the game, instead of an error." },
    { key = "B65", text = "[B65] (XayaUI 0.6.28 / Options 0.6.25) A rule with an Icon cue. Load tab > Zones, Instances, Bosses and Items: open it, press Add current on Zones. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Here:\" names the zone you stand in with its ID, and the ID appears in the box; the icon shows here. Fly to another zone. |cffffd100Expect:|r the icon goes away (and comes back in the first zone). Put a minus before the ID: the opposite. Then: enter a dungeon and add its instance ID and its difficulty (Add a difficulty menu); add a trinket you wear under Items equipped and unequip it (|cffffd100Expect:|r the icon goes away); in a raid or dungeon, add the boss under Boss encounters during a pull (|cffffd100Expect:|r the icon shows only while that boss is engaged). Type |cff88ccff/xui debug status|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r a \"place:\" line with map, instanceID, difficulty, size and encounterID. Note any value that reads nil where you expected a number." },
    { key = "B66", text = "[B66] (XayaUI 0.6.29 / Options 0.6.26) Two rules with icons in a group (e.g. Active Mitigation), one nested group with an icon. Press Unlock Positions (or |cff88ccff/xui unlock|r). |cffffd100Expect:|r a thin orange outline around each group and a small tab with the group's name above it; the nested group's tab sits above its parent's. Hover a tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r a tooltip with the group's path and what click / right-click / drag do, and its outline turns bright. Click the tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r the settings window opens on that group's page. Drag the tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r the whole group moves and stays there; the window does not open. Right-click the tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r the X / Y popup. Hover an icon. |cffffd100Expect:|r a tooltip with the rule's name and group; click it opens that rule; its right-click menu ends with Edit Its Group. Drag a single icon. |cffffd100Expect:|r it still moves on its own (the outline does not get in the way). Lock again. |cffffd100Expect:|r tabs and outlines are gone." },
    { key = "B67", text = "[B67] (Options 0.6.27) Rules > Enabled: open a rule that has an Icon cue, a Sound cue and a condition, on its Cues tab. Delete the condition (red X). |cffffd100Expect:|r the same rule stays open, on the same tab. Delete the Sound cue. |cffffd100Expect:|r the same. Delete a trigger (red X on the trigger's header). |cffffd100Expect:|r the same; if the window leaves the rule, note exactly what you did just before (which list, which tab, which trigger kind). Repeat from Smart Categories > Icons. |cffffd100Expect:|r the same." },
    { key = "B68", text = "[B68] (Options 0.6.28) A rule with an Icon cue on a buff with stacks (or a shield). Open the cue on the Cues tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r inside Icon Options, after Size & Orientation and Border & Background, a box \"Text: duration, stacks / charges, absorb\" with Buff Duration Text, Stacks / Charges Count and Shield / Absorb Amount. Tick Show remaining buff time and the count. |cffffd100Expect:|r the icon shows the time and the stacks. Same on a Texture cue. A Text cue's options look as before." },
    { key = "B69", text = "[B69] (XayaUI 0.6.31) Unlock Positions. Right-click a group's tab (e.g. Active Mitigation, next to your player frame), press Anchor to a frame on screen..., point at your player frame (a green outline with its name, e.g. PlayerFrame) and press Shift. |cffffd100Expect:|r the group does not move; the popup says Anchored to PlayerFrame. Move your player frame (Edit Mode). |cffffd100Expect:|r the group follows it. Snap flush to that frame. |cffffd100Expect:|r the group touches the frame's edge. Anchor to the screen. |cffffd100Expect:|r it stays where it is. /reload. |cffffd100Expect:|r the anchor is kept. Right-click a single icon > Snap Target > Pick a frame on screen..., pick an action bar. |cffffd100Expect:|r the icon sits against that bar on its nearest side. Point at nothing / press Cancel. |cffffd100Expect:|r nothing changes." },
    { key = "B70", text = "[B70] (Options 0.6.29) Open a rule. |cffffd100Expect:|r a box \"Search this rule's options\" above its tabs. Type |cff88ccffglobal cooldown|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r a result Trigger > ... > Count the global cooldown; click it. |cffffd100Expect:|r the Trigger tab opens. Type |cff88ccffcoldown|r (a typo). |cffffd100Expect:|r still found. Type |cff88ccff/zone||difficult/|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the Load tab's Zones and Difficulties lists. Type |cff88ccff/[abc/|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r a red line saying the pattern is not valid. Clear search. |cffffd100Expect:|r the results go away. Cues and conditions have no box of their own." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-combat-6", { title = "3. Combat displays (6 of 16)", order = 300.06, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "B71", text = "[B71] (Options 0.6.30) Open the settings window. |cffffd100Expect:|r at the bottom left \"XayaUI v0.6.31\" (or the current version), then \"Addon Info\"; no empty boxed bar between them and Close. Click Settings. |cffffd100Expect:|r an Acknowledgements entry in the left sidebar with the credits; Addon Info shows the version, author, license and source, and a line pointing to Settings > Acknowledgements. Collapse the window (the arrow) and expand it. |cffffd100Expect:|r the version label hides with the window and comes back. Open another addon's AceGUI window (e.g. another addon's options, if you have one). |cffffd100Expect:|r its own status bar is still there." },
    { key = "B72", text = "[B72] (Options 0.6.31) Rules > Enabled, open a group page and click Group, Display, Load several times, then a rule's tabs. |cffffd100Expect:|r the sidebar and the right pane keep their widths. Drag the sidebar narrower, then click tabs and edit a rule. |cffffd100Expect:|r it stays at the width you dragged (long names end in \"...\"; hovering a row shows the whole name). A fresh window (after /reload) with deep nesting: |cffffd100Expect:|r the sidebar is widened once so names fit, then stays." },
    { key = "B73", text = "[B73] (XayaUI 0.6.32) With the XayaUI Game Menu button on and another addon that adds its own menu button (e.g. EllesmereUI), press Esc. |cffffd100Expect:|r the menu's box reaches below Return to Game with the same margin as above Options; nothing touches or crosses its bottom edge. Turn the XayaUI button off (Settings > UI Options > Display > Menu button) and open the menu again. |cffffd100Expect:|r the same margin. If it still clips, type |cff88ccff/xui debug gamemenu|r and send the \"height fit\" line." },
    { key = "B74", text = "[B74] (XayaUI 0.6.33 / Options 0.6.32) A group with two rules that show icons. Its Load tab > Only Load This Group When > Zones, Instances, Bosses and Items: Add current on Zones. |cffffd100Expect:|r both rules' icons show here; fly to another zone: they go away. Set the group to Always: they show everywhere again. A rule in a nested group follows its parent's list too. |cff88ccff/xui debug status|r on a rule that does not load names the group and the list (e.g. \"group Raid auras: zone\")." },
    { key = "B75", text = "[B75] (Options 0.6.33, #351 phase 1) Open a few settings pages with rows of small controls side by side (a rule's Display tab, colour pickers, icon + label rows, the Load tab's tick rows). |cffffd100Expect:|r a small even gap (10 px) between any two controls on a row; nothing touches its neighbour or the box edge. Rows that used to fit exactly may now wrap a control to the next line: note any that look wrong." },
    { key = "B76", text = "[B76] (core 0.6.36, Options 0.6.36, QoL 0.7.10; #351 phase 2) Open the console (|cff88ccff/xui console|r), a copy box (console > Copy), the Import window (settings > Import) and the Stat Calculator panel. |cffffd100Expect:|r in each, nothing touches the window's edge or another control: about 10 px inside every edge (the close X and the console's resize grip sit in the corner, as in Blizzard's windows); the console's buttons 10 px apart and from its close X; the copy box's text area ends above Select all with a gap; the Import window's status lines (paste something unreadable to get an error) end above Close / Import; the Stat Calculator's \"Show: %\" button 10 px left of its X and its tabs 10 px under it. The console cannot be made narrower than 420 px. No Lua error." },
    { key = "B77", text = "[B77] (Chat 0.6.11; #351 phase 2) Open the chat history window (the Chat Bar's history button or |cff88ccff/xui chat history|r). |cffffd100Expect:|r about 10 px between the tab buttons and the search box, the search box and the text, the text and the Refresh / Live row, that row and the grey note under it, and under the note to the window's edge; Refresh and Live 10 px apart; the note stops 10 px short of the resize grip. Drag the window to its smallest size: the same, nothing overlapping. No Lua error." },
    { key = "B78", text = "[B78] (Bonus 0.6.9; #351 phase 2) Notepad: the menu button > Share this note..., then Export / import, then the restore list; have someone share a note with you (or skip that one). |cffffd100Expect:|r in each window about 10 px inside every edge (the small x in the corner aside) and 10 px between the rows and buttons: Send and Cancel, the three buttons of a shared-note offer, the export window's text and its Select all button. The share window's status line no longer runs into Send / Cancel (it is taller now: 210 px). The restore list opens 10 px right of the notepad. No Lua error." },
    { key = "B79", text = "[B79] (core 0.6.37; #351 phase 2) Mover view (|cff88ccff/xui unlock|r): right-click a group's name tag. |cffffd100Expect:|r the X / Y popup's rows (X, Y, the four buttons, the anchor line, the three anchor buttons, Close) 10 px apart and Close 10 px above the bottom edge (the popup is a little taller); a long anchor line (\"Anchored to: ...\") wraps onto a second line without touching the button under it. Click \"Anchor to a frame on screen...\". |cffffd100Expect:|r the banner's text 10 px from its top-left corner. No Lua error." },
    { key = "B80", text = "[B80] (Bonus 0.6.10; #351 phase 2) Open the notepad (|cff88ccff/xui notes|r). |cffffd100Expect:|r the text starts about 10 px from the left and right edges and 10 px under the toolbar (toolbar on top) or 10 px from it (toolbar left / right / bottom: try each in its settings); with the format bar on, the text starts 10 px under it; in the name row the name box and the character count sit 10 px from its sides and 10 px apart. The title bar, name row and toolbar still touch each other as one header. Type a long note: nothing runs under the resize grip's corner more than before. No Lua error." },
    { key = "B81", text = "[B81] (core 0.6.38) A rule's Actions tab > During (or Start): Message on, type \"Speak it\" (text-to-speech), message \"Shield up\". Make the rule fire (Test, or in game). |cffffd100Expect:|r you hear \"Shield up\" in your text-to-speech voice (Options > Accessibility > Text to Speech) at full volume; before core 0.6.38 it was silent. No Lua error." },
    { key = "B82", text = "[B82] (core 0.6.39) Press Escape with the XayaUI button on (and the XayaUI skin on, as in your screenshot). |cffffd100Expect:|r the menu's dark panel ends a short, even distance under Return to Game, not far below it. Close and reopen it five times: it stays the same height every time. With another addon's button in the menu (EllesmereUI): still fits. |cff88ccff/xui debug gamemenu|r (or the diagnostics) shows \"natural bottom padding N\" with N a small number (under 60). No Lua error." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-combat-7", { title = "3. Combat displays (7 of 16)", order = 300.07, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "B83", text = "[B83] (core 0.6.41; #309) Load conditions still answer as before: a rule with a zone list loads only in that zone, one with an equipped-item list only with the item on, a group's lists apply to its rules (QA B74 again). |cff88ccff/xui debug status|r shows the same \"place:\" line. Report the addon memory in the Addon List tooltip after 10 minutes of play, as before (61.8 MB on 2026-11-04) and after this version." },
    { key = "B84", text = "[B84] (core 0.6.42) Mover view (|cff88ccff/xui unlock|r): drag a display fast and let go near the screen edge (or onto a snap point, so it jumps away from the cursor), then right-click it at once. |cffffd100Expect:|r its menu opens on the first right-click, every time (repeat 5 times). A left click without dragging still opens it in the editor; letting go of a drag never opens the editor. No Lua error." },
    { key = "B85", text = "[B85] (core 0.6.43) Mover view: click a display ten times, letting the mouse wobble a little as you click. |cffffd100Expect:|r it opens in the editor each time and does not move; |cff88ccff/reload|r and check its X / Y in its Display tab: unchanged. A display set to snap to a frame still snaps after such clicks. A real drag (more than a few pixels) still moves it and keeps the new place." },
    { key = "B29", text = "[B29] (Options 0.6.7) A condition's cue changes: set Desaturate to \"off (full color)\" and Glow to \"off\", close and reopen the settings. |cffffd100Expect:|r both still read \"off\" (they used to fall back to \"no change\")." },
    { key = "B100", text = "[B100] (Options 0.6.34) Rules > Enabled, open a group that holds at least one display and pick its |cffffd100Display|r tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Pause preview animations\" is the first tick box on the Display tab; the |cffffd100Group|r tab no longer shows it. Turn on the group's preview (eye icon in the sidebar), tick it: the sample countdown, fades and flash stop while the images stay on screen; untick: they run again. A group with no displays has no Display tab and so no tick box." },
    { key = "B101", text = "[B101] (Options 0.6.4, #300) A rule whose Buff / Aura trigger tracks an aura that never stacks (e.g. Untethered Rage), with an icon or text cue: open the cue's display settings. |cffffd100Expect:|r no \"Stacks / Charges Count\" section (unless it was already switched on before, then it stays). A rule whose Cooldown trigger tracks a spell with 2 or more charges: the section is there." },
    { key = "B102", text = "[B102] (core 0.5.76, #288) A rule whose built-in Buff / Aura trigger is already in use: Triggers tab, add a trigger. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Buff / Aura (another)\" is offered; add it with a second aura ID; both triggers stay in the rule after closing and reopening it." },
    { key = "B103", text = "[B103] (#192, #193) A rule with two triggers, out of combat. |cffffd100Expect:|r a \"This rule is activated by\" choice at the top of the Triggers tab; each trigger's header shows TRUE (green), FALSE (red) or UNKNOWN (yellow) and changes when the aura or cooldown changes. In combat, a trigger the game hides shows UNKNOWN (and does not fire)." },
    { key = "B104", text = "[B104] (#194) A rule with a condition of two checks: open the Conditions tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r each check's line shows \"check TRUE/FALSE\" and \"so far TRUE/FALSE\" (the running result), and a false check never reads UNKNOWN." },
    { key = "B105", text = "[B105] (#150) A rule with an icon cue and no condition set: click the eye icon on the rule in the sidebar. |cffffd100Expect:|r the icon preview appears (the cue follows the rule's triggers)." },
    { key = "B106", text = "[B106] (#147) On a Death Knight, add a trigger. |cffffd100Expect:|r runes are under \"Class Resource (combo points, runes, holy power...)\" as \"Runes (Death Knight)\"; there is no separate runes entry in the add list. An older rule that used the separate runes trigger still works." },
    { key = "B107", text = "[B107] (#285) A rule with an icon cue: in its Buff / Aura trigger type a new aura ID and press Enter. |cffffd100Expect:|r the icon changes from \"?\" to the aura's icon at once, without reopening the rule." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-combat-8", { title = "3. Combat displays (8 of 16)", order = 300.08, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "B108", text = "[B108] (#173, #314) A speech or sound cue set to fire at \"seconds left 2 or less\" on a buff that is NOT in your Cooldown Manager; pull a training dummy and get the buff. |cffffd100Expect:|r the cue fires once, about 2 s before the buff ends. If it is early, late or silent: type |cff88ccff/xui debug timing|r and send its output." },
    { key = "B109", text = "[B109] (#311) Death Knight: a rule tracking Anti-Magic Shell with an icon (duration sweep and time text) or a duration bar. In combat on a dummy, cast Anti-Magic Shell. |cffffd100Expect:|r the sweep or bar drains and the time counts down. If the icon shows but does not drain: |cff88ccff/xuiengine|r while it is up, and send the output." },
    { key = "B110", text = "[B110] (#353) A Sound cue with a [Game] sound and channel \"Master\". In the game's Sound settings untick Sound Effects (keep Master on) and test the cue. |cffffd100Expect:|r it plays. Then set the cue's channel to \"Ambience\", untick Ambience in the game: |cffffd100Expect:|r silent. Report both." },
    { key = "B111", text = "[B111] (#155) While stunned, then feared, rooted and silenced (a duel or a mob that does it), type |cff88ccff/xui debug loc|r each time. |cffffd100Expect:|r one line per effect with its type and spell ID. Send all lines (they settle which effect names the \"Loss of control on you\" trigger uses)." },
    { key = "B112", text = "[B112] (core 0.6.34, #121) Any icon with time text on a buff with a readable duration, out of combat. |cffffd100Expect:|r the time counts down as before (an internal tidy-up of the same code; nothing should look different)." },
    { key = "B113", text = "[B113] (core 0.6.35, B4) Pick a spell a talent replaces on your bar (the bar shows the replacement). Make two rules on the base spell's ID, State \"Cooldown ready\", each with an icon; tick |cffffd100Exact spell ID|r on the second. Use the replacement, then |cff88ccff/xui debug status|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the first rule reads the replacement (its status line says \"reading <ID>, the spell on your bar\" for a charge spell); the second reads the base ID. Report whether the two icons differ: the game's documentation does not say whether it gives the base ID its own cooldown while it is replaced (if both always match, the tick box changes nothing for that spell)." },
    { key = "B114", text = "[B114] (core 0.6.40, #309) Play 5 minutes with your usual rules (a few pulls on a dummy), then hover the addon-usage tooltip and note XayaUI's memory. Type |cff88ccff/run collectgarbage(\"collect\")|r and hover again. |cffffd100Expect:|r XayaUI's memory climbs more slowly than on 0.6.39 between collections, and after the collect it drops to a few MB (the bench measured 7.8 MB live with your rules). Send both numbers; nothing else should look or sound different." },
    { key = "B98", text = "[B98] (Options 0.6.37) |cff88ccff/reload|r, then |cff88ccff/xui|r and open a rule with a Buff / Aura trigger. Type |cff88ccffwell|r in its aura box with food in your bags. |cffffd100Expect:|r Well Fed shows with \"from <your food>\", and the list's bottom right reads |cffffd100Search all spells|r. Hover the latency tooltip: |cffffd100Expect:|r XayaUI_Options is far below the 521 MB seen before (note the number). Type a spell of another class: |cffffd100Expect:|r \"No match in your spells, rules or bags\"; click |cffffd100Search all spells|r: |cffffd100Expect:|r the footer counts up and the spell appears. Close the settings window, wait 10 seconds, |cff88ccff/run collectgarbage(\"collect\")|r, hover the tooltip again: |cffffd100Expect:|r XayaUI_Options back down to about where it was before you clicked Search all. Note all three numbers." },
    { key = "B115", text = "[B115] (core 0.6.45, Options 0.6.39) With all your rules loaded, |cff88ccff/xui|r, then Settings > Debugging. Tick and untick |cffffd100Console window (separate from this window)|r a few times. |cffffd100Expect:|r the console window opens / closes on the click with no noticeable pause, and the tick follows (before: two full rebuilds of the window per click, about 0.9-1.3 s of Lua work with 229 rules in the test harness; not measured in game). Untick and tick |cffffd100Show the debug console at the bottom of the window|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the strip under the window disappears / comes back on the click itself, no pause. With the settings window still open, close the console window with its X, then type |cff88ccff/xui console|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the switch unticks / ticks within a frame, no pause. Then rename a rule (or change any other setting) and check the left list shows the change straight away (a change that needs a full redraw still gets one). No Lua error." },
    { key = "B116", text = "[B116] (Options 0.6.39) Open the settings window. |cffffd100Expect:|r bottom-left corner shows only \"XayaUI v0.6.39\" (no \"Addon Info\" next to it), in your theme's accent color (purple with the default theme, your class color with the class theme). Hover it. |cffffd100Expect:|r it turns the lighter accent and a tooltip says it opens Addon Info. Click it. |cffffd100Expect:|r the Addon Info page opens. Change the theme (Settings > Theme) and look again. |cffffd100Expect:|r the version text takes the new accent color. Collapse the window (the arrow) and expand it: the text hides and comes back. (B71 checked the old layout with a separate Addon Info link.)" },
    { key = "B117", text = "[B117] (Options 0.6.39) Rules tab: click Smart Categories, Enabled, Disabled and Drafts in turn. |cffffd100Expect:|r the sub-tab row looks the same every time: compact tabs, each just wider than its name, starting at the left, and Class/Spec Rule Creator alone at the right edge (as it looked with Smart Categories selected). Make the window narrower and wider by dragging its edge. |cffffd100Expect:|r the tabs never stretch to fill the row. Note it if any other tab row (a rule's own tabs, QoL) still stretches: only the Rules sub-tab row was changed." },
    { key = "B130", text = "[B130] (core 0.6.46) Type |cff88ccff/xui help|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"commands (N):\" and then one command per line (in chat, or in the console window if your messages go there; also under Console in the chat history), each command in your theme's accent color with what it does after it, and |cff88ccff/xui debug auras|r listed twice (with targets, and with a spell ID) on separate lines. No line holds two commands. Arguments like |cff88ccff[on||off]|r show a single \"||\"." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-combat-9", { title = "3. Combat displays (9 of 16)", order = 300.09, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "B118", text = "[B118] (core 0.6.46; cursor trail colors as UI themes) First note your current theme (or save it: Name and Save at the bottom of the Theme page). |cff88ccff/xui|r, Settings > UI Options > Theme, open the |cffffd100Theme|r list. |cffffd100Expect:|r after the Light mode and Colorblind entries, nine new ones in this order: Cursor trail: Fel, Fire, Ocean, Aurora, Sunset, Vaporwave, Rainbow, Gold, Frost; then Custom and your saved themes. Pick |cffffd100Cursor trail: Fire|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the window background, panes, borders and the rule names (body text) look exactly as with the XUI default (dark, near-white text); headings and field labels pale yellow; the selected rule's name light orange; the selected tab's outline and the footer's \"XayaUI v...\" text orange; the red Add buttons now dark orange with pale-yellow text; the glow behind a selected rule's top group dark red. Pick each of the other eight in turn. |cffffd100Expect:|r every heading, label, button text, the selected rule's name and the footer text are easy to read on the window in all nine (computed at 4.5:1 or better; the window's see-through background over a bright scene can make it worse in game: note any that is hard to read and where). Frost's headings come out white and Gold's cream: say whether you want them that way. Then pick your own theme again. |cffffd100Expect:|r everything as before. No Lua error." },
    { key = "B119", text = "[B119] (core 0.6.46) Pick |cffffd100Cursor trail: Ocean|r, then change one Palette color (e.g. Muted text). |cffffd100Expect:|r the theme switches to Custom and its |cffffd100Start from|r shows Cursor trail: Ocean; the Start from list also offers all nine cursor themes. Click Clear my colors, then pick Cursor trail: Ocean again. Switch |cffffd100XayaUI QoL|r off in the AddOns list and relog (or |cff88ccff/reload|r). |cffffd100Expect:|r the Ocean colors are still there and the nine themes are still listed (they do not need QoL). Switch QoL back on, relog, and pick your own theme again." },
    { key = "B131", text = "[B131] (Options 0.6.40) |cff88ccff/xui|r, the toolbar's Settings button, then UI Options > Rule Creation. |cffffd100Expect:|r under Rule list, a section |cffffd100All talents (every class and spec)|r: a line \"Last talent scan <date> (build <n>): N classes, M nodes.\" (or \"No talent scan saved yet.\"), the text naming |cff88ccff/xui debug talents|r, |cff88ccff/xui debug talents status|r and |cff88ccff/xui debug talents <name>|r, and a |cffffd100Scan all talents now|r button. Out of combat with the talent window closed, click the button. |cffffd100Expect:|r chat says \"Scanning all classes (about a second)...\", then \"talent scan done: 13 classes, ...\"; the same \"talent scan done\" line shows under the button and the last-scan line shows today's date and time. Then Rules > Class/Spec Rule Creator. |cffffd100Expect:|r no All talents section and no scan button there (the spec buttons and Auto-populate are unchanged). Open a rule's talent requirement and search a talent of another spec of your class. |cffffd100Expect:|r it is found (the search reads that scan)." },
    { key = "B140", text = "[B140] (core 0.6.47, V14 off costs nothing) |cff88ccff/xui|r, Settings > UI Options > Display: untick |cffffd100Show a XayaUI button in the Game Menu (ESC menu)|r, then |cff88ccff/reload|r. Press Esc. |cffffd100Expect:|r Blizzard's menu with no XayaUI entry and no empty gap; every entry is visible and does what it says. Type |cff88ccff/xui debug gamemenu|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the first line says |cff88ccffenabled=false|r and |cff88ccffhooked=false|r (nothing of the button was set up). Close the menu, tick the switch again, press Esc. |cffffd100Expect:|r the XayaUI button after Macros, as before; it opens the settings window. Close the menu, untick the switch, press Esc. |cffffd100Expect:|r no XayaUI entry and no invisible gap; click |cffffd100Return to Game|r and |cffffd100Macros|r to check both work (a slot the button had used is given back). No Lua error." },
    { key = "B141", text = "[B141] (Reskin 0.6.2) Blizzard UI Reskin > Esc Menu: untick |cffffd100Use the XayaUI Game Menu look|r (its tooltip now says a /reload removes its hooks fully), |cff88ccff/reload|r, press Esc. |cffffd100Expect:|r Blizzard's own menu, fully visible (not faded, not see-through). |cff88ccff/xui debug gamemenu|r prints |cff88ccffgame menu skin: on=false|r. Tick the look, press Esc. |cffffd100Expect:|r XayaUI's look, as in G1. Close the menu, untick the look, press Esc at once. |cffffd100Expect:|r Blizzard's menu fully visible right away (it must never open invisible or faded). Tick it again and check the look comes back. No Lua error." },
    { key = "B142", text = "[B142] (core 0.6.47) Settings > Debugging: untick |cffffd100Advanced Debugging|r, |cff88ccff/reload|r. Change zone and hit a training dummy until combat ends. Tick |cffffd100Advanced Debugging|r (with |cffffd100Keep the debug record|r ticked and the default categories), change zone, fight the dummy again, then |cffffd100View the debug record|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r a \"zone: ...\" line, and \"combat N starts\" / \"combat N ends\" lines with the engine status. Untick the |cffffd100Game state|r category, change zone, fight again, view the record. |cffffd100Expect:|r no new \"zone:\" line, but new combat start / end lines. Tick Game state again. Untick |cffffd100Advanced Debugging|r, fight once more. |cffffd100Expect:|r nothing new in the record. No Lua error." },
    { key = "B143", text = "[B143] (core 0.6.47) Settings > Debugging: set |cffffd100XayaUI's messages|r to |cffffd100Both|r (they then reach chat and the console window), tick |cffffd100Console window|r, type |cff88ccff/xui debug gamemenu|r, then close the console window with its X. Type |cff88ccff/xui debug status|r and |cff88ccff/xui debug gamemenu|r again. Then |cff88ccff/xui console|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the window shows the lines of both commands typed while it was closed, below the first |cff88ccff/xui debug gamemenu|r lines, in the order you typed them, each once. With |cffffd100XayaUI's messages|r set to the console window and |cffffd100Open the console window when a message arrives|r ticked: close the window and type |cff88ccff/xui debug gamemenu|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the window opens by itself and the new lines are at the bottom, each once (not twice). No Lua error." },
    { key = "B144", text = "[B144] (core 0.6.47) Settings > Minimap Button: untick |cffffd100Show the minimap button|r, |cff88ccff/reload|r, then take a portal or hearth (a loading screen). |cffffd100Expect:|r no XayaUI minimap button at any point. Tick it. |cffffd100Expect:|r the button appears at its saved position at once. Take another loading screen. |cffffd100Expect:|r the button is still on the minimap edge at the same place. Untick it. |cffffd100Expect:|r it disappears at once and stays gone after the next loading screen." },
    { key = "B145", text = "[B145] (core 0.6.47) A rule with a sound file and a Buff / Aura trigger (as in B33): tick |cffffd100Let the game play this sound on the aura itself|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r after a moment the status line under it says the game plays the sound; gaining the aura plays it once. Untick it. |cffffd100Expect:|r the status line goes; gaining the aura plays XayaUI's own copy once (not twice, not silent). With no rule ticked, |cff88ccff/reload|r and gain the aura: |cffffd100Expect:|r XayaUI's own sound once, as before. No Lua error." },
    { key = "B132", text = "[B132] (Options 0.6.41, V14 off costs nothing) |cff88ccff/xui|r, Rules tab, click |cffffd100Smart Categories|r, then click the eye on any rule row so its display shows on screen as a preview. Close the window with its X. |cffffd100Expect:|r the preview display disappears at once (not a moment later). |cff88ccff/xui|r again. |cffffd100Expect:|r Smart Categories is the open sub-tab and no eye is on." },
    { key = "B133", text = "[B133] (Options 0.6.41) Settings > Debugging: set |cffffd100XayaUI's messages|r to |cffffd100Both|r and keep |cffffd100Show the debug console at the bottom of the window|r ticked. |cff88ccff/xui|r, read the last line of the debug console strip under the window, close the window, then type |cff88ccff/xui calc 2+2|r. |cff88ccff/xui|r again. |cffffd100Expect:|r the strip's last line now reads |cff88ccff2+2 = 4|r, below the line you read (nothing missing, nothing twice)." },
    { key = "B134", text = "[B134] (Options 0.6.41) Settings > UI Options > Rule Creation: |cffffd100Use drafts (save bar)|r unticked (the default). |cff88ccff/xui|r, click a rule, change one of its settings (e.g. a trigger's spell or a display's size), wait a second, press |cffffd100Ctrl+Z|r with the mouse over the window. |cffffd100Expect:|r chat says \"undid the last change to '<rule>'\" and the setting is back to what it was; the very first change to that rule can be undone. Tick |cffffd100Use drafts (save bar)|r, change the rule again. |cffffd100Expect:|r the unsaved-changes strip shows under the window as before; close the window: the rule goes back and the edit is in Drafts." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-combat-10", { title = "3. Combat displays (10 of 16)", order = 300.1, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "B135", text = "[B135] (Options 0.6.41) Type |cff88ccff/xui debug perf|r (rebuild timing ON), |cff88ccff/xui|r, click a tab, then another. |cffffd100Expect:|r chat lines \"trace +N frame(s): ...\" with N counting up from 0 after each click, as before. |cff88ccff/xui debug perf|r again (OFF), close the window. |cffffd100Expect:|r no more trace lines." },
    { key = "B146", text = "[B146] (Options 0.6.42; SUPERSEDED by B151-B153: the picker became the table in Options 0.6.44, skip) Rules > Class/Spec Rule Creator, in a spec whose debuffs are in your Cooldown Manager (e.g. Vengeance with Fiery Brand and Sigil of Flame tracked). |cffffd100Expect:|r under |cffffd100Choose which rules to make|r your cooldowns first, then your target debuffs marked \"(target debuff)\"; a buff on yourself is not listed as a debuff. Hover a debuff: the tooltip names its aura ID and the Cooldown Manager ID. Send a screenshot if a debuff is missing or a buff shows up as a debuff (that tells us what the game's \"selfAura\" flag really means)." },
    { key = "B147", text = "[B147] (Options 0.6.42; SUPERSEDED by B151-B153: the picker became the table in Options 0.6.44, skip) Tick one cooldown with |cffffd100Speech|r, one with |cffffd100Icon|r, one debuff with |cffffd100Progress texture|r / |cffffd100On the target|r and one with |cffffd100Speech|r / |cffffd100Missing from target|r, and one row with |cffffd100Progress bar|r. Press |cffffd100Make the ticked rules|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the message says 4 made and 1 not made (progress bar); 4 rules under \"<Class> <Spec> - autorule population\" > Cooldowns / Target Debuffs, each with one cue. Out of combat: the speech says \"<name> ready\" when the cooldown comes back; the progress texture shows while your debuff is on the target and drains; the \"missing\" speech plays when the debuff falls off. Press Make again: nothing new is made." },
    { key = "B148", text = "[B148] (Options 0.6.42, still valid in 0.6.44) In combat on a dummy, with a debuff rule from B153 whose debuff IS in your Cooldown Manager and one whose debuff is NOT. |cffffd100Expect:|r the first follows the debuff in combat; the second is unknown in combat (no cue), and |cff88ccff/xui status|r says why." },
    { key = "B136", text = "[B136] (Options 0.6.41, Bonus 0.6.12) With Bonus Features > Data Panels ticked and its Right Panel on (FPS is one of its blocks), |cff88ccff/xui|r, open a few pages, close the window and wait 10 seconds out of combat. Hover the FPS block. |cffffd100Expect:|r under \"Top by CPU (now)\" |cffffd100XayaUI_Options|r is not listed, or shows 0.0% (its window driver no longer runs while the window is closed). (INFERENCE: the list reads the game's add-on profiler, C_AddOnProfiler; if the game has it switched off the tooltip says so and this step is skipped.)" },
    { key = "B149", text = "[B149] (core 0.6.48, Options 0.6.43) Make a rule on a buff the game hides in combat (most of them; |cff88ccff/xui debug auras <ID>|r says \"no (secret in combat ...)\") that is NOT in your Cooldown Manager, with an icon cue. Open the rule's Display tab, then its Cues tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r both start with a red line \"This aura (<name>, <ID>) requires Blizzard's Cooldown Manager to track it before it can be tracked by the addon ...\". Add the buff to Tracked Buffs in the Cooldown Manager's settings, reopen the rule: the line is gone. A rule on an aura that is never hidden shows no line. Do the same with a Target Debuff rule (B147): the line says \"This debuff (...)\"." },
    { key = "B150", text = "[B150] (core 0.6.49; the map, Xaya: \"map eclipses full screen\", 2026-11-06: \"only with XayaUI on\". NOT a fix: the cause was not found offline; this step finds it) 1. With XayaUI on, press |cffffd100M|r. If the map fills the screen, type |cff88ccff/xui debug map|r and copy the lines (\"map: world map: ... maximized ...\", \"map: CVars: miniWorldMap N ...\", \"map: XayaUI since login: ...\"). 2. Click the map's shrink button (top right), close it, press |cffffd100M|r again, |cff88ccff/xui debug map|r again. 3. |cff88ccff/reload|r, press |cffffd100M|r, |cff88ccff/xui debug map|r once more. 4. Bisect: in the AddOns list switch off |cffffd100XayaUI QoL|r only, relog, press |cffffd100M|r; then QoL back on and |cffffd100XayaUI Blizzard Reskin|r off; then |cffffd100XayaUI Bonus Features|r; then |cffffd100XayaUI Chat|r (one at a time). Also try with the Character Reskin's |cffffd100Wider window|r unticked. |cffffd100Expect / report:|r which step makes the map open small again, and the copied lines (miniWorldMap 0 means the game itself is set to open the map full screen; 1 with a full-screen map means something else maximized it)." },
    { key = "B151", text = "[B151] (Options 0.6.53) Rules > Class/Spec Rule Creator, in a spec whose auras and debuffs are in your Cooldown Manager. Press your spec's |cffffd100Generate All Rules for <Spec>|r button. |cffffd100Expect:|r nothing is made; a box below the buttons titled |cffffd100Auto-populate: <Spec>|r, two help lines, the switch |cffffd100Hide / Show already generated rules (can potentially cause duplicates)|r (unticked), a header row: tick box || Name || Type || Trigger || Cue type || Cue set-up || Combat load, then the headers |cffffd100Spell CD|r, |cffffd100Aura|r, |cffffd100Debuff|r, each with a tick box and its rows A-Z; each Name has the spell's icon. At the bottom, in one row: |cffffd100Advanced|r, |cffffd100Populate|r, |cffffd100Reload list|r, |cffffd100Close|r. |cffffd100Each row sits on one line, the columns line up under the header, nothing runs past the right edge|r (send a screenshot at your normal window size either way; say if a dropdown's text is cut or a column is too narrow for its text)." },
    { key = "B152", text = "[B152] (Options 0.6.53) Click the header tick box: every row is ticked; again: all unticked. Click the |cffffd100Aura|r header's tick box: only the aura rows are ticked; again: they untick. Press |cffffd100Advanced|r: an |cffffd100Extra cues|r column appears; give one Speech row an extra |cffffd100Sound|r: its Cue set-up cell shows the Customize box and a sound picker side by side, and the row still fits on one line. Press |cffffd100Generate All Rules for my class|r: the title says \"(all specs)\", a |cffffd100Spec|r column appears after Name, all specs' rows are mixed under the same three headers (other specs list cooldowns only). |cffffd100Reload list|r re-reads the list; |cffffd100Close|r hides the table." },
    { key = "B153", text = "[B153] (Options 0.6.53) Tick: a cooldown with |cffffd100Speech|r (leave Customize unticked), a cooldown with |cffffd100Speech|r and tick |cffffd100Customize|r (a small window opens: type \"test words\", OK: the cell shows \"test words\"), an aura with |cffffd100Progress texture|r and no picture picked, a debuff with |cffffd100Sound|r (its Trigger switches to |cffffd100When missing|r by itself) and no sound picked, a cooldown with |cffffd100Icon|r, and one row with |cffffd100Progress bar (soonTM)|r. Press |cffffd100Populate|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r a popup with OK: \"error issue making the following rules: [<aura>, <debuff>]. Please finish configuring them to create them.\"; the two speech rules and the icon rule are made and leave the table; the unfinished two stay ticked; the progress bar row stays and the message says it is (soonTM). Pick the picture and the sound, press |cffffd100Populate|r again: both are made. In the sidebar: <Class> > <Spec> > Speech / Icons / Progress Textures / Sounds; the rules are named after the spells (no icon in the name), the cues \"<spell> (speech)\", \"<spell> (icon)\", ... Out of combat: the first speech says the spell's name when it comes back, the second says \"test words\"; the sound plays when your debuff is missing from the target." },
    { key = "B154", text = "[B154] (Options 0.6.53) On screen after B153: the shown cues sit in rows of 3 centred on the middle of the screen (the 2nd cue of a row on the centre): row 1 at the centre, row 2 below, row 3 above, row 4 further below. Nothing sits on top of another cue (screenshot). Drag one of them away (|cff88ccff/xui unlock|r), make one more icon rule with |cffffd100Populate|r: the dragged cue stays where you put it; the others are laid out again from the centre with the new one. Untick |cffffd100Include talents I have not picked|r with your own spec's table open: your unpicked talent cooldowns leave the list; press another spec's button: all of its talent cooldowns are listed. Your ticks and choices are still there after a /reload. Performance: with the all-specs list open, |cff88ccff/xui debug perf|r while clicking ticks (report the numbers for #309; they decide whether the list needs pages, A2)." },
    { key = "B155", text = "[B155] (Options 0.6.53) Press |cffffd100Reload list|r after B153: the rules you made are not listed. Tick |cffffd100Hide / Show already generated rules (can potentially cause duplicates)|r: they are listed again, unticked. Tick one by hand, press |cffffd100Populate|r: a second copy of that rule is made (as the label warns). Untick the switch: they leave the list again. Open a row's |cffffd100Cue type|r dropdown: Icon, Progress texture, Progress bar (soonTM), Texture, Text, Speech, Sound, Custom (soonTM), every one readable." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-combat-11", { title = "3. Combat displays (11 of 16)", order = 300.11, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "B160", text = "[B160] (Options 0.6.54; Xaya, 2026-11-06: four Generate buttons per spec, each filters the list; Select all tick box) Rules > Class/Spec Rule Creator, freshly opened after /reload. |cffffd100Expect:|r no table and no list yet. Under \"Auto-populate my class / spec\": for each of your specs four buttons, worded exactly |cffffd100Generate All Rules for <Spec>|r, |cffffd100Generate CD Tracking Rules for <Spec>|r, |cffffd100Generate Aura Tracking Rules for <Spec>|r, |cffffd100Generate Target Debuff Tracking Rules for <Spec>|r, and the same four ending |cffffd100for my class|r; no button says \"Auto-populate\". Press |cffffd100Generate CD Tracking Rules for <your current spec>|r: a table lists only Spell CD rows. |cffffd100Generate Aura Tracking Rules ...|r: only Aura rows. |cffffd100Generate Target Debuff Tracking Rules ...|r: only Debuff rows. |cffffd100Generate All Rules ...|r: all three groups. Press |cffffd100Generate Aura Tracking Rules|r for a spec you are NOT in: the table says \"Auras and target debuffs are read from your Cooldown Manager for the spec you are in now. Switch to <Spec>, then press the button again.\" In any list: the tick box |cffffd100Select all|r sits above the header row; click it: every row shown is ticked; again: all unticked; after a filtered button only the rows listed are ticked. |cffffd100Reload list|r and |cffffd100Include talents I have not picked|r keep the filter. |cffffd100Report:|r whether the buttons fit (none cut off, how they wrap), and whether you want a second Select all (there is also the header-row tick box)." },
    { key = "B156", text = "[B156] (core 0.6.50; Xaya 2026-11-05: \"XUI Console does nothing and has no input options\") Settings > Debugging: set |cffffd100XayaUI's messages|r to |cffffd100Chat window|r. Type |cff88ccff/xui console|r, then press |cffffd100Clear|r in the window. |cffffd100Expect:|r the window says \"Nothing here yet. Type a XayaUI command in the line below ...\" and \"XayaUI's other messages go to the chat window\"; along the bottom, left of the resize grip, a line reading \"Type a command, Enter to run it (help, debug, debug status)\". Click that line, type |cff88ccffdebug status|r, press Enter. |cffffd100Expect:|r |cff88ccff> /xui debug status|r in grey, then the status lines, all in the console window and none in chat; the hint is gone; the line is empty and still has the cursor. Type |cff88ccff/xui help|r, Enter. |cffffd100Expect:|r the command list in the console window. Press the Up arrow. |cffffd100Expect:|r |cff88ccff/xui help|r comes back (then Down / Up walk the earlier ones; if the arrows do nothing, report it: that part is not checked outside the game). Type |cff88ccff/reload|r, Enter. |cffffd100Expect:|r a red \"Only XayaUI's own commands run here\" line, and no reload. Press Esc: the cursor leaves the line. Type |cff88ccff/xui debug status|r in the normal chat box. |cffffd100Expect:|r it prints in chat, as before. |cffffd100Clear|r again: the hint is back. No Lua error. Screenshot please." },
    { key = "B157", text = "[B157] (core 0.6.50; Xaya 2026-11-05: \"can't some of these be consolidated into a /xui debug _____ ? this is a LOT of noise\"; her answers of 2026-11-06: status and auras shortcuts, \"/xui debug loader\", \"Back to '||'\") Settings > Debugging: |cffffd100XayaUI's messages|r = |cffffd100Chat window|r; close the console window. Type |cff88ccff/xui help|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r 16 lines (it was 29): |cff88ccff/xui|r, console, bug, unlock, status, auras, debug, then the features' (data, notes, calc, chat, panel, privacy, cursor, stats, reskin with the add-ons you have on); no probe / perf / timing / chatprobe lines; option lists read |cff88ccff[on||off||...]|r with every |cff88ccff|||r and every letter there (it showed |cff88ccff[highlighttrail]|r and |cff88ccffstatusidthprobe|r), also in the chat history window's Console tab (D12). Type |cff88ccff/xui debug|r in the normal chat box. |cffffd100Expect:|r the console window opens and shows \"debug commands (N), each typed as /xui debug <name>:\" with one line per command (since core 0.6.56, without XayaUI Dev Assist: status, perf, talents, loader, auras; with it also probe, debuffs, perf ui, timing, model, tracker, loc, media, mods, groups, icons, seed, map, gamemenu, chatprobe, widthprobe); nothing of it in chat. Close the console window; type |cff88ccff/xui debug status|r in chat. |cffffd100Expect:|r the console window opens with the status lines; none in chat. Type |cff88ccff/xui status|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the status lines in chat. Type |cff88ccff/xui auras|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r your buffs with IDs, in chat. Set |cffffd100XayaUI's messages|r to |cffffd100XayaUI console window|r and type |cff88ccff/xui status|r again. |cffffd100Expect:|r still in chat. In the console's own line type |cff88ccffstatus|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r in the console window. |cff88ccff/xui debug loader|r: two lines starting \"debug:\" in the console window; |cff88ccff/xui debug window|r: \"there is no debug command\". |cff88ccff/xui perf|r (an old form): the |cff88ccff/xui help|r list instead. |cff88ccff/xui debug nosuch|r: \"there is no debug command\" and the list. With XayaUI Dev Assist switched off in the AddOns list (|cff88ccff/reload|r), |cff88ccff/xui debug chatprobe|r |cffffd100Expect:|r \"there is no debug command \"chatprobe\".\" and the list (core 0.6.56; it said \"part of XayaUI Chat\" before). No Lua error." },
    { key = "B158", text = "[B158] (core 0.6.50; Xaya 2026-11-06: \"Yes, but /save should trigger a reload\", of /reload \"Both work\", and of chat-routed messages in the console: \"Only xui console messages should display\") Settings > Debugging: |cffffd100XayaUI's messages|r = |cffffd100Chat window|r. |cff88ccff/xui console|r, then type |cff88ccff/xui unlock|r twice in the normal chat box. |cffffd100Expect:|r the unlock / lock lines in chat only, none in the console window. In the console's command line type |cff88ccff/dance|r, Enter. |cffffd100Expect:|r the red \"Only XayaUI's own commands run here (and /save or /reload, which reload the interface)\" line, no dance. Type |cff88ccff/save|r, Enter. |cffffd100Expect:|r the interface reloads (loading screen) with no \"Interface action failed\" or \"blocked\" message; afterwards your settings are as you left them. Open the console again, type |cff88ccff/reload|r, Enter. |cffffd100Expect:|r the same reload. No Lua error." },
    { key = "B159", text = "[B159] (core 0.6.52) Open a rule on a buff the game hides in combat that is NOT in your Cooldown Manager (as in B149). |cffffd100Expect:|r the red line reads exactly \"This aura (<name>) requires Blizzard's Cooldown Manager to track it before it can be tracked by the addon. In the Cooldown Manager's settings, move it to Tracked Buffs or Tracked Bars (the game hides it in combat, encounters, Mythic+ and PvP).\" (the name, no ID; a target debuff rule says \"This debuff (<name>) ...\"). For an aura the Cooldown Manager does not offer for your spec at all, it reads exactly \"Blizzard's Cooldown Manager does not offer in-combat tracking for this aura for your current spec. Rule might not work reliably.\"" },
    { key = "B190", text = "[B190] (core 0.6.56, Options 0.6.55; fast-tracked, Xaya 2026-11-06: \"typing /xui and closing the menu does not turn off previews\") |cff88ccff/xui|r. In the sidebar unlock one rule (its padlock turns into the gold arrows), click the eye of another, unlock a group's padlock, and press |cffffd100Lock Positions|r in the toolbar. Displays show with their boxes and names. Type |cff88ccff/xui|r again (or press Close). |cffffd100Expect:|r every one of those displays is gone at once (except ones whose aura is really up). |cff88ccff/xui|r again: every row shows the white padlock and the slashed eye. Then type |cff88ccff/xui unlock|r with the window closed, open and close the window: the displays stay unlocked (that unlock was not made in the window); |cff88ccff/xui unlock|r again locks them." },
    { key = "B191", text = "[B191] (Options 0.6.55) The sidebar icons: the eye and the headphone have a slash and are dimmed while their preview is off, plain and bright while it is on; the |cffffd100LOADED|r and |cffffd100NOT LOADED|r rows have an eye that previews every rule in that list (no headphone there). The movement lock is a flat white padlock; an unlocked row shows a flat gold four-way arrow (the toolbar's |cffffd100Lock Positions|r button uses the same padlock). Send a screenshot of the sidebar." },
    { key = "B192", text = "[B192] (Options 0.6.55) Ctrl+click two rules that each show a display. |cffffd100Expect:|r the bar above the list reads |cffffd100Delete (2)|r, |cffffd100Move (2)|r, |cffffd100Deselect (2)|r, every label readable inside its button. Right-click one of them: |cffffd100Link 2 Selected (move together)|r. Choose it, |cff88ccff/xui unlock|r, drag one display: the other moves with it (Shift-drag: alone). Right-click again: |cffffd100Unlink 2 Selected|r; after it they move separately." },
    { key = "B193", text = "[B193] (core 0.6.56, D7) With many rules, switch a group of them off (right-click > Disable). |cff88ccff/xui debug perf|r for a minute of normal play, before and after. |cffffd100Expect:|r the switched-off rules' displays are gone at once and do not come back in the unlock view (|cff88ccff/xui unlock|r); their eye in the sidebar still previews them (and the display goes away again when the preview ends); they are still listed under Rules > Disabled; switching one back on shows it as before. Report the two perf readings." },
    { key = "B194", text = "[B194] (core 0.6.56) Make a rule with the trigger Player State > |cffffd100Dead, not released|r = Yes and a text cue \"DEAD\". Die (a duel or fall damage works). |cffffd100Expect:|r \"DEAD\" shows while you lie dead with the release window up; it goes away the moment you release (as a ghost) and stays away; it never shows while alive." },
    { key = "B195", text = "[B195] (core 0.6.56, Options 0.6.55) Open a rule's Load tab, Talents: Match ALL, add a talent you have picked. |cffffd100Expect:|r its control reads |cffffd100Known|r in green; click: |cffffd100Not known|r in red (the rule stops loading); click: |cffffd100Not set|r (it loads again whatever the talent); click: |cffffd100Known|r again." },
    { key = "B196", text = "[B196] (core 0.6.56) Add a new |cffffd100Sound|r cue to a rule. |cffffd100Expect:|r its Sound channel reads |cffffd100SFX|r; pick a [Game] sound and test it; lower the game's SFX volume (Options > Sound): the cue gets quieter, Master unchanged. A cue you made before keeps its channel. A Speech cue has no channel choice that matters (the game's speech has none)." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-combat-12", { title = "3. Combat displays (12 of 16)", order = 300.12, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "B211", text = "[B211] (core 0.6.56) Log in on spec A with some auras / debuffs in its Cooldown Manager; wait 5 s out of combat. Switch to spec B. Open Rules > Class/Spec Rule Creator and press spec A's |cffffd100Auto-populate|r button. |cffffd100Expect:|r spec A's list now shows its Aura and Debuff rows too (before: cooldowns only). A spell ID search box finds those auras / debuffs." },
    { key = "B212", text = "[B212] (#278 items 5/6, Xaya: \"I can track sigil of chains slow on an enemy as well as sigil of silence and sigil of misery. Nova and imprison also track\") On a training dummy, for each of Sigil of Chains, Sigil of Silence, Sigil of Misery, Chaos Nova and Imprison: make a Target Debuff rule (Auto-populate's Debuff rows, or by hand with the DEBUFF ID) with a text cue. Cast it in combat. |cffffd100Expect / report per spell:|r the cue shows while the debuff is on the dummy and goes when it ends, in combat. If one does not: type |cff88ccff/xui debug debuffs target|r while it is on the dummy and send the lines. Also say which of them are in your Cooldown Manager." },
    { key = "B199", text = "[B199] (core 0.6.56, D4 / #115) Make a rule on a buff you press (e.g. Demon Spikes) with a Sound cue, and one on a short cooldown with a Sound cue. Press them on a dummy. |cffffd100Expect:|r each sound plays right as the buff appears / the cooldown comes back (no noticeable lag). Then |cff88ccff/xui debug perf|r for one fight on the previous version and on this one if you can (or just this one): report both readings (they decide whether routing stays)." },
    { key = "B180", text = "[B180] (core 0.6.56, Options 0.6.55; REQUEST-LOG #81, Xaya 2026-11-06: developer diagnostics \"Move all of them\"; Combat Tracking Setup \"Rule Creation\"; /xuiskin \"move pad and alpha to dev\"; players keep /xui debug perf, the console forms status and auras, /xuiengine full and refresh) Switch |cffffd100XayaUI Dev Assist|r off in the AddOns list, |cff88ccff/reload|r. Type |cff88ccff/xui debug|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the console window lists exactly status, perf [on||off], talents, loader and auras (two auras lines), and nothing else. Type |cff88ccff/xui debug probe 203720|r, |cff88ccff/xui debug timing|r, |cff88ccff/xui debug map|r, |cff88ccff/xui debug perf ui|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r each says \"there is no debug command ...\" and lists the commands. |cff88ccff/xui debug perf on|r, then |cff88ccff/xui debug perf|r: |cffffd100Expect:|r the engine meter works as before. |cff88ccff/xui status|r and |cff88ccff/xui auras|r: in chat as before. |cff88ccff/xuitt aura 203720|r: |cffffd100Expect:|r the game says it does not know the command. |cff88ccff/xui chat wrap|r: |cffffd100Expect:|r only the Chat Panel's status line, whose word list has no wrap / indent / whispers. |cff88ccff/xuiskin pad 5|r: |cffffd100Expect:|r \"/xuiskin switches the settings window's skin on or off (type it without anything after it).\" and the skin unchanged; |cff88ccff/xuiskin|r alone: \"window skin OFF - type /reload to apply\" (type it again to turn it back on). |cff88ccff/xuiengine auto off|r: |cffffd100Expect:|r the engine status, automatic mode still \"on\", and a help line offering only |cff88ccff/xuiengine full|r and |cff88ccff/xuiengine refresh|r; |cff88ccff/xuiengine full|r and |cff88ccff/xuiengine refresh|r print the status. Open Settings > Debugging. |cffffd100Expect:|r no \"Keep the debug record\", no \"What to record\", no \"Also run the game-data probe\", no \"Combat Tracking Setup\"; a |cffffd100Debug report|r group with |cffffd100Open the debug report|r. Settings > UI Options > Rule Creation. |cffffd100Expect:|r |cffffd100Combat Tracking Setup|r at the bottom with |cffffd100Open Combat Tracking Setup|r (opens the setup window) and |cffffd100Estimate buffs the game hides in combat|r (same tick state as before). No Lua error." },
    { key = "B181", text = "[B181] (core 0.6.56, Dev Assist 0.7.5; REQUEST-LOG #81) Switch |cffffd100XayaUI Dev Assist|r on, |cff88ccff/reload|r. |cff88ccff/xui debug|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the five player commands plus probe (two lines), debuffs, perf ui, timing, model, tracker, loc, media, mods, groups, icons, seed, map, gamemenu, chatprobe, widthprobe. Run |cff88ccff/xui debug probe 203720|r, |cff88ccff/xui debug timing|r, |cff88ccff/xui debug mods|r, |cff88ccff/xui debug map|r, |cff88ccff/xui debug gamemenu|r, |cff88ccff/xui debug perf ui|r (twice: ON then OFF). |cffffd100Expect:|r each prints its report as before 0.6.56 (\"probe spell 203720 ...\", \"timing in combat: ...\", \"map: world map: ...\", \"game menu button: ...\", \"rebuild timing ON ...\"). |cff88ccff/xuitt aura 203720|r: the aura report. |cff88ccff/xui chat wrap|r, |cff88ccff/xui chat indent|r, |cff88ccff/xui chat whispers|r: their measurements. |cff88ccff/xuiskin pad 12|r, reopen the window: the right pane's gutter is wider; |cff88ccff/xuiskin alpha 0.9|r: the background more solid on reopen (|cff88ccff/xuiskin pad 8|r, |cff88ccff/xuiskin alpha 0.62|r back). |cff88ccff/xuiengine auto off|r: automatic mode OFF; the help line also names auto, on / off <group>, reset <group>; |cff88ccff/xuiengine auto on|r. Settings > Debugging. |cffffd100Expect:|r a |cffffd100Dev Assist settings|r group with |cffffd100Also run the game-data probe|r and the |cffffd100Detailed debug record|r (Keep the detailed record, the 11 kinds with their cost, Light set / Everything / Defaults, Lines kept, View / Clear the detailed record, Read a debug report string). No Lua error." },
    { key = "B182", text = "[B182] (core 0.6.56; REQUEST-LOG #82, Xaya 2026-11-06: error codes, auto detection, \"a simple debug report that someone can directly send to me -- either via import/export string or screenshot\"; her answers \"On, errors only\", \"Errors + warnings only\", \"Both: string and screenshot view\") XayaUI Dev Assist off, Settings > Debugging: |cffffd100Advanced Debugging|r ticked (the default). Settings > Debugging > Bug report: |cffffd100Clear the error log|r. Type |cff88ccff/xui report|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r a window \"XayaUI debug report\": made <date>, Game 12.1.5 (build ...), XayaUI addons with versions, \"0 entries ...\" and \"No errors or warnings recorded.\"; a string at the bottom starting |cff88ccffXUIREP1:|r and a |cffffd100Copy string|r button. Now type |cff88ccff/run local f = loadstring(\"error('QA test error')\", \"@Interface/AddOns/XayaUI/QA.lua\"); f()|r (the game shows the error as usual; BugSack too if you have it). Then |cff88ccff/run error(\"not XayaUI\")|r. Type |cff88ccff/xui report|r again. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"1 entry: 1 error, 0 warnings\"; |cff88ccffXUI-E001  x1  Lua error in XayaUI (core: rules, displays, sounds, the combat engine)|r, the first / last time, \"Interface/AddOns/XayaUI/QA.lua:1: QA test error\"; nothing about \"not XayaUI\". Screenshot it. Press |cffffd100Copy string|r, Ctrl+C, and paste it to Xaya. Untick Advanced Debugging, run the first |cff88ccff/run|r again, |cff88ccff/xui report|r: still x1 and \"Advanced Debugging is OFF\". Tick it again. No Lua error from XayaUI itself." },
    { key = "B183", text = "[B183] (core 0.6.56, Dev Assist 0.7.5; REQUEST-LOG #82) With XayaUI Dev Assist on, copy the string from B182 (|cff88ccff/xui report|r > Copy string). Type |cff88ccff/xuidev report|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r a window \"XayaUI Dev Assist: read a debug report string\"; paste the string, press |cffffd100Read|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r a box with the same entries as the report window, each error with a \"stack:\" line. Change one character in the middle of the string and Read again. |cffffd100Expect:|r a red \"The checksum does not match ...\" line. Paste the string into the window of XayaUI's |cffffd100Import|r button. |cffffd100Expect:|r it is refused as not a XayaUI share string; nothing imported." },
    { key = "B168", text = "[B168] (Options 0.6.52; Insivius 2026-11-06: \"Scroll panel broke when I tried to select \"Cursor Highlight\". It will not show more than 4 lines at a time\"; Xaya: \"clicking options in the right hand side panel still consistently drops elements nested within it across all tabs\") Turn on |cffffd100Character Toolkit|r (tick box on its row in QoL). Open |cffffd100QoL > Cursor > Gradient Cursor Trail|r. Click |cffffd100Reverse colors|r on the right five times, then change |cffffd100Gradient|r in its dropdown. Then do the same on Cursor Highlight, on |cffffd100Bonus Features|r (any page) and on |cffffd100Blizzard UI Reskin > Character Pane|r (tick and untick a box). Then drag the window's bottom-right corner up until the sidebar scrolls, and back down to full size. |cffffd100Expect:|r after every click the left sidebar still shows every row it has room for (QoL: Character Toolkit, Panel, Slot Overlays, Spell Math, Tooltip lines, Cursor, Cursor Highlight, Gradient Cursor Trail); no empty space under a few rows; no scroll bar while everything fits; with the window short, fewer rows and a scroll bar; tall again, every row back." },
    { key = "B169", text = "[B169] (core 0.6.54; Xaya 2026-11-06: \"theme names should drop \"cursor theme:\" prefix\") Settings > Theme > |cffffd100Theme|r dropdown. |cffffd100Expect:|r the gradient themes read |cffffd100Fel, Fire, Ocean, Aurora, Sunset, Vaporwave, Rainbow, Gold, Frost|r (no \"Cursor trail:\" in front), after the colour blind ones and before |cffffd100Custom (make your own)|r; a theme you had picked before stays picked (its saved key did not change). Same names in Custom's |cffffd100Start from|r list." },
    { key = "B171", text = "[B171] (Options 0.6.54; group page, Xaya 2026-11-06: \"tabs Group || Display || Load || Config (Group first)\") Open any group. |cffffd100Expect:|r four tabs Group, Display, Load, Config, in that order; Group is picked. Config holds the group's name, an |cffffd100Enabled|r tick box (unticking switches every rule in the group and its nested groups off; ticking switches them all on), Group type (static / dynamic, display groups only), |cffffd100Sound Channel Override|r, + New rule, + Nested group, Delete, and \"Made by: <character> (made here, <date>)\" for a group made now (\"not recorded\" for an older one; an imported group shows its maker or \"imported\"). The Group tab has the group's opacity, scale and layer and the every-display size; Display no longer has the \"Whole group\" box." },
    { key = "B172", text = "[B172] (Options 0.6.54; #372 \"labels on the left and right-hand side with dropdown menus\") Group tab > Group position: |cffffd100Expect:|r Relative to, This group's anchor point and Point on the frame it is relative to each sit on one row, the label on the left and the dropdown on the right; changing them still moves the group." },
    { key = "B173", text = "[B173] (Options 0.6.54; #343, Xaya 2026-11-06: pressing a rule row and dragging did \"Nothing at all\") Rules > Enabled: press and hold a rule row, move the mouse a little. |cffffd100Expect:|r a dark label with the rule's name follows the mouse and says \"above / below <rule>\" or \"into <group>\"; a gold line or a highlighted group row shows where it lands; letting go moves the rule there. A press without moving still just opens the rule. Note it if the label still does not appear." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-combat-13", { title = "3. Combat displays (13 of 16)", order = 300.13, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "B174", text = "[B174] (core 0.6.55, Options 0.6.54; G5 / G11, Xaya: \"size = auto or set + clip / wrap tick boxes; auto fits the showing items, border follows\"; #372 \"background (puts an assigned color / texture under the aura)\") A group with two or more displays: Group tab > Size: |cffffd100Auto|r. Tick |cffffd100Border|r and |cffffd100Background|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r a box with a thin border and a dark background sits behind the showing displays, a few pixels larger (Padding); hide one display (its trigger goes away): the box shrinks to the rest within a fraction of a second. Pick |cffffd100Set|r: Width and Height appear (the old numbers come back); the box takes that size; tick |cffffd100Clip|r: anything outside the box is cut off. Back to Auto: Clip and the sizes hide, nothing is cut off. Background texture: type a texture path or file ID: it shows under the displays in the background colour. Untick both: the box is gone." },
    { key = "B175", text = "[B175] (core 0.6.55, Options 0.6.54; G8, Xaya: \"nested groups get \"anchored to: screen / parent group\"\") A group with a nested group that shows something: open the nested group > Group tab > Group position. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Anchored to: The parent group\" (top-level groups do not show it). Move the parent group (mover view): the nested group moves with it. Pick |cffffd100The screen|r: the nested group now sits from the screen centre by its X / Y and stays put when the parent moves; the parent's opacity and scale still apply to it. In combat a dynamic nested group's icons sit where its outline is." },
    { key = "B176", text = "[B176] (Dev Assist 0.7.4, core 0.6.55; Xaya 2026-11-06: \"All they should have to do is open up /xui dev qa and pick an item and have the addon walk them through steps\") With XayaUI Dev Assist on: |cff88ccff/xui dev qa|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r a window \"XayaUI QA walkthroughs\" listing the walkthroughs (group page, group size / border / background, nested group, sidebar drag, Blizzard UI Reskin switches, Shopping List), each \"not run\". Run \"Group page\": every step shows its text; Do it for me opens the group page; Pass / Fail / Skip go on; the last step deletes the QA test group. End screen: Screenshot saves a screenshot; Export code shows a code starting XUIQA1: (Ctrl+C copies it); Import a code with that code shows the same results; the list now shows the result. |cff88ccff/xui qa test|r and |cff88ccff/xui qatest|r open the same window (Xaya's aliases). Switch Dev Assist off, /reload, |cff88ccff/xui dev qa|r: a line says to switch Dev Assist on. The list also has the walkthroughs made from this checklist, first \"1. Open bugs to confirm\", then \"2. Looks and layout (no effect on use)\", \"3. Combat displays\", \"4. Urgent items\" and one per section; each step starts with its checklist ID. A long step scrolls with the mouse wheel; a long list scrolls too." },
    { key = "B177", text = "[B177] (core 0.6.55, Options 0.6.54; P1 / #268, Xaya 2026-11-06: \"separate points\"; her labels \"Anchor point\" -> \"Anchored to\" -> \"To <target>'s point\") Open a rule with a display in a group that has a set size: its Position section. |cffffd100Expect:|r |cffffd100Anchor point|r (a point of the display), a line \"|cffffd100Anchored to:|r Group: <group name>\" (a display in no group: \"The screen\"), then |cffffd100To <group name>'s point|r (in no group: \"To the screen's point\"); no \"Place the display\" any more. Set Anchor point to Bottom left and To ...'s point to Right: the display does not move when either changes, and from then on its bottom left corner sits at the middle of the group box's right edge plus X / Y (try X = 0, Y = 0). An older display set to \"Outside\" with a corner (for example Top left) now sits outside the box at that corner; before, it sat inside." },
    { key = "B178", text = "[B178] (core 0.6.55; P4 / P5, Xaya 2026-11-06: \"arrow-key nudges yes; moves held until Save\"; \"lock icon in mover tool allows for a temporary lock ... does not force a save. exiting out of mover mode first creates a prompt to cancel or commit move changes\"; the draft) |cff88ccff/xui unlock|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the chat line names the arrow keys and the lock. Click a display, press the arrow keys: it moves 1 pixel per press (Shift: 10); other keys (movement, chat) still work. Click a group's name tab and press an arrow: the whole group moves. Each group tab has a small lock at its right: click it: the tab says \"(locked)\", its displays can no longer be dragged and a display under them can be; click it again to unlock. |cff88ccff/xui unlock|r again: a prompt \"You moved N display(s) or group(s) ... Save the moves, or cancel them\" with |cffffd100Save moves|r and |cffffd100Cancel moves|r; Escape does not close it. Cancel moves: everything jumps back to where it was when you unlocked. Do it again and Save moves: the moves stay after |cff88ccff/reload|r. Then unlock, move something, and |cff88ccff/reload|r without locking: after the reload a prompt says the mover view was left without Save and offers Save moves / Cancel moves. (A game crash cannot keep moves: the game writes saved data only at logout or /reload; after a crash the last saved layout loads.) Arrow keys do nothing in combat." },
    { key = "B179", text = "[B179] (core 0.6.55, Options 0.6.54; G7, Xaya 2026-11-06: \"align / distribute / spacing saved and kept applying\"; a dragged display: \"Arrangement wins\") A static group with three displays: Display tab > Align & Arrange: |cffffd100Horizontal|r = Space horizontally, |cffffd100Vertical|r = Align top. |cffffd100Expect:|r the displays line up along their tops, 8 pixels apart (Gap for Space shows only while a Space choice is picked; change it and the gaps follow). |cff88ccff/xui unlock|r, drag one of them away: it goes back into the line when you let go; arrow-key nudges also snap back. Add a display to the group or make one bigger: it joins the line and the gaps stay. Displays in a nested group, and a display snapped to a game frame, are not moved. Pick |cffffd100None|r for both: dragging now leaves a display where you drop it. Dynamic groups do not show the section." },
    { key = "B179b", text = "[B179b] (core 0.6.55, Options 0.6.54; G9, Xaya 2026-11-06, static group scaling: \"Toggle + ask on resize\") A static group with displays spread wider than 200 pixels: Group tab > Size: |cffffd100Set|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r below Width and Height a tick box |cffffd100Scale items to fit the box|r (not on dynamic groups, not with Auto). Lower Width until the box is narrower than the displays: a question \"|cffffd100Scale the items to fit?|r\" with Yes / No, once (dragging the slider further does not ask again). Yes: the tick box is ticked and everything in the group shrinks so the displays sit inside the box (turn on Border to see it); the box keeps the width you set; the displays' own X / Y and sizes are unchanged (untick and they are back). No: nothing changes; it asks again only after the box was wide enough once more. Items that already fit are never made bigger." },
    { key = "B179c", text = "[B179c] (core 0.6.55, Options 0.6.54; G10, Xaya 2026-11-06: \"Group tab should show options found in weak auras group tab\"; \"Limit (Recommended),Align (Recommended)\"; Align & Arrange: \"Move to Group tab\") A dynamic group with three or more displays of different heights, growing Right: Group tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r |cffffd100Limit (show at most)|r and |cffffd100Align|r beside Sort and Spacing. Limit 2: only the first two (in the group's sort order) show; when one of them goes away, the third appears in its place; 0 shows all again. Align Top: the displays line up along their tops; Bottom: along their bottoms; Center (the default) as before. Grow Down: Align reads Left / Center / Right. A static group: Limit and Align are not shown, and |cffffd100Align & Arrange|r is now on its Group tab (no longer on Display)." },
    { key = "B197", text = "[B197] (Options 0.6.56; Xaya 2026-11-06: \"clicking version number in the bottom right should bring up a standalone pane above XayaUI\"; REQUEST-LOG #86-#88, A9) |cff88ccff/xui|r. Click the version text in the settings window's bottom-left corner. |cffffd100Expect:|r a pane opens over the settings window (in front of it, not behind), title \"XayaUI v<version>\", tabs |cffffd100Patch Notes || Info|r, left list What's New then dated entries, What's New open. Click a dated entry: blue-post style notes with soft-blue *Developers' notes* under their bullets; commands in the accent colour, no stray |cffffd100 or ` marks; a \"||\" in the Chat 0.6.17 note shows as one \"||\". Click |rInfo|cffffd100: Version info, Readme, Help (FAQ), Credits + Acknowledgements; Version info shows the version, date, author and a copyable source link (click it, Ctrl+A, Ctrl+C, paste in chat: the link). Credits: (Options 0.6.64: the sections no longer collapse; see E1z200.) Scroll a long page with the mouse wheel. Drag the pane by its title bar, close it with X, click the version again. |rExpect:|cffffd100 it reopens where you left it. Press |rEsc|cffffd100 once. |rExpect:|cffffd100 the pane closes and the settings window stays open; Esc again closes the settings window. Click the |r?|cffffd100 in the settings window's title bar (left of the collapse arrow). |rExpect:|cffffd100 the pane opens on Info > Help (FAQ). Collapse the settings window: the ? stays beside the arrow. In the pane, the collapse button shrinks it to its title bar and back; its own ? opens Help (FAQ). Settings: no Acknowledgements page any more; no Addon Info page. Change the theme (Settings > Theme) with the pane open: its colours follow. No Lua error. |rNot tested by the automated tests (game only):** the real text heights and wrapping, the \"•\" bullet glyph in the game font, the scroll bars, and Esc order." },
    { key = "B186", text = "[B186] (Options 0.6.55; REQUEST-LOG UI-5 / UI-7, Xaya 2026-11-06: \"Tabs at the highest level should be evenly distributed across the pane, wider, and thicker\"; her answer \"32 px, 14 pt, outlined\") Open |cff88ccff/xui|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r Rules, QoL, Bonus Features and Blizzard UI Reskin share the top row evenly from the window's left edge to its right edge, none overlapping, each clearly taller than before, the names larger and outlined; no tick box on any tab. Click each tab: they stay the same size. Drag the window wider and narrower: they stay even. Screenshot please." },
    { key = "B187", text = "[B187] (Options 0.6.55; UI-6 / UI-7: \"replace the visual of the two column pane boxed display with a clean divider line and remove the frames otherwise\"; her answer \"Borders go, fills stay\") Any tab with a left pane (QoL, Bonus Features, Blizzard UI Reskin, Rules). |cffffd100Expect:|r no border line around the left pane, the right pane or the box under the tabs; the darker fills stay; one thin line between the left and right pane. Drag that line to resize the left pane: it follows. Screenshot please." },
    { key = "B188", text = "[B188] (Options 0.6.55; UI-5 / UI-8: \"appropriately nested\", her answer \"Parent's name + 8 px\") QoL tab: Character Toolkit's parts (Panel, Slot Overlays, Spell Math, Tooltip lines); Bonus Features: Utilities' Calculator and Notepad. |cffffd100Expect:|r each part's tick box starts a little right (8 px) of where its feature's name starts, so the parts read as under it." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-combat-14", { title = "3. Combat displays (14 of 16)", order = 300.14, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "B189", text = "[B189] (Options 0.6.55; UI-5 / UI-8: \"all options that are deselected should grey out\", her answer \"Left pane + their settings\") Untick Release Guard (QoL) and Notepad (Bonus Features > Utilities). |cffffd100Expect:|r their names turn grey in the left pane; open their pages: every setting is greyed and cannot be changed. Tick them again: the names and settings are back to normal. Untick Character Toolkit: its name is grey (its parts leave the list as before)." },
    { key = "B198", text = "[B198] (Options 0.6.55, Chat 0.6.21, QoL 0.7.34, Reskin 0.6.5; UI-5 / UI-7: \"the check box should be enable and disable in the tab itself and then after a reload individual reskin items populate\", her answer \"Right pane + reload prompt\") Blizzard UI Reskin tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r the first row is |cffffd100Overview|r; its page shows |cffffd100Enable Blizzard UI Reskin|r (ticked). Untick it: every reskin goes off at once and a box asks \"reload now ...?\" with Reload / Later. Pick Reload: the tab now lists only Overview. Tick it again, Reload: Character Pane, Chat Panel, Esc Menu and Shopping List are listed again under Overview, each with its own tick box as before. Type |cff88ccff/xui reskin status|r while it is off: the message says Blizzard UI Reskin is off and points to Blizzard UI Reskin > Overview." },
    { key = "B213", text = "[B213] (Options 0.6.63; UI-43 to UI-45, her answers \"28 px, 12 pt, outlined\" and \"2 + call it \"Auto-Generate Rules\"\") Open the Rules tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r the sub-tab row is taller than before, the names larger with an outline; Smart Categories, Enabled, Disabled and Drafts are the same width, side by side from the left; |cffffd100Auto-Generate Rules|r (the old Class/Spec Rule Creator) sits apart at the far right. Click each sub-tab: nothing moves or changes width. Tell us if any name is cut off." },
    { key = "B214", text = "[B214] (Options 0.6.63 and every feature addon; UI-42: \"all should just show a one-sentence description and an enabled/disabled status\") Hover the tick box on the Data Panels row (Bonus Features), then on Esc Menu (Blizzard UI Reskin). |cffffd100Expect:|r three lines each time: the row's name, one sentence, and |cffffd100Enabled|r (green) or |cffffd100Disabled|r (grey); no \"Off: ...\" text. Tick or untick and hover again: the last line follows." },
    { key = "B215", text = "[B215] (Options 0.6.63; UI-46 / UI-48: \"If the item is not enabled no additional fill should exist\") Bonus Features > Data Panels with its tick box off. |cffffd100Expect:|r the page shows one line, \"Shows info panels on your screen: time, gold, frame rate and more.\", and no tab row or empty box under it. Tick it: the General tab appears, the tabs fill the row evenly, a little smaller than the Rules sub-tabs (24 px, 11 pt, outlined). Do the same with Enhanced Tooltips (its tabs: IDs, Item level, ...)." },
    { key = "B216", text = "[B216] (Options 0.6.63; UI-48: \"First try unbordered boxes (darker blocks) and dividing lines\") Open a page with titled groups, for example Blizzard UI Reskin > Chat Panel > Sounds (\"Tab 1: General\", \"Whisper sound overrides\"). |cffffd100Expect:|r each group is a slightly darker block with a thin line along its top and no border around it. Say whether you like it (this one was \"first try\")." },
    { key = "B217", text = "[B217] (Options 0.6.63; UI-48: \"Half width, two per row\") Open a page with text boxes, for example Blizzard UI Reskin > Shopping List (Enchant: Head ...). |cffffd100Expect:|r each one-line text box takes half the row, two side by side, instead of stretching across it. Multi-line boxes are still full width." },
    { key = "B218", text = "[B218] (Options 0.6.63; UI-8 \"Parent's name + 8 px\") In the Blizzard UI Reskin tab, open Chat Panel. |cffffd100Expect:|r its parts (Layout, Look, ...) start 8 px right of where \"Chat Panel\" starts, with no empty gap before their names." },
    { key = "B219", text = "[B219] (Options 0.6.63; UI-49: \"Note theme has to tie into the skin.lua in some way\") Settings > Theme: pick a font other than the game font. |cffffd100Expect:|r the top tabs, the Rules sub-tabs and a page's section tabs all show their names in that font. Change |cffffd100Muted text|r: the name of a switched-off feature in the left pane (e.g. Release Guard, off by default) turns that colour, and so does \"Disabled\" when you hover its tick box. Hover a rule row and open an (i) info box: their highlight and border follow the theme too." },
    { key = "B220", text = "[B220] (Options 0.6.63; UI-50, her answer \"Scale with theme\") Settings > Theme > |cffffd100Text size|r Large, then open the Rules tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r the sub-tabs are taller and their names larger than at Medium (about 32 px instead of 28); the top tabs and a page's section tabs grow the same way. Small makes them smaller. Back to Medium: as in B213." },
    { key = "B221", text = "[B221] (core 0.6.61, Options 0.6.63; UI-50: \"Advanced customization opens up them and more as options, but by default they are not offered\") Settings > Theme. |cffffd100Expect:|r a tick box |cffffd100Advanced customization|r, unticked; no Tab / Selected tab / Tree bars colours and no Class overrides. Tick it: those colours and the Class overrides box appear; change |cffffd100Tab|r and the tabs take that colour. Untick it: they disappear and the tabs go back to the theme's own colour." },
    { key = "B222", text = "[B222] (core 0.6.61, Bonus 0.6.24; UI-53, the trial page: \"isolated to an info icon that opens/closes a description box — try this out for one text-heavy segment and confirm POC before proceeding for all\") Bonus Features > Utilities > Calculator. |cffffd100Expect:|r two short sentences at the top with an (i) icon to their right (no word under the icon); the three long paragraphs are gone. Hover the icon: \"Description\" and one sentence. Click it: a box titled |cffffd100Description|r opens under the summary with the three paragraphs; click again: it closes. |cffffd100Open calculator|r still works. Tell us whether this should be rolled out to every text-heavy page." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-combat-15", { title = "3. Combat displays (15 of 16)", order = 300.15, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "E1z93", text = "[E1z93] (QoL 0.7.39; UI-57, Insivius: \"Release guard doesn't seem to work outside of instances\"; UI-58, Xaya: \"There also should not be an everywhere button\") QoL > Release Guard ticked. |cffffd100Expect:|r Where offers |cffffd100Raids only|r and |cffffd100Raids and dungeons|r, no Everywhere (if Everywhere was picked before, it now reads Raids only). Die outside an instance: no box (as it should be). Die in a raid (or in a dungeon with Raids and dungeons): the black NO RELEASE box over Release Spirit; a click there does nothing; hold Shift and the click releases. Whatever you see in the raid, type |cff88ccff/xui releaseguard|r while still dead and send the two lines it prints." },
    { key = "E1z94", text = "[E1z94] (QoL 0.7.39; UI-62, Xaya: \"Global Cooldown should be GCD / Critical strike effectiveness should be title cased like every other line\") Open the character window with the stat list (and the Stat Calculator's Stats tab). |cffffd100Expect:|r General reads Health, your resource, |cffffd100GCD|r, |cffffd100Movement Speed|r; Offensive ends with |cffffd100Critical Strike Effectiveness|r; every line in title case." },
    { key = "E1z95", text = "[E1z95] (QoL 0.7.39; UI-63 / UI-64, her answer \"Formula + live check\") Stat Calculator > Stats, the |cffffd100GCD|r line (and Offense > Timing). |cffffd100Expect:|r the value is 1.5 / (1 + your haste), never below 0.75 s, even before you cast anything; under it |cffffd100Rule|r \"1.5 s / (1 + haste), never below 0.75 s\" and |cffffd100Live reading|r (cast any spell: the game's own figure). On a Rogue, a Druid in Cat Form, a Brewmaster or Windwalker: |cffffd1001.00 s|r with the rule \"a fixed 1.0 s (energy)\", and Haste's Influences no longer list GCD. When a buff changes it (e.g. Outlaw's Adrenaline Rush), the live reading is orange and says the rule gives a different figure. Type more haste: the GCD shows the lower figure (unless already at 0.75 s)." },
    { key = "B200", text = "[B200] (core 0.6.58 / Options 0.6.59; walkthrough: |cff88ccff/xui dev qa|r > |cffffd100Bar cues (progress bars)|r, Dev Assist 0.7.14, with pre-fill: it makes and removes its own test rule; Xaya 2026-11-06 \"Time to build progress bar cues!\", REQUEST-LOG S8-1 to S8-4) Rules > |cffffd100New Rule|r > |cffffd100Progress Bar|r. On the Trigger tab add |cffffd100Buff / Aura|r with a buff of yours (for example Demon Spikes 203819), State = present. |cffffd100Expect:|r the Cues tab shows \"Cue 1:  Bar 1\" with a |cffffd100Bar Options|r box (Size, Tracks, Fill, Colour, Icon and spark, Background and border), a |cffffd100Text: name, time, stacks / charges|r box and |cffffd100Position|r; no \"Custom cues will run your own Lua\" note. Rules > Smart Categories > |cffffd100Progress Bars|r lists the rule (not Textures). Click the eye icon: a 220 x 22 bar, black background at 20 %, 1 px black border, the buff's icon at the left, its name at the left inside the bar, a time at the right, draining from right to left." },
    { key = "B201", text = "[B201] (core 0.6.58) Out of combat, cast the buff from B200. |cffffd100Expect:|r the bar appears full and drains smoothly toward the left edge until the buff ends, a bright spark on the fill's right edge, the time counting down at the right; the bar hides when the buff ends. Tick |cffffd100Fill up instead of draining|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r next cast, the bar starts empty and fills up. Set |cffffd100Drains toward|r = Right. |cffffd100Expect:|r the fill shrinks toward the right edge and the spark sits on its left edge. No Lua error." },
    { key = "B202", text = "[B202] (core 0.6.58, combat engine) Same rule, on a training dummy in combat; type |cff88ccff/xuiengine|r first. |cffffd100Expect:|r |cff88ccff/xuiengine|r lists the rule as drawn by the engine; in combat the bar keeps draining exactly with the buff (no freeze, no jump on recast), with the buff's icon, name and time. Report \"drains / frozen / empty\" and the |cff88ccff/xuiengine|r line for the rule." },
    { key = "B203", text = "[B203] (core 0.6.58; colour, S8-4 \"Tooltip first\") Make a Bar rule for a spell whose tooltip says \"<school> damage\" (for example a Fire spell such as Immolation Aura 258920, or Sigil of Flame), and one for a buff whose tooltip names no school or dispel type. Open each Bar cue's |cffffd100Colour|r section. |cffffd100Expect:|r the Fire one's \"Now:\" line reads \"Fire, named in the tooltip\" with an orange swatch and the bar is that orange; the other reads \"the fixed blue (no type found yet ...)\" and the bar is blue, unless the buff is a Magic aura, which turns the Magic colour while it is up out of combat (\"Magic, the aura's dispel type\"). Set |cffffd100Colour|r = Fixed colour and pick any colour. |cffffd100Expect:|r the bar takes that colour. Report each \"Now:\" line (English client: on another language the tooltip words are not matched and the bar stays blue)." },
    { key = "B204", text = "[B204] (Options 0.6.59; colour styles, REQUEST-LOG S8-10) Open the Fire Bar cue from B203, |cffffd100Colour|r section. |cffffd100Expect:|r a |cffffd100Colour style|r list (Blizzard default, Neon, Pastel, Muted / Dark, Custom) on the cue itself; Settings > UI Options has no \"Bar Colours\" section. Pick Neon, then Pastel, then Muted / Dark. |cffffd100Expect:|r each time the bar changes at once and keeps its colour family (Neon brighter and stronger, Pastel paler, Muted / Dark duller and darker). Pick Custom. |cffffd100Expect:|r 12 colour pickers (Magic, Curse, Disease, Poison, Bleed, Physical, Holy, Fire, Nature, Frost, Shadow, Arcane) under it; change Fire. |cffffd100Expect:|r the bar takes the picked colour; another Bar cue is not changed. Back to Blizzard default. |cffffd100Expect:|r the original colour. Report whether the preset strengths look right (S8-8: \"Decide after seeing them\")." },
    { key = "B205", text = "[B205] (core 0.6.58; cooldown bar) On a rule with a Cooldown trigger (a spell with a cooldown of 20 s or more), add a Bar cue and set |cffffd100Tracks|r = Spell cooldown / recharge. Cast the spell, then do the same in combat. |cffffd100Expect:|r the bar drains over the cooldown (out of combat and in combat), the time text shows the cooldown's time, the bar is empty once the spell is ready. |cff88ccff/xuiengine|r lists the rule as kept with XayaUI: \"a Bar that times the spell's cooldown / charges (XayaUI draws it; the game drives the bar)\"." },
    { key = "B206", text = "[B206] (core 0.6.58; stacks / charges) A Bar cue with |cffffd100Tracks|r = Stacks on a stacking buff, Maximum 0. |cffffd100Expect:|r the line under Maximum reads \"Full at N\" (the game's maximum stacks) or, if the game gives none, \"The game gives no maximum here: set Maximum.\" Set Maximum to the buff's real maximum. |cffffd100Expect:|r out of combat the bar fills by the stack count (3 of 5 = three fifths); in combat it is drawn by the engine and still follows the stacks. Then |cffffd100Tracks|r = Charges on a spell with charges. |cffffd100Expect:|r the bar shows charges out of the maximum." },
    { key = "B207", text = "[B207] (core 0.6.58; bars in a dynamic group) Put two Bar rules (two different buffs) in one |cffffd100Dynamic Group|r, growth Down. Get both buffs. |cffffd100Expect:|r two bars stacked one under the other, each with its own icon, name, time and colour; when one buff ends the other moves up; the same in combat. No Lua error." },
    { key = "B208", text = "[B208] (core 0.6.58 / Options 0.6.59; group colour style, REQUEST-LOG S8-10 \"Cue sets it, group overrides if forcibly set\") Put two Bar rules in one group. Open the group, |cffffd100Display|r tab, section |cffffd100Every bar: colour style|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Colour style (changes 2 bars)\" and a |cffffd100Force on every bar in this group|r tick box, unticked. Pick Pastel. |cffffd100Expect:|r both bars turn Pastel, and each Bar cue's own Colour style now reads Pastel. Tick |cffffd100Force|r, pick Muted / Dark. |cffffd100Expect:|r the label reads \"(forced on 2 bars)\", both bars turn Muted / Dark; on each Bar cue the Colour style is greyed out with the line \"Colour style: Muted / Dark, forced by the group '<name>'\". Untick Force. |cffffd100Expect:|r both bars go back to Pastel (their own style)." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-combat-16", { title = "3. Combat displays (16 of 16)", order = 300.16, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "B209", text = "[B209] (core 0.6.58 / Options 0.6.59; tooltip words, S8-10) A Bar cue on a spell whose tooltip says \"<school> damage\" (for example Immolation Aura 258920), Colour section. |cffffd100Expect:|r the \"Now:\" line reads \"Fire Damage, named in the tooltip\" with \"Fire Damage\" title-cased in the Fire colour; for a tooltip that writes a dispel type in brackets after the damage words, the bracket follows in its dispel colour, e.g. \"Fire Damage (Magic)\" with \"(Magic)\" in the Magic colour. Report any tooltip you find with a \"(Magic)\" style bracket, since none was confirmed while writing this." },
    { key = "B210", text = "[B210] (core 0.6.58; bar textures, REQUEST-LOG S8-12, S8-13) With at least one addon that shares bar textures installed (ElvUI, WeakAuras or a SharedMedia pack), open a Bar cue, |cffffd100Bar texture|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r Flat, Blizzard and Raid frame once each (no second \"Blizzard\", \"Solid\" or \"Blizzard Raid Bar\"); a run of |cffffd100Blizzard power: ...|r entries (Health, Mana, Rage, Energy, Fury, Insanity, ...); the other addons' textures; \"Texture ID / path...\"; no \"XayaUI: ...\" entries (a roadmap feature, RM-BARFILLS). Pick |cffffd100Blizzard power: Fury|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the bar draws that art, tinted by the bar colour (Colour = Fixed, white, shows it as the game draws it). In ElvUI or WeakAuras' own texture list: no \"XayaUI ...\" entries." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-urgent-1", { title = "4. Urgent items", order = 400.01, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "E1x", text = "[E1x] (Done 2026-11-05: her result \"120 px wider (540 -> 660) ... all ok\"; QoL 0.7.22 builds the wider window on it: E1z40. The probe now refuses while the Character Pane's wider window is on.) (QoL 0.7.12; in-game data for the wider character window) Out of combat, open the character window (C) on its Character tab, then type |cff88ccff/xui debug widthprobe|r (or |cff88ccff/xui debug widthprobe 150|r for 150 px). |cffffd100Expect:|r a chat line \"width probe: on, 120 px wider (... -> ...)\" listing each step as ok. Report: (1) did the right-hand slots and the stats pane move out, the model get wider, the weapons sit centred? (2) with it open, press P and N: do those windows sit beside it without overlapping? (3) fight a training dummy and open / close bags, spellbook and map in combat: any \"width probe: ADDON_ACTION_...\" line or Blizzard's \"Interface action failed because of an AddOn\"? Then |cff88ccff/xui debug widthprobe off|r and |cff88ccff/reload|r. A screenshot of (1) and the chat lines answer whether the Character Reskin can widen the window safely." },
    { key = "E1z6", text = "[E1z6] (QoL 0.7.19: the labels now wrap and the sockets are XayaUI's: E1z11-E1z13; the rest of this step stands.) (QoL 0.7.14; Blizzard UI Reskin > Character Pane, A1-A5, A7) Switch Character Reskin on (Blizzard UI Reskin > Character Pane) (off by default) and open the character window. |cffffd100Expect:|r a flat background in your theme's window colour with a thin border, no portrait or stone frame, a clean model area (no backdrop picture), theme-coloured title and tabs (the selected tab highlighted). Each slot: no slot frame art, one item level at its bottom, coloured by upgrade track (Veteran green, Champion blue, Hero purple, Myth orange, Explorer / Adventurer grey) and brighter for higher upgrade steps (compare a 1/6 and a 6/6 item of one track); an item with no track shows its quality colour. Beside each slot, toward the model: the enchant's name in green, or \"No enchant\" in orange on a slot that takes one; the game's own gem / socket marks stay. The stat list: plain headers with a thin rule, a faint stripe on every other row. If another addon draws item levels on the slots too, note it (two numbers would come from it). Turn each part off in the settings: that part goes back to Blizzard's look. Turn the reskin off: Blizzard's window exactly as before. Open and close the character window in combat: no error, no \"Interface action failed\". |cff88ccff/xui reskin status|r shows the faded count. Screenshot please." },
    { key = "E1z40", text = "[E1z40] (QoL 0.7.22; the wider window, Xaya 2026-11-05 \"character pane still broken\": every enchant label over the model; her width probe of the same day: all ok) Blizzard UI Reskin > Character Pane: Character Reskin on, Clean window off, Item level, Enchants, Gems and Stat list on. |cffffd100Expect:|r new settings \"Wider window (room for the enchant names)\" (ticked), \"Extra width\" (240) and \"Background opacity\" (95%); no \"/xui debug widthprobe\" line. Out of combat open the character window (C) on its Character tab with the stat list open, mouse away from the model. |cffffd100Expect:|r the window is wider than before (|cff88ccff/xui reskin status|r says \"Wider window: on, 240 px wider (540 -> 780)\"); the model is its usual size, whole, centred between the two slot columns; the right column and the stat list moved out; the weapons centred under the model; every enchant, embellishment and gem line sits between its slot and the model, none over the model, none over another line, a slot or a number. Move the mouse over the model. |cffffd100Expect:|r the zoom / rotate buttons show and no line hides or touches them. Click the Reputation tab, then Character again; close and reopen the stat list (the arrow). |cffffd100Expect:|r Blizzard's width on Reputation, the wider window back on Character each time. Press P and N. |cffffd100Expect:|r the spellbook / talents open beside it (say if they overlap or close it). Fight a training dummy: open and close the window, switch its tabs, open bags and the map. |cffffd100Expect:|r no \"Interface action failed because of an AddOn\" and no ADDON_ACTION line; in combat the window may stay at or go back to Blizzard's width and widens again when the fight ends. Set Extra width to 120, then 300. |cffffd100Expect:|r the lines stay clear of the model at both; at 120 some are cut with \"...\" (hover shows the whole line). Untick Wider window. |cffffd100Expect:|r Blizzard's width at once, the lines over the model's sides again (that is what off means). Screenshot please at 240, with the mouse away from the model." },
    { key = "E1z45", text = "[E1z45] (QoL 0.7.23; the window, Xaya 2026-11-05: \"a toggle open/close button on the character menu and remember the last-left state on next open\") Character Toolkit and its Panel on. Open the character window (C) on the Character tab, with the Character Reskin's wider window on and then off. |cffffd100Expect:|r a small |cffffd100Stat Calc|r button in the window's title row, just left of the close X, not over the title text, the item slots or Blizzard's buttons. Click it: the Stat Calculator closes; close and reopen the window: it stays closed; /reload and open the window: still closed. Click Stat Calc: it opens beside the window; close and reopen the window: it opens with it. The button looks selected while the panel is open. No Lua error." },
    { key = "E1z80", text = "[E1z80] (QoL 0.7.31; REQUEST-LOG #72 / #73, \"character pane option should also allow for extra height\", her answer \"either one\") Blizzard UI Reskin > Character Pane: |cffffd100Extra height|r sits right under Extra width, 0-300, at 0. Open the character window. |cffffd100Expect:|r Blizzard's height and spacing. Set 70: the window 70 px taller; the gaps between the slots of both columns equally wider (10 px more each); the model taller; the weapons at the bottom as before, lower; enchant / gem lines may use the extra room. Set it in combat: nothing changes until the fight ends, then it applies. Back to 0: exactly Blizzard's layout. Untick Wider window: Extra height greys and does nothing." },
    { key = "E1z81", text = "[E1z81] (QoL 0.7.31; #70 / #71 / #74, her answers \"2 but customizable and prettified with colors\", \"Show / hide each stat, Order, % / rating / both, Groups and colours\", \"Everything on\") Character Reskin on, open the stats pane. |cffffd100Expect:|r every Character Stats line of the Stat Calculator, under Core Stats, Primary, General, Offensive, Defensive, Secondaries, Tertiaries; each stat's name in its colour; the numbers match the Stat Calculator's Stats tab (no typed numbers); hover a line: the Stat Calculator's hover; scroll with the mouse wheel when the list is longer than the pane. Character Pane > |cffffd100Stat list|r: untick Haste (it leaves the list), set Critical Strike to Rating then Both (\"528 / 22.48%\"), move it Down (after Haste), rename a heading and a stat and change their colours: the pane follows each change. |cffffd100Reset the list|r puts it all back. Untick |cffffd100Full stat list|r: Blizzard's own list. Works the same in combat (numbers the game hides read \"hidden in combat\")." },
    { key = "E2e", text = "[E2e] (core 0.6.51, Options 0.6.50, Chat 0.6.18, Reskin 0.6.4, QoL 0.7.32; S1 #48, the Blizzard UI Reskin tab's switches) Open the Blizzard UI Reskin tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r the tab button itself has a tick box left of its name, |cffffd100All reskins|r (ticked), and the name is not covered by it; the left pane has no All reskins row; the Character Pane, Chat Panel, Esc Menu and Shopping List rows each have their own tick box left of the name, and their pages no longer show that switch. Hover a box: its name and explanation. Tick the Character Pane and Chat Panel boxes (and the others you use), then untick |cffffd100All reskins|r on the tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r at once Blizzard's own chat, character window (open it) and Esc menu (press Esc), and the Shopping List panel goes; the four row boxes stay ticked but greyed. Resize the window and switch tabs: the box stays on the Reskin tab only and never covers its name. /reload: everything stays Blizzard's, no XayaUI chat frame or character-window art. |cff88ccff/xui chat|r and |cff88ccff/xui reskin status|r say All reskins is off. Tick |cffffd100All reskins|r again: the reskins whose boxes are ticked come back without a /reload. No Lua error, no \"Interface action failed\"." },
    { key = "E1z90", text = "[E1z90] (QoL 0.7.33, Dev Assist 0.7.5; REQUEST-LOG #81) XayaUI Dev Assist off, |cff88ccff/reload|r, open the character window, type |cff88ccff/xui debug widthprobe 60|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"there is no debug command \"widthprobe\".\"; the window unchanged. Dev Assist on, |cff88ccff/reload|r, untick the Character Reskin's |cffffd100Wider window|r, open the character window, |cff88ccff/xui debug widthprobe 60|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"width probe: ...\" and the window 60 px wider; |cff88ccff/xui debug widthprobe off|r puts it back. No Lua error." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-a-1", { title = "5. A. Install", order = 500.01, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "A1", text = "[A1] In |cff88ccffWorld of Warcraft\\_retail_\\Interface\\AddOns\\|r, put these folders side by side (the game can stay open; |cff88ccff/reload|r afterwards): |cff88ccffXayaUI|r, |cff88ccffXayaUI_Options|r, |cff88ccffXayaUI_Chat|r, |cff88ccffXayaUI_QoL|r, |cff88ccffXayaUI_Bonus|r, |cff88ccffXayaUI_Reskin|r (and |cff88ccffXayaUI_Media|r if you have one). Each must sit directly in |cff88ccffAddOns|r (not inside another folder)." },
    { key = "A2", text = "[A2] If you had 0.5.x: delete or switch off |cff88ccffAddOns\\XayaUI_CombatEngine|r if it exists." },
    { key = "A3", text = "[A3] Start the game. At the character screen open |cffffd100AddOns|r." },
    { key = "A4", text = "[A4] Log in. |cffffd100Expect:|r no red Lua error. Chat shows no XayaUI error lines." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-b-1", { title = "5. B. Core", order = 501.01, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "B1", text = "[B1] Type |cff88ccff/xui|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the XayaUI window opens (the first time can take a moment: the settings window loads now). Tabs along the top include Chat, QoL, Bonus Features, Import / Export." },
    { key = "B2", text = "[B2] |cff88ccff/xui|r again. |cffffd100Expect:|r the window closes." },
    { key = "B3", text = "[B3] Open the game's Options > AddOns > XayaUI and press |cffffd100Open XayaUI|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the game's options close and the XayaUI window opens." },
    { key = "B4", text = "[B4] Minimap button: left-click. |cffffd100Expect:|r a list with Notes, Settings, Custom data panels, Chat Panel, Chat privacy cover. Right-click: the window opens." },
    { key = "B5", text = "[B5] Make a rule (for example a sound when a spell comes off cooldown) and trigger it. |cffffd100Expect:|r it plays as it did in 0.5.x." },
    { key = "B6", text = "[B6] Your existing rules (if you had 0.5.x): all there, all still working." },
    { key = "B7", text = "[B7] |cff88ccff/xui debug status|r and |cff88ccff/xui unlock|r (twice). |cffffd100Expect:|r a status printout; unlock shows movable displays, the second one locks them." },
    { key = "B8", text = "[B8] A rule with a |cffffd100Boss encounter|r load condition set to \"Only during a boss encounter\": enter a boss fight. |cffffd100Expect:|r the rule loads during the fight (this was broken for some clients before 0.6.0)." },
    { key = "B9", text = "[B9] A rule whose Actions |cffffd100say|r something in /say or /yell inside a dungeon, or in group chat: trigger it. |cffffd100Expect:|r the message is sent (also fixed in 0.6.0)." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-c-1", { title = "5. C. Settings window switched off", order = 502.01, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "C1", text = "[C1] At the character screen switch off |cffffd100XayaUI Options|r only. Log in, type |cff88ccff/xui|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r one line saying the settings window is switched off and how to turn it on. Rules still work. No Lua error." },
    { key = "C2", text = "[C2] Switch XayaUI Options back on." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-d-1", { title = "5. D. XayaUI Chat (1 of 3)", order = 503.01, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "D1", text = "[D1] With Chat on: |cffffd100Expect|r the restyled chat panel as before; |cff88ccff/xui chat|r prints its commands; |cff88ccff/xui chat settings|r opens Blizzard UI Reskin > Chat Panel (Chat 0.6.13; it was Chat > Chat Panel)." },
    { key = "D1b", text = "[D1b] In the window: Blizzard UI Reskin > Chat Panel (Chat 0.6.13). |cffffd100Expect:|r the Chat Panel page shows Enable Chat Panel and the theme switch; under Chat Panel in the left pane: Layout, Appearance, Chat Bar, Fade and hide, Filters, History, Sounds, Privacy. Click Appearance: tabs Background and border || Chat text || Tabs || Input line. Click Privacy: tabs Look || Button || Area and behavior. Every setting you had before is still there and keeps its value." },
    { key = "D3", text = "[D3] Click the input area under the panel. |cffffd100Expect:|r the chat edit box opens. Collapse the panel while typing. |cffffd100Expect:|r the edit box closes." },
    { key = "D4", text = "[D4] |cff88ccff/xui privacy|r twice. |cffffd100Expect:|r the cover hides the chat, then shows it again." },
    { key = "D4e", text = "[D4e] (0.6.5) |cff88ccff/xui debug chatprobe|r inside a dungeon or in combat. |cffffd100Expect:|r no \"chat probe failed ... Probe.lua:229 ... secret boolean\" line; it prints \"chat probe: N lines kept\"." },
    { key = "D4h", text = "[D4h] (Chat 0.6.8) Blizzard UI Reskin > Chat Panel > Text inset: set it to its lowest (2). |cffffd100Expect:|r a small gap (2 px) between the panel's left edge and the chat text; the slider does not go below 2. If the text still touches the edge, type |cff88ccff/xui chat indent|r and send the line it prints." },
    { key = "D4j", text = "[D4j] (Chat 0.6.10) Blizzard UI Reskin > Chat Panel > Sounds > Whisper sound overrides: + Add a sender, type a friend's character name, pick a sound. Have them whisper you. |cffffd100Expect:|r that sound, not the tab sound. Add a Battle.net friend by BattleTag (or the part before #) with another sound; have them whisper you on Battle.net. |cffffd100Expect:|r that sound. Tick Play a sound for Battle.net favorites with a third sound; a favorite who is not on the list whispers you. |cffffd100Expect:|r the favorites sound. Someone not listed and not a favorite. |cffffd100Expect:|r the tab sound as before. In a Mythic+ or a boss fight, note whether the override still plays (during chat lockdown it falls back to the tab sound by design)." },
    { key = "D4l", text = "[D4l] (Chat 0.6.12) Options > Social > New Whispers: New Tab. |cff88ccff/reload|r. Have someone whisper you, or whisper someone. |cffffd100Expect:|r a tab named after them appears in the tab row (or in the list at the row's end). If it does not: type |cff88ccff/console scriptErrors 1|r, have them whisper you again, then type |cff88ccff/xui chat whispers|r and send every line it prints and any Lua error." },
    { key = "D5", text = "[D5] Switch |cffffd100XayaUI Chat|r off, /reload (or relog). |cffffd100Expect:|r Blizzard's normal chat; the Chat Panel page is gone from the Blizzard UI Reskin tab; the minimap list has no Chat rows; |cff88ccff/xui chat|r says XayaUI Chat is switched off. No Lua error. Switch it back on." },
    { key = "D6", text = "[D6] (Chat 0.6.14, rule V14 \"off costs nothing\") Blizzard UI Reskin > Chat Panel: untick |cffffd100Enable Chat Panel|r, then |cff88ccff/reload|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r Blizzard's own chat, no Chat Bar, no eye (privacy) button, no history button. Stand in a capital city for two minutes with Trade / General busy (or a busy custom channel). Open the game's AddOns list (Esc > AddOns) and look at |cffffd100XayaUI Chat|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r its CPU stays at or near 0 and its memory does not grow while the channel scrolls. |cff88ccff/xui chat|r prints \"Chat Panel: OFF\"; |cff88ccff/xui|r still prints its help. Press Enter, type, Escape a few times. |cffffd100Expect:|r no Lua error." },
    { key = "D7", text = "[D7] (Chat 0.6.14) Same session, no |cff88ccff/reload|r: tick |cffffd100Enable Chat Panel|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the Chat Panel appears at once with its Chat Bar (clock and frame rate change every second) and the eye button. Untick it again. |cffffd100Expect:|r Blizzard's chat is back at once, exactly where it was; press Enter, type, Escape: no Lua error; within a few seconds XayaUI Chat's CPU in the AddOns list is back at or near 0." },
    { key = "D8", text = "[D8] (Chat 0.6.14) Chat Panel on. Fade and hide: tick |cffffd100Fade the chat when it is idle|r (it is off by default). |cffffd100Expect:|r after 10 s with no mouse over the chat, nothing typed and no new message, the chat fades out; moving the mouse over it, typing, or a new message (with \"A new message brings the chat back\" on) brings it back, as before. Untick it. |cffffd100Expect:|r the chat is fully visible at once and stays so." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-d-2", { title = "5. D. XayaUI Chat (2 of 3)", order = 503.02, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "D9", text = "[D9] (Chat 0.6.14) Each switch works at once, no |cff88ccff/reload|r: Chat Bar: untick |cffffd100Show the Chat Bar|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the bar is gone; tick it: back, clock running. History: untick |cffffd100Keep recent messages|r, say something, open the history window. |cffffd100Expect:|r the new line is not there; tick it again, say something: it is there. Untick |cffffd100Keep console lines in a Console tab|r, type |cff88ccff/xui|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r no new Console lines; tick it, |cff88ccff/xui|r: they appear (after Refresh). Sounds: give a tab a sound, untick |cffffd100Play tab sounds|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r no tab sound on a message; a whisper override still plays while its own switch is on. Filters: untick |cffffd100Hide repeated messages|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r a message repeated by the same player shows twice; untick |cffffd100Make web addresses clickable|r: a web address stays plain text. Privacy > Button: untick |cffffd100Show the toggle button beside the chat|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the eye button is gone at once; tick it: back. Tick |cffffd100Cover fades away while the mouse is over it|r, cover the chat. |cffffd100Expect:|r the cover fades under the mouse; untick it: the cover stays." },
    { key = "D10", text = "[D10] (Chat 0.6.14) Privacy: tick |cffffd100Cover the chat at every login|r, |cff88ccff/reload|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the chat is covered when the loading screen ends (this moved from a timer on the loading screen to the moment the settings load)." },
    { key = "D12", text = "[D12] (Chat 0.6.17; Xaya 2026-11-06: fix the chat history window's \"||\" \"in this update\") Type |cff88ccff/xui help|r and |cff88ccff/xui debug|r (with XayaUI's messages set to chat for help). Open the chat history window, Console tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r the lines read |cff88ccff/xui cursor [highlight||trail]|r, |cff88ccff/xui stats [on||off||options||status]|r, |cff88ccff/xui debug widthprobe [px||off]|r with every |cff88ccff|||r and every letter (not |cff88ccff[highlighttrail]|r or |cff88ccffstatusidthprobe|r). Type |cff88ccffon||off|r in the window's Search box. |cffffd100Expect:|r the stats line stays listed. Select a line with a |cff88ccff|||r and copy it (Ctrl+C), paste it into the chat box without sending. |cffffd100Expect:|r one |cff88ccff|||r (report it if it pastes as |cff88ccff|||||r: that part is not known outside the game). No Lua error." },
    { key = "D13", text = "[D13] (Chat 0.6.19; REQUEST-LOG O-81) Type |cff88ccff/xui chat|r. Open the chat history window, Console tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r the line reads |cff88ccff/xui chat on||off||reset||move||history||wrap||indent||whispers||settings|r with every letter (0.6.18 showed |cff88ccffon||off||eset|r). Say in chat a line with a |cff88ccff|||r before r or n, for example |cff88ccffa||rb|r and |cff88ccffx||ny|r, then open the history on that chat tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r |cff88ccffa||rb|r and |cff88ccffx||ny|r as typed (if not, report what shows: how the game sends a typed |cff88ccff|||r is not known outside the game). No Lua error." },
    { key = "D14", text = "[D14] (Chat 0.6.20, Dev Assist 0.7.5; REQUEST-LOG #81) XayaUI Dev Assist off, |cff88ccff/reload|r. |cff88ccff/xui chat|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Chat Panel: ON. /xui chat on||off||reset||move||history||settings\" (no wrap, indent, whispers). |cff88ccff/xui chat whispers|r: the same status, no whisper report. Dev Assist on, |cff88ccff/reload|r, whisper someone. |cff88ccff/xui chat|r: the list adds wrap||indent||whispers. |cff88ccff/xui chat whispers|r: |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Chat whispers: the game's setting ...\" and \"1 sent\"; |cff88ccff/xui chat wrap|r and |cff88ccff/xui chat indent|r: their measurement lines. No Lua error." },
    { key = "D19", text = "[D19] (Chat 0.6.20; REQUEST-LOG UI-2 / UI-4, Xaya 2026-11-06: \"text differences between general / combat log / user created panes should not exist. make sure all align properly\") Chat Panel on, tab row shown. Select General, then Combat Log, then a tab you created (for example Trade), then a whisper tab (Options > Social > New Whispers: New Tab, whisper someone). |cffffd100Expect:|r on every selection, every tab's name sits on one line, at the same height; only the colour of the selected tab differs (the Chat Panel's Selected tab text color, or the theme's). The whisper tab's name stays left of centre, beside its icon. Screenshot please. If General (or any tab) still sits lower: type |cff88ccff/xui debug chatprobe|r, |cff88ccff/reload|r, and send the saved file (its \"ChatFrame1Tab\" part lists where the name is anchored)." },
    { key = "D15", text = "[D15] (Chat 0.6.22; REQUEST-LOG UI-20, Xaya 2026-11-06: \"pressing the collapse button should collapse the chat data bar down, not pull the chat up to it\") Chat Panel > Chat Bar: Place the bar = Above the chat. Click the arrow at the bar's left end. |cffffd100Expect:|r the chat disappears and the bar drops down to where the chat's bottom edge was (the bottom of the whole block stays where it was); the arrow now points up. Click it again: the chat comes back above the bar's place and the bar returns to the top; the arrow points down. With the bar below the chat nothing changes from before (the bar stays at the bottom). Screenshot please." },
    { key = "D17", text = "[D17] (Chat 0.6.24; REQUEST-LOG UI-11, Xaya 2026-11-06: \"mouse hover over should also allow for chat to reappear if this option is selected\"; her answer \"Its own tick box\") Chat Panel > Fade and hide: tick |cffffd100Fade the chat when it is idle|r, Seconds before it fades 5. |cffffd100Expect:|r under \"A new message brings the chat back\" a new tick box, |cffffd100The mouse over the chat brings it back|r, ticked. Wait for the chat to fade, move the mouse over it: it comes back. Untick the new box, wait for the fade, move the mouse over it: it stays faded; press Enter to type: it comes back." },
    { key = "D18", text = "[D18] (Chat 0.6.25; REQUEST-LOG UI-12 / UI-17, Xaya 2026-11-06: \"allow a modifier selector (alt, ctrl. fn(?))\"; her answer \"detect available modifiers based on available keybinds not already assigned; also allow user to record and save their own keybind\") Chat Panel > Filters, Quick ignore. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Click a player's name in chat to ignore them\", a |cffffd100Click|r list and a |cffffd100Record your own|r button, and a line \"Now: Ctrl + right-click on a player's name.\" Open the list: right-clicks with Alt, Ctrl, Shift (Cmd too on a Mac) and their pairs, minus any the game has a key binding for (bind Alt + right-click in the game's Key Bindings first to see it leave the list). Pick Shift + right-click; right-click a name holding Ctrl: nothing; holding Shift: \"Ignoring <name> (Shift + right-click)\". Press Record your own, click the box without a key: it asks again; hold Alt and middle-click it: saved, the line says Alt + middle-click. Remove the test player from your Ignore list afterwards." },
    { key = "D21", text = "[D21] (Dev Assist 0.7.9; REQUEST-LOG A14 CHATREV-6, Xaya 2026-11-06: \"ensure qa has a handler that can automatically generate an answer\", \"For every issue here\", \"Pre-fill, I confirm\") |cff88ccff/xui dev qa|r. Run the four chat walkthroughs (#210, #229 items 1-4, #250, #296), pressing |cffffd100Do it for me|r where offered. |cffffd100Expect:|r after each check, a button |cffffd100Accept: Pass|r or |cffffd100Accept: Fail|r shows the addon's own verdict; nothing is recorded until you click it (or Pass / Fail / Skip); Accept puts the addon's reading in the note unless you typed one; #296's last step is a question and has no Accept; each walkthrough's last step puts your chat back as it was. Other walkthroughs (no pre-fill) still say \"you still decide\" and have no Accept." },
    { key = "D24", text = "[D24] (Chat 0.6.31, Dev Assist 0.7.13; REQUEST-LOG A14 CHATREV-10 / CHATREV-11, Xaya 2026-11-07: \"creating new whisper tabs by sending a new message don't automatically shift to a new whisper window from general tab\"; \"why is chat functionality still not placed correctly in its appropriate location?\", built from her #246 words) |cff88ccff/xui dev qa|r: run |cffffd100Chat: a whisper tab you start opens|r and |cffffd100Chat: settings laid out as asked in #246|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r with New Whispers = Both, whispering someone new from General opens their tab and switches to it; replying to someone who already has a tab keeps you on General. (since Chat 0.6.33 the parts are split over two pages: see D25); Timestamps changes the game's Chat Timestamps setting (the walkthrough puts yours back). Also run |cffffd100Chat: exact X / Y position from the mover (#430)|r: in |cff88ccff/xui chat move|r, a click on the blue box (not a drag) opens \"Chat position\" with X and Y; typing a number and Enter moves the chat there; each arrow moves 1 pixel, 10 with Shift; it closes with the mover. Also run |cffffd100Chat: every tab at one height (CHATREV-12)|r: General and Combat Log sit on the same line as Guild, Self and whisper tabs, also after a new whisper tab opens." },
    { key = "D25", text = "[D25] (Chat 0.6.33, Dev Assist 0.7.25; REQUEST-LOG UI-18 / UI-19 / UI-21, Xaya 2026-11-06: purely visual = Blizzard UI Reskin > Chat Panel, anything that changes how chat behaves = QoL > Improved Chat, two independent switches, her item list \"Yes, as listed\") |cff88ccff/xui dev qa|r: run |cffffd100Chat: settings split, look vs behaviour|r and |cffffd100Chat: Chat Panel and Improved Chat switch on and off apart|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r Blizzard UI Reskin > Chat Panel shows only General (Font options, Color + display options), Chat Tabs and Layout. QoL > |cffffd100Improved Chat|r has its own tick box on its row, a note that it likely displays better with a chat reskin and works with other chat reskins, and General (Scroll and fade options, Chat history, Timestamp, copying, and links), Chat Data Panel, Filters, Sounds, Privacy. With the Chat Panel off and Improved Chat on: Blizzard's own chat where the game puts it, the Chat Data Panel right under it, the privacy eye beside it, repeated messages still hidden. With the Chat Panel on and Improved Chat off: the restyled chat with no Chat Data Panel, collapse arrow, slow-scrolling bar, history button or privacy eye. Right-click a data block: QoL > Improved Chat > Chat Data Panel opens." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-d-3", { title = "5. D. XayaUI Chat (3 of 3)", order = 503.03, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "D27", text = "[D27] (Chat 0.6.35, core 0.6.68, Dev Assist 0.7.27; REQUEST-LOG UI-3 / UI-17 / A16 CR-4, CR-6, CR-7) |cff88ccff/xui dev qa|r: run |cffffd100Chat: the chat sidebar|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r QoL > Improved Chat > |cffffd100Sidebar|r is on by default, on the left of the chat, as tall as it, with a dark background tinted in your class colour; top to bottom: privacy eye, Blizzard's chat menu and channel buttons (voice buttons only in a voice channel), history, Chat windows, Newest message. The chat keeps its size; near the screen's left edge the chat moves in so the strip stays on screen. On mouseover: hidden until the mouse is over the chat or the strip; Fade with the chat: fades with it; Hide in combat: gone in combat, back after; the buttons always do the same as the strip. Side Right / Top / Bottom move it; with the Chat Data Panel on the left, the strip sits outside it. Width of the whole chat 600: chat + strip = 600. Settings > Minimap Button > |cffffd100Show it in|r: Chat sidebar puts XayaUI's button in the strip and off the minimap; with the minimap button turned off it is in the strip anyway. Sidebar off: the eye is back beside the chat, Blizzard's buttons back in their own strip, the history button back at the tab row's end." },
    { key = "D28", text = "[D28] (Chat 0.6.36, Dev Assist 0.7.28; REQUEST-LOG O-143, Xaya 2026-11-07: \"weird chat appearance when chat fades -- the sidebar icons should also be fading\") |cff88ccff/xui dev qa|r: run |cffffd100Chat: every icon fades with the chat|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r with Fade the chat when it is idle on, after the chat fades the collapse chevron, the privacy eye and the sidebar with all its buttons are gone too (nothing stays at full strength). Moving the mouse over the chat, the sidebar or the eye brings everything back together." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-e-1", { title = "5. E. XayaUI QoL (1 of 4)", order = 504.01, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "E1c", text = "[E1c] Type |cff88ccff/xui cursor|r, then |cff88ccff/xui cursor trail|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the window opens on the Cursor page, then on Gradient Cursor Trail (no \"did not respond\" line)." },
    { key = "E1d2", text = "[E1d2] Haste is the best in-game test of diminishing returns: at 1,287 haste rating = 29.25% (44.0 rating per 1%), the first threshold should sit near 1,320 rating (30%). |cffffd100Expect:|r Haste shows \"Next threshold\" about 33 rating away. If it says the converter shows none, the game's converter does not apply diminishing returns; then gear past 1,320 haste rating should show the orange \"converter disagrees\" line." },
    { key = "E1e", text = "[E1e] Hover Critical Strike in Blizzard's stat list. |cffffd100Expect:|r a \"XayaUI Character Toolkit\" block under Blizzard's text. Hover Mastery in the panel. |cffffd100Expect:|r the threshold list and your mastery factor." },
    { key = "E1e2", text = "[E1e2] (Replaced in QoL 0.7.14 by E1z2-E1z4: skip.) Panel tabs: click Stats, Gear, What If, Spells (and its All, Offense and Defense buttons; QoL 0.7.7). |cffffd100Expect:|r each fills in without an error. Stats > Character: your mastery text (\"Increases Armor by ..% of your Agility\" for Vengeance). Stats > Leech: \"Other sources\" equals your whole Leech if you have no leech rating. Gear: item levels match your gear; Summary's crit \"character\" figure matches Blizzard's crit tooltip rating (528 in Xaya's screenshot)." },
    { key = "E1f", text = "[E1f] (Replaced in QoL 0.7.14 by E1z2 (Global cooldown on the Stats map) and E1z4: skip.) Cast any spell out of combat. |cffffd100Expect:|r Spells > Offense > Global Cooldown shows the GCD (about what your GCD display shows). Spell Math: switch it on, add Fracture (or any damage spell). |cffffd100Expect:|r on the Spells tab, its description numbers with a percent of attack power." },
    { key = "E1j", text = "[E1j] (QoL 0.7.0) Pull a training dummy and look at the panel in combat. |cffffd100Expect:|r no Lua error; values the game hides show \"hidden in combat\" (not 0, not a number) and fill in again after combat. Global Cooldown: note whether it updates in combat or says hidden in combat, and report which (the game decides; both are handled)." },
    { key = "E1l2", text = "[E1l2] (QoL 0.7.5) Stats > Character. |cffffd100Expect:|r no \"Mythic+ rating\" line or cell anywhere in the Character Toolkit; the other lines (item level, movement, mastery) are still there and nothing is left blank where it was. Open the Group Finder's Mythic+ tab, then the character window: no Lua error." },
    { key = "E1o", text = "[E1o] (QoL 0.7.1, core 0.6.23) Shift-click with Blizzard's deprecation fallbacks off. First note your setting: |cff88ccff/dump GetCVar(\"loadDeprecationFallbacks\")|r. Type |cff88ccff/console loadDeprecationFallbacks 0|r, then |cff88ccff/reload|r. QoL > Character Toolkit on, open the character window, What If tab, click into the Item box, shift-click an item from your bags. |cffffd100Expect:|r the item link appears in the box (as in E1k) and no Lua error. Then set the setting back to the value you noted (|cff88ccff/console loadDeprecationFallbacks 1|r if it was 1) and |cff88ccff/reload|r. (That a /reload re-reads this setting is an inference: Blizzard's fallback files check it when they load.)" },
    { key = "E1q", text = "[E1q] (QoL 0.7.3) Open the character window with the toolkit on. |cffffd100Expect:|r the panel's title reads \"Stat Calculator\" (the settings page is still QoL > Character Toolkit)." },
    { key = "E1s", text = "[E1s] (QoL 0.7.6) With Slot overlays on and the Enchant Slots tab never touched: open the character window. |cffffd100Expect:|r E? (orange) or E (green) on head, shoulders, chest, legs, feet, both rings and main hand only; nothing on neck, back, wrists, waist, hands, trinkets, shirt or tabard; on the off hand only when it holds a weapon (not a shield or off-hand frill). Untick Head: |cffffd100Expect:|r head's mark goes, the others stay, and after |cff88ccff/reload|r Head is still unticked. Click |cffffd100This expansion's slots|r: |cffffd100Expect:|r Head is ticked again. Note in the QA notes any slot that takes an enchant this expansion but is not checked, or the reverse." },
    { key = "E1r", text = "[E1r] (Replaced in QoL 0.7.14 by E1z3: skip.) (QoL 0.7.4) What If: shift-click a trinket. |cffffd100Expect:|r under Compare an item, its stat changes (e.g. -21 Agility, +63 Leech for Lightspire Core against your lower trinket), also with Show set to the short view; both equipped trinkets listed, the replaced one marked Replacing; the rating boxes and the Agility box above filled with those changes. Click the other trinket. |cffffd100Expect:|r the numbers and boxes change to that comparison. Type your own amount in one box, then empty the item box. |cffffd100Expect:|r the filled amounts go away, yours stays. Type 100 in the Agility box. |cffffd100Expect:|r +100 attack power (or what the game gives) next to it." },
    { key = "E1t", text = "[E1t] (Replaced in QoL 0.7.14 by E1z2-E1z4: skip.) (QoL 0.7.7) Character Toolkit panel. |cffffd100Expect:|r the tabs read Stats || Gear || What If || Spells (no Defense or Offense tab; no Sheet since QoL 0.7.13). Open Spells. |cffffd100Expect:|r three buttons All || Offense || Defense above the list. With Spell Math off: All shows the \"Spell Math is off\" note; Offense also shows Power, Weapons, Timing and resources; Defense also shows Health and armor, Avoidance, Damage taken (the same lines the old tabs had). Turn Spell Math on (QoL > Character Toolkit > Spell Math). |cffffd100Expect:|r on All, your spec's spells with numbers in their description (Vengeance: Immolation Aura, Fel Devastation, Chaos Nova, Fracture and others) without adding any by hand; a grey \"N without numbers\" line. A spell's numbers do not include a radius in yards, a duration in seconds or a target count. Click Offense: the damage spells (Immolation Aura, Fel Devastation, Fracture); no spell whose text only adds armor. Click Defense: spells whose text heals, absorbs or adds armor (Fel Devastation if its text mentions healing), plus the Defense lines; a spell whose only numbers are percents or seconds (Demon Spikes, if that is its text) is counted under \"without numbers\" instead. Hover a listed spell. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"From your spellbook\", attack power named for Agility, and the filter it was put in. Tick List spells without numbers. |cffffd100Expect:|r Demon Spikes and other spells without numbers listed, each saying \"none in the description\". Report any spell under the wrong filter, and how long the list takes to fill after a /reload (spells whose text the game has not sent show as \"still loading\")." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-e-2", { title = "5. E. XayaUI QoL (2 of 4)", order = 504.02, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "E1u", text = "[E1u] (Replaced in QoL 0.7.14 by E1z2 (the Agility card's » Armor line): skip.) (QoL 0.7.8) Vengeance, out of combat, no temporary armor buffs (no Demon Spikes or Metamorphosis up). Stats > Agility: \"Armor from it\" = your Agility x the percent in your mastery text (88.7% in your screenshot). Spells > Defense > Armor: \"From Agility\" shows the same number. What If: type 100 in the Agility box. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Armor from it\" about +89 and a small damage-reduction gain. Shift-click an item with more Agility than the one it replaces. |cffffd100Expect:|r the Armor line reads \"+N (item +a, Agility +b)\" with b = the Agility change x the mastery percent. To check the link itself: note your armor in Blizzard's character window, equip an item whose only difference is Agility (or note Agility and armor before and after any swap), and report whether the armor changed by the item's armor plus b. Also report Blizzard's armor tooltip and the panel's Base / From buffs and talents lines, so we can see which UnitArmor figure holds the armor from Agility." },
    { key = "E1v", text = "[E1v] (QoL 0.7.14: a plain click on an icon now picks it for the comparison, E1z3; shift-click still links it.) (QoL 0.7.9) Character Toolkit > Gear. |cffffd100Expect:|r an Equipped section first: one icon per equipped item (no shirt or tabard), in the character window's slot order, two rows for a full set; under each, its item level matching the character window, coloured like the item's name (purple for epic). Hover an icon. |cffffd100Expect:|r the same tooltip the character window's slot shows. Shift-click one with a chat box open. |cffffd100Expect:|r the item's link in chat. Switch to another tab and back: the icons are gone and come back; no Lua error." },
    { key = "E1y", text = "[E1y] (QoL 0.7.13) Gradient Cursor Trail on, shape |cffffd100Smooth line|r, your usual size. Swing the mouse around fast for a few seconds, in and out of combat. |cffffd100Expect:|r the line is one smooth band (no separate dots, no gaps along it), it fades out at the length you set, and it disappears while you turn the camera with the right mouse button. Compare the feel of the cursor with the trail on and off: note in the QA notes whether the trail on still makes the cursor feel slower." },
    { key = "E1z", text = "[E1z] (QoL 0.7.14) Open the character window with the Stat Calculator on. |cffffd100Expect:|r no Sheet tab; the panel opens on Stats (also if it was left on the Sheet before). No Lua error." },
    { key = "E1z3", text = "[E1z3] (QoL 0.7.14; Stat Calculator > Gear, the comparison) Put a spare ring, a spare trinket and a spare helm in your bags. Gear tab: click your helm's icon. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Compare: Head\" lists the helms in your bags (best item level first; not the rings); the helm's icon is marked under its item level. Click one. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Side by side\": item level, primary stat, Stamina, armor and each rating, Equipped || that item || Change, green for better and orange for worse; then \"What it changes\": only the cards and lines that change (e.g. crit -> parry, Agility -> attack power and armor, Stamina -> health), with \"now -> then\". Click your first ring's icon, then a bag ring. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Replacing / Replace instead\" rows for both rings; click the other: the table follows. Drag a bag trinket onto a trinket icon. |cffffd100Expect:|r compared at once, the cursor empty. Shift-click an item from chat with the Gear tab shown. |cffffd100Expect:|r it goes into the box and is compared. The Stats tab's own boxes are not changed by any of this. In combat: the comparison says \"hidden in combat\" for ratings, no error." },
    { key = "E1z4", text = "[E1z4] (QoL 0.7.14; Stat Calculator > Spells, #377) With Spell Math off (QoL > Character Toolkit > Spell Math), open Ability Scaling (the Spells tab until QoL 0.7.28). |cffffd100Expect:|r one button, \"Configure spell data\"; click it: Spell Math turns on and your spells are listed under \"Active spells\", with a \"Refresh spell data\" button on top. Hover a spell's name. |cffffd100Expect:|r the game's own spell tooltip, then the toolkit's lines under it. |cffffd100Expect:|r spells your picked talents change show \"Changed by talents: ...\" (talents whose text names the spell). A folded \"+ Inactive: talents not picked\" section at the bottom; click it: castable talents you have not picked, each with its numbers. Offense / Defense filters list spells only (the stat sections are on Stats now). Change a talent, click Refresh spell data: the lists follow." },
    { key = "E1z5", text = "[E1z5] (QoL 0.7.40: the header above the tabs is now the two item levels, no name, spec or class: E1z198; the size part below still applies.) (QoL 0.7.14; panel header and size, #383, #381) |cffffd100Expect:|r above the tabs: your name, your spec and class in your class colour, and your equipped item level (overall in brackets) on the right; no role, no movement speed. Drag the panel's bottom-right corner. |cffffd100Expect:|r the panel resizes (it stops at its limits), the content reflows to the new width without overlaps, and the size is kept after closing and reopening the character window and after /reload. QoL > Character Toolkit > Panel > Layout: \"Reset size\" puts it back. Settings: the Panel's tabs are Layout || Your numbers || Tooltips." },
    { key = "E1z9", text = "[E1z9] (QoL 0.7.17, core 0.6.46; the trail follows the UI theme) QoL > Cursor > Gradient Cursor Trail, switch it on, Colors tab, open |cffffd100Gradient|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r after Frost, \"Match the UI theme\", then \"Custom (build your own)\". Set the theme to |cffffd100XUI default (purple)|r (Settings > UI Options > Theme), then pick |cffffd100Match the UI theme|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the preview strip and the trail run light purple (at the cursor), purple, dark purple. Keep the settings window open and pick Settings > UI Options > Theme > |cffffd100Cursor trail: Ocean|r, then move the mouse. |cffffd100Expect:|r the trail turns pale cyan, blue, navy at once (no trail setting touched) and looks the same as picking Ocean in the Gradient list; back on the trail page the preview shows the Ocean strip. Pick Class colors as the theme. |cffffd100Expect:|r the trail takes your class color, light to dark. Pick |cffffd100Fel|r in the Gradient list, then change the theme again. |cffffd100Expect:|r the trail stays Fel. Switch the trail off and change the theme a few times. |cffffd100Expect:|r nothing is drawn, no Lua error. Put your trail and theme back as they were." },
    { key = "E1z10", text = "[E1z10] (QoL 0.7.17; the highlight takes the theme's accent) QoL > Cursor > Cursor Highlight, switch it on, |cffffd100Color and Size|r tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r a tick box \"Use the UI theme's accent\" above Color, unticked; the shape in your own color. Tick it. |cffffd100Expect:|r the shape takes the theme's accent (purple with the XUI default, your class color with Class colors), the Color button is greyed out, the Opacity slider still works. Pick Settings > UI Options > Theme > |cffffd100Cursor trail: Fire|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the shape turns orange at once. Behavior tab: tick |cffffd100Only show in combat|r (out of combat the shape hides), then change the theme again. |cffffd100Expect:|r the shape stays hidden. Untick Only show in combat, untick the accent option. |cffffd100Expect:|r the shape is back in the color you had picked. No Lua error. Put your highlight and theme back as they were." },
    { key = "E1z42", text = "[E1z42] (QoL 0.7.22; one item level per slot, her screenshot: a large purple item level over each slot plus XayaUI's) With the other character-sheet addon as it is, open the character window and type |cff88ccff/xui reskin status|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Text on the slots that is not XayaUI's (n): Head 334 (frame name) ...\" and \"XayaUI's item level is hidden on n slot(s) where that text shows the same number\"; each slot shows ONE number (the other addon's). Please send that chat line (the frame names say which addon it is). To have XayaUI's track-coloured number instead: turn the other addon's own item-level option off (in its settings; /reload if it asks). |cffffd100Expect:|r XayaUI's number back on every slot, still one per slot. Or untick \"Item level on each slot\" here. |cffffd100Expect:|r only the other addon's." },
    { key = "E1z46", text = "[E1z46] (QoL 0.7.23; on its own, Xaya: \"its own open button on the minimap ... openable as its own standalone window without opening the character sheet\") Character window closed. Click the XayaUI minimap button. |cffffd100Expect:|r a |cffffd100Stat Calculator|r row in its list (Minimap Button settings > Buttons in the list has it too); click it: the Stat Calculator opens on its own, the character window stays closed. Drag it somewhere, close it with the row, open it with |cff88ccff/xui stats|r: it comes back where you left it. Open the character window: the panel moves beside it; close the window: the panel stays open at its own place. Switch the Character Toolkit (or its Panel) off: the row leaves the list and the Stat Calc button is gone." },
    { key = "E1z49", text = "[E1z49] (QoL 0.7.23; Stat Weights, Xaya: \"a collapsible pane below the character stats that shows how all stats affect one another\") |cffffd100Expect:|r under Character Stats, |cffffd100Stat Weights|r: Stat || Rating (P / %) || PPP || DR Threshold || T/L Rating, one row per stat (your primary stat, Stamina, the four secondaries, the three tertiaries), and \"Influences: ...\" under each row (its own column once the panel is about 580 wide or more). Haste: \"Influences: GCD (-0.xx s), Attack Speed (-0.xx s)\"; hover the row: \"Haste decreases Global cooldown by 0.xx s (estimate)\". A stat past a diminishing-return threshold shows a second \"DR: N / 1%\" line under PPP and an L above 0. Click the header: it folds, and stays folded after /reload. Compare T and L against your own sheet; tell us any column you want named differently." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-e-3", { title = "5. E. XayaUI QoL (3 of 4)", order = 504.03, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "E1z50", text = "[E1z50] (QoL 0.7.24; the Spells filter, Xaya 2026-11-05: \"a filter icon on the right hand side with \"none\" by default (therefore showing all)\"; options \"none\" (show all), \"offense,\" \"defense,\" \"utility\"\") Stat Calculator > Ability Scaling (the Spells tab until QoL 0.7.28), Spell Math on. |cffffd100Expect:|r no All / Offense / Defense buttons; a small funnel icon at the right end of the top row, muted. Click it: a menu under it with |cffffd100None|r (marked), |cffffd100Offense|r, |cffffd100Defense|r, |cffffd100Utility|r. Choose Utility: the menu closes, the header reads \"Active utility spells\", only spells whose text has no damage or defensive words are listed, and the icon turns gold with a dot. /reload: still Utility. Choose None: every spell again, icon muted. Tell us any spell you think is in the wrong filter." },
    { key = "E1z54", text = "[E1z54] (QoL 0.7.40: each item's change is now in brackets beside its number, not under it: E1z197.) (QoL 0.7.24; Changes, Xaya: \"Rename the section to \"Changes\" and show stat changes and then \"Spell Changes\". show added proc differences and anticipated RPPM where applicable\"; \"Stat DR threshold and diminishing return true >> lost rating information\") |cffffd100Expect:|r no \"Side by side\" or \"What it changes\"; one |cffffd100Changes|r section: Stat || Pt value || Equipped || each item, each item's number with its change under it; under a secondary rating an item changes, |cffffd100DR threshold|r (equipped now, then each item; \"crosses N\" in orange when it passes one) and |cffffd100True / lost|r (\"T 1,423\" with \"L 4.8\" under it). Then |cffffd100Stat effects|r, then |cffffd100Spell Changes|r (your spells' numbers now and with each item; a ring with more Agility raises them), then, when an item has an on-use or proc effect, |cffffd100On-use and proc effects|r with the tooltip's own words for the equipped item and each picked one, what changes (\"adds an effect\", \"loses the equipped item's effect\", \"a different effect\"), and \"RPPM not given by the game\" (no number). Compare a T / L pair with the Stats tab's Stat Weights row for the same stat: the Equipped column must match it." },
    { key = "E1z63", text = "[E1z63] (QoL 0.7.24; Xaya: \"I did not ask for notes ...\"; her answer \"Remove it entirely\") Stat Calculator > Stats, then drag the panel wide (760). |cffffd100Expect:|r the heads read exactly |cffffd100Stat || Rating || Current value || Pt value || Change|r at every width (no |cffffd100Note|r column); no grey note text anywhere (no \"before DR\", \"next at N rating (N away)\", \"101.8% of Agility, mastery\", \"cast any spell to read it\", \"with your numbers: not given by the game\"), not under a line and not in the hover. No \"(what feeds it)\" anywhere in the panel or its settings." },
    { key = "E1z64", text = "[E1z64] (QoL 0.7.24; her answer \"Assume yes for now\" for the Tooltip lines' own row) QoL > Character Toolkit (ticked). |cffffd100Expect:|r under it the rows Panel, Slot Overlays, Spell Math and |cffffd100Tooltip lines|r, each with its tick box; Panel has no Tooltips tab any more. Untick |cffffd100Tooltip lines|r, |cff88ccff/reload|r, hover Agility in the character window's stats. |cffffd100Expect:|r Blizzard's tooltip only. Tick it, hover again: the XayaUI block under Blizzard's text." },
    { key = "E1z65", text = "[E1z65] (QoL 0.7.27; REQUEST-LOG #58-#59, her answer \"Same, land it now\") On the install that ran QoL 0.7.22-0.7.24 (Extra width still 240), log in, open the character window (C). |cffffd100Expect:|r the window is 380 wide without the stats pane and 582 with it, not 578 / 780: |cff88ccff/xui reskin status|r prints \"Wider window: on, 42 px wider (338 -> 380)\" (or \"(540 -> 582)\" with the stats pane), and |cff88ccff/xui reskin options|r shows Extra width 42. Then set Extra width to 240, |cff88ccff/reload|r: it stays 240 (the step runs once). Note how the enchant and gem blocks look at 380 (the stand-in predicts most side blocks have no room)." },
    { key = "E1z82", text = "[E1z82] (QoL 0.7.31; REQUEST-LOG #10 / #39 / #75 / #76, her design: \"black box over the \"release\" button that says \"NO RELEASE\" (customizable)\", flavour texts \"Each death\", modifier \"Choice in settings\", \"by default raid only\") QoL > tick |cffffd100Release Guard|r. Die in a raid (QoL 0.7.39: Where has no Everywhere any more, see E1z93). |cffffd100Expect:|r a black box exactly over the death window's Release Spirit button: \"NO RELEASE\" and under it \"BAD MONKEY\"; clicking it does nothing; hold Shift: the box goes and the click releases you. Next death: \"death comes for us all\", then \"NOPE\" ... As a ghost: no box. Die in a dungeon with Where = Raids only: no box. Change the key to Ctrl: Shift no longer lets you through, Ctrl does. Untick it: no box. Tell us if the box ever covers the wrong button or stays after you are resurrected." },
    { key = "E2a", text = "[E2a] (QoL 0.7.32; Blizzard UI Reskin > Shopping List, S1-S2) Switch Shopping List on. Track a recipe in your profession window (one with reagents you partly have). |cffffd100Expect:|r the Shopping List panel (movable) with \"Missing on your gear\", \"To buy\" and the recipe's name with each required reagent and have / need, matching Blizzard's objective tracker numbers; buy or loot a reagent: the count updates. Finished lines ticked and dimmed. |cff88ccff/xui shop|r hides and shows it. Switch it off: the panel goes; |cff88ccff/xui shop status|r says off." },
    { key = "E2b", text = "[E2b] (QoL 0.7.32; suggestions, S4-S7) Unequip a ring's enchant (or wear an item that takes one but has none) and an item with an empty socket. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Ring: <your usual enchant>\" (or \"no enchant / nothing used yet\" if XayaUI never saw one there) and \"<slot>: <your usual gem> x<n>\", each with have / need from your bags. Settings > Your defaults: type an enchant name for that slot: the panel shows it instead; empty it: back to the most used. \"Forget what this character used\" clears the counts." },
    { key = "E2c", text = "[E2c] (QoL 0.7.32; Select other, + Add, Auction House, S8-S10) Open the Auction House. Click a suggestion's name. |cffffd100Expect:|r the name in the Auction House search box and the search runs (Buy tab). Click \"Other\": what you used, what is in your bags; \"List what the Auction House has\": its enchants for that slot (gems: its gems) join the list, and Blizzard's results list shows them too. Click one: it becomes the suggestion for now and is searched; \"Default\": it becomes your default. \"+ Add\": it appears under To buy with have / need; buy it: the line ticks; x removes it. With the Auction House closed a name click does nothing but its hover. Note any \"Interface action failed\" or Lua error." },
    { key = "E2d", text = "[E2d] (QoL 0.7.32; Blizzard's Professions list restyled, S3) With \"Restyle Blizzard's Professions list\" on and a tracked recipe: |cffffd100Expect:|r the objective tracker's Professions header without its banner art, header text in the theme's label colour, recipe names and unfinished reagents in the theme's text colour, finished reagents muted. Accept a quest / complete an objective / enter combat: no \"Interface action failed\", the quest item buttons still work. Switch it off and /reload: Blizzard's own colours. Note it if another UI addon also skins the tracker." },
    { key = "E2f", text = "[E2f] (Options 0.6.50; Xaya 2026-11-04: \"default, expiration, name, important, manual\") Open a dynamic group's page > Group tab > Sort. |cffffd100Expect:|r the list reads Default, Expiration, Name, Important, Manual (in that order, \"Manual\" without \"(your order)\"); a group that was on Manual still shows Manual; \"Save order and reload\" shows with Manual." },
    { key = "E2g", text = "[E2g] (QoL 0.7.32; C9, Xaya 2026-11-06: \"Stay dimmed, allow user to \"clear\" manually — prompt user after all reagents are found in bag if they want to stop tracking\") Track a recipe you are one reagent short of. |cffffd100Expect:|r no question. Get the last reagent. |cffffd100Expect:|r under the recipe's title \"All reagents are in your bags. Stop tracking it?\" with |cffffd100Stop|r and |cffffd100Keep|r. Keep: the question goes and does not come back until a reagent is short again. Stop: the recipe leaves the panel AND Blizzard's objective tracker. The |cffffd100x|r on a recipe's title does the same at any time. Finished lines stay ticked and dimmed until cleared." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-e-4", { title = "5. E. XayaUI QoL (4 of 4)", order = 504.04, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "E2h", text = "[E2h] (QoL 0.7.32; C10, \"1 as long as prismatic / diamond is always considered\") Wear gear with an empty socket and no Eversong Diamond (or this expansion's one-per-character gem) in any socket. |cffffd100Expect:|r the first empty socket's line reads \"<slot>: <diamond> (one per character)\" (or \"one-per-character gem (none worn)\" when none was seen yet), the other sockets ask for your normal gem; Select other on it lists only such gems, and its Default button (or the settings box \"One-per-character gem (diamond)\") makes one your default for it. Socket a diamond: the line goes and every empty socket asks for your normal gem. Note it if a diamond is not recognised (the game must report it as unique-equipped, limit 1)." },
    { key = "E2", text = "[E2] Switch |cffffd100XayaUI QoL|r off, relog. |cffffd100Expect:|r no cursor changes, no QoL tab, no error." },
    { key = "E3", text = "[E3] (QoL 0.7.18, Options 0.6.40) QoL tab. |cffffd100Expect:|r in the left pane a tick box just left of |cffffd100Cursor Highlight|r and of |cffffd100Gradient Cursor Trail|r (where an open / close arrow would be; their names do not move), and one right after the arrow of |cffffd100Character Toolkit|r (its name moves right by the box's width only); |cffffd100Cursor|r itself has no box. Each box shows your saved state; hovering it names the switch and says what it does. With Cursor selected, click Cursor Highlight's box. |cffffd100Expect:|r the shape appears at the mouse at once, the box ticks, the right pane still shows Cursor (the row was not opened), and no noticeable pause. Click it again. |cffffd100Expect:|r the shape is gone. Open Cursor Highlight's page. |cffffd100Expect:|r no on/off switch on it; its tabs show while it is on, only the intro while it is off. Tick Character Toolkit's box. |cffffd100Expect:|r Panel, Slot Overlays and Spell Math appear under it, each with its own box (Panel ticked), and the Character Toolkit box is still under the mouse (it did not move). Open the character window (C): the panel shows. Untick Panel's box: the panel hides. Tick Slot Overlays' box: the slot marks appear. Untick Character Toolkit's box: its parts leave the list, the panel and marks go. Its own page has no switches any more (the tooltip lines switch is on Panel > Tooltips). Report any name in the QoL list that is cut off (\"...\") and was not before." },
    { key = "E1z91", text = "[E1z91] (QoL 0.7.35; REQUEST-LOG UI-34, UI-35, UI-36, UI-37, UI-38) Character window > Stat Calc, Gear: compare an item in a slot whose equipped item has an Equip / Use / proc line (her case: the Guillotine item). |cffffd100Expect|r under On-use and proc effects: \"Equipped: <the equipped item's name>\", then on the next line the game's effect text; for each compared item \"Compared: <its name>\", then its effect text on the next line; \"<name>: a different effect ...\" lines as before. When the equipped item belongs to a set: \"Set: <set name> (with <the other equipped set items>)\" under it, and under each compared item \"Also in <set name>\" (green) or \"Not in <set name>: replacing the equipped item breaks the set\" (orange). Vengeance (or any spec whose mastery gives armor from the primary stat): the row under Armor reads \"From mastery: Fel Blood passive\" (the mastery's own name for other specs). Screenshot please." },
    { key = "E1z195", text = "[E1z195] (QoL 0.7.40; REQUEST-LOG #87 / #88, her words \"put the numerical contributions on a row for each stat -- make each stat collapsible, in which case the rows bundle neatly into the tooltip\", her answers \"\\\"Modified By\\\" only\", \"Collapsed\", \"Only \\\"Modifies\\\" column\"; walkthrough |cff88ccff/xui dev qa|r > \"Stat Calculator: contribution rows, folding, Modifies column\") Stat Calculator > Stats. |cffffd100Expect:|r the heads read |cffffd100Stat || Current value || Pt value || Change || Modifies|r (Rating too over Secondaries / Tertiaries; no \"Influences\", no \"Modified By\"). Every stat that has lines under it shows a small |cffffd100+|r left of its name and no lines under it (folded is the default). |cffffd100Attack Power|r's Modifies cell reads only Damage per second. Hover Attack Power. |cffffd100Expect:|r the hover lists From Agility (or Strength) with its number, From Mastery where your mastery raises attack power, and \"Click: show these rows under the stat.\" Click Attack Power. |cffffd100Expect:|r |cffffd100-|r, and one row per contribution one indent in, each with its number in Current value: |cffffd100from Agility +2,616|r, |cffffd100from Mastery +27.80%|r. Type a number in Agility's Change box: under |cffffd100from Agility|r's number its new value with its sign in the accent colour. |cff88ccff/reload|r and open the panel. |cffffd100Expect:|r Attack Power still open, the others folded. Click it again: folded." },
    { key = "E1z200", text = "[E1z200] (Options 0.6.64; REQUEST-LOG B6 / ATTR-1, reading taken; her words \"increase the gutter by 10px / credits and attribution are h1 / subheaders (code, ideas and design, etc) h2 / each section under a subheader should have an unrounded box with rows (no columns) on a slightly less transparent background (10%)\"; walkthrough \"Credits + Acknowledgements: h1 / h2, one box per section\") Click the version text in the settings window's bottom-left corner, then Info > |cffffd100Credits + Acknowledgements|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Credits and attribution\" as the big heading with no paragraph under it; each section heading (|cffffd100Code|r, |cffffd100Ideas and design|r, |cffffd100Sounds|r, |cffffd100Game art|r) a plain heading in normal case: no arrow, no count, no capitals, no line under it, and it does not fold; under each, one square box holding all of that section's credits as rows one under the other (no columns), its background a little less see-through than the pane; 10 px more room than before between one section's box and the next heading." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-f-1", { title = "5. F. XayaUI Bonus Features (1 of 2)", order = 505.01, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "F1", text = "[F1] |cff88ccff/xui notes|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the Notepad box with its icon toolbar (icons, not green squares). Type, close, reopen: the text is still there." },
    { key = "F2", text = "[F2] Bonus Features > Data Panels (Bonus 0.6.11: tick the box next to it in the left pane first): switch on the left panel. |cffffd100Expect:|r the strip appears with its data. Hover the FPS block: addon CPU and memory lines." },
    { key = "F3", text = "[F3] Hover a spell or item. |cffffd100Expect:|r ID lines as configured on Bonus Features > Tooltips." },
    { key = "F4", text = "[F4] Chat and Bonus both on: the Chat Bar and the data panels both show their blocks. Then switch only |cffffd100XayaUI Chat|r off: the data panels still work. Then only |cffffd100Bonus|r off (Chat on): the Chat Bar still works." },
    { key = "F6", text = "[F6] (Bonus 0.6.8) |cff88ccff/xui calc 23,249 / 3,472|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r chat prints |cff88ccff23,249 / 3,472 = 6.696141|r. |cff88ccff/xui calc 1/0|r: |cffffd100Expect:|r |cff88ccffcalc: cannot divide by zero (1/0)|r. |cff88ccff/xui calc|r alone: |cffffd100Expect:|r the Calculator window opens in the middle of the screen with a typing line and 20 keys, none of them cut off. Click 1, 2, +, 3, =: |cffffd100Expect:|r 15 shows, and the line above lists |cff88ccff12+3 = 15|r. Type |cff88ccff200*15%|r and press Enter: |cffffd100Expect:|r 30. Move the window, |cff88ccff/reload|r, |cff88ccff/xui calc|r: |cffffd100Expect:|r it opens where you left it. Escape: |cffffd100Expect:|r it closes. The minimap button's list has |cffffd100Calculator|r." },
    { key = "F8", text = "[F8] (Bonus 0.6.11) Bonus Features > Utilities. |cffffd100Expect:|r a short overview naming Calculator and Notepad. Click Calculator. |cffffd100Expect:|r what it is, what a sum can hold, how to open it (with |cff88ccff/xui calc 23,249 / 3,472|r giving |cff88ccff23,249 / 3,472 = 6.696141|r), and an |cffffd100Open calculator|r button. Click the button. |cffffd100Expect:|r the calculator opens with the cursor in its line; a second click leaves it open." },
    { key = "F9", text = "[F9] (Bonus 0.6.12, V14 off costs nothing) Bonus Features > Tooltips: untick |cffffd100Show IDs on tooltips|r, |cffffd100Show player item level on hover|r, |cffffd100Show count and % on hostile units|r and |cffffd100Show formula lines on spell tooltips|r (each tab), |cff88ccff/reload|r. Hover a spell, an item and a player. |cffffd100Expect:|r no XayaUI lines at all. Tick |cffffd100Show IDs on tooltips|r again (no reload). |cffffd100Expect:|r hovering a spell shows its Spell ID line at once. Untick it: the line is gone at once. Each of the four switches' tooltips says a /reload removes the tooltip hooks fully." },
    { key = "F10", text = "[F10] (Bonus 0.6.12; since Bonus 0.6.14 the row's box is the whole Notepad and |cffffd100Show Notepad|r is on its page: F15) Untick |cffffd100Show Notepad|r on Bonus Features > Utilities > Notepad (the box hides), |cff88ccff/reload|r, then enter and leave combat on a training dummy. |cffffd100Expect:|r no notepad, no error. Tick it. |cffffd100Expect:|r the box appears where you left it with its toolbar; with |cffffd100Formatting tools|r off there is no format bar; tick |cffffd100Formatting tools|r: the format bar appears under the toolbar. Untick |cffffd100Show toolbar|r, |cff88ccff/reload|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the box shows without a toolbar; tick it again: the toolbar appears." },
    { key = "F11", text = "[F11] (Bonus 0.6.12) Two characters with XayaUI in one party. On the receiver, Notepad page > Share: untick |cffffd100Accept notes shared by other XayaUI users|r, |cff88ccff/reload|r. The sender shares a note to Party (toolbar menu > Share this note...). |cffffd100Expect:|r the sender's chat says \"Note shared (N parts sent).\" and the receiver gets no offer window. On the receiver tick |cffffd100Accept notes shared...|r (no reload), the sender shares again. |cffffd100Expect:|r the offer window with Save / Dismiss. Its tooltip says the message name stays registered until a /reload." },
    { key = "F13", text = "[F13] (Bonus 0.6.13; 0.6.15; since Bonus 0.6.18 the \"via ...\" text follows XayaUI Dev Assist, not Advanced Debugging: F19) XayaUI Dev Assist on. Bonus Features > Tooltips: Aura IDs and the icon ID option on. Out of combat, as Vengeance with Fiery Brand in your Cooldown Manager, hover Fiery Brand on your action bar. |cffffd100Expect:|r each \"Aura ID:\" line ends in grey with where it was found (\"via this tooltip\", \"via Cooldown Manager\", \"via your casts\", \"via buff on you\" or \"via recorded earlier\"), and no \"Aura icon ID\" line repeats the number on the \"Icon ID:\" line (1344647 shows once). Hover a food item with a Well Fed block. |cffffd100Expect:|r its \"Aura icon ID\" line is still there. |cff88ccff/xuitt aura 204021|r: |cffffd100Expect:|r \"tooltip shows:\" names the same sources. Send a screenshot of the Fiery Brand tooltip: which source each ID shows helps settle which of 207771 / 207744 lands on the enemy." },
    { key = "F12", text = "[F12] (Bonus 0.6.12) Bonus Features > Data Panels: tick its box with the Left Panel on. |cffffd100Expect:|r the panel shows and its clock / FPS numbers update every second; hover-only panels (Mouseover) fade in on hover. Untick the box. |cffffd100Expect:|r the panel hides. Tick the box with every panel's |cffffd100Enable|r off. |cffffd100Expect:|r no panel, no error; switch the Left Panel on: it shows at once and updates." },
    { key = "F14", text = "[F14] (Bonus 0.6.14; Xaya: \"yes, give an enable / disable \"Enhanced Tooltips\" as a feature\") Bonus Features. |cffffd100Expect:|r the row reads |cffffd100Enhanced Tooltips|r with a tick box (ticked); its page still has the four switches (IDs, Item level, Enemy forces, Formulas). Untick the row's box, |cff88ccff/reload|r, hover a spell, an item and an enemy. |cffffd100Expect:|r no XayaUI line on any tooltip, no error. Tick it: the ID lines are back at once." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-f-2", { title = "5. F. XayaUI Bonus Features (2 of 2)", order = 505.02, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "F15", text = "[F15] (Bonus 0.6.14; Xaya: \"It should only enable or disable notepad functionality in its entirety\") Bonus Features > Utilities. |cffffd100Expect:|r Notepad's row has a tick box (ticked); its page starts with |cffffd100Show Notepad|r. Tick Show Notepad: the box appears. Untick the row's box. |cffffd100Expect:|r the box and any Restore / export window close; the page's controls grey out; |cff88ccff/xui notes|r says the Notepad is off; the minimap list has no Notes row; a party member sharing a note gets no offer window on your side. |cff88ccff/reload|r: still nothing of it. Tick the row's box: the box comes back where it was (Show Notepad stayed ticked), your notes intact." },
    { key = "F16", text = "[F16] (Bonus 0.6.15; replaced by F19 since Bonus 0.6.18: Advanced Debugging no longer decides the \"via ...\" text) Settings > Debugging: untick |cffffd100Advanced Debugging|r. Hover Fiery Brand again (Aura IDs and icon IDs on). |cffffd100Expect:|r the \"Aura ID:\" lines show the ID and name only, with no grey \"via ...\" at the end; 1344647 still shows only once. |cff88ccff/xuitt aura 204021|r: |cffffd100Expect:|r its \"tooltip shows:\" line has no \"via\" either. Tick Advanced Debugging again: |cffffd100Expect:|r the grey \"via ...\" comes back on the next hover." },
    { key = "F17", text = "[F17] (Bonus 0.6.16; Xaya 2026-11-06: \"Calculator needs its own enable / disable toggle\") Bonus Features > Utilities. |cffffd100Expect:|r Calculator's row has a tick box left of its name, ticked, like Notepad's. Hover it. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Calculator\" and \"Turns the Calculator on or off as a whole ...\". Open the calculator with |cff88ccff/xui calc|r, then untick the box. |cffffd100Expect:|r the calculator window closes; the right-hand page does not change; the Calculator page's |cffffd100Open calculator|r button is greyed out. Type |cff88ccff/xui calc|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r it prints only |cff88ccffThe Calculator is off: tick it in Bonus Features > Utilities > Calculator.|r; no window. Type |cff88ccff/xui calc 2+2|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r chat prints |cff88ccff2+2 = 4|r (sums in chat keep working while it is off); no window. Open the XayaUI minimap button's list. |cffffd100Expect:|r no Calculator row (Notes still there if the Notepad is on). |cff88ccff/reload|r with it unticked, then |cff88ccff/xui calc|r again. |cffffd100Expect:|r the same line, no window, no Lua error. Tick the box. |cffffd100Expect:|r |cff88ccff/xui calc|r opens the window where you left it, with your earlier sums still listed; the minimap list has Calculator again." },
    { key = "F18", text = "[F18] (Bonus 0.6.17; Xaya 2026-11-05, CHAT-6: \"/notes /calc to be commands that the addon recognizes and accepts in the console to open the notes and calculator respectively\") With the Notepad and the Calculator both ticked on, type |cff88ccff/notes|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the Notepad shows; |cff88ccff/notes|r again hides it. Type |cff88ccff/calc|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the calculator window opens; |cff88ccff/calc|r again closes it. Type |cff88ccff/calc 23,249 / 3,472|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r chat prints \"23,249 / 3,472 = 6.696141\". Untick the Calculator, type |cff88ccff/calc|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"The Calculator is off: tick it in Bonus Features > Utilities > Calculator.\"; |cff88ccff/calc 2+2|r still prints \"2+2 = 4\". Untick the Notepad, /reload, type |cff88ccff/notes|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the game says it does not know the command (it is not registered while the Notepad is off); tick the Notepad on and type |cff88ccff/notes|r without a /reload. |cffffd100Expect:|r the Notepad shows. If another addon of yours already uses /notes or /calc, that addon keeps it: say which one, and check |cff88ccff/xui notes|r / |cff88ccff/xui calc|r still work." },
    { key = "F19", text = "[F19] (Bonus 0.6.18; REQUEST-LOG #81, Xaya 2026-11-06: \"Tooltip, Dev Assist on\") Advanced Debugging on (Settings > Debugging). XayaUI Dev Assist |cffffd100off|r, |cff88ccff/reload|r. Bonus Features > Tooltips: Aura IDs on. As Vengeance, hover Fiery Brand. |cffffd100Expect:|r each \"Aura ID:\" line shows the ID and name, with no grey \"via ...\" at the end. Dev Assist |cffffd100on|r, |cff88ccff/reload|r, hover it again. |cffffd100Expect:|r each \"Aura ID:\" line ends in grey with \"via this tooltip\", \"via Cooldown Manager\", \"via your casts\", \"via buff on you\" or \"via recorded earlier\". Untick Advanced Debugging and hover again: the \"via ...\" stays (it follows Dev Assist only). Screenshot both tooltips please." },
    { key = "F21", text = "[F21] (Bonus 0.6.20; Xaya 2026-11-06 \"Also in game tooltips\", REQUEST-LOG S8-10) Bonus Features > Enhanced Tooltips, tab |cffffd100Type colours|r: |cffffd100Colour damage schools and dispel types|r is ticked by default. Hover a spell whose text says \"... fire damage ...\" (for example Immolation Aura) and a buff of yours whose tooltip says \"Magic\" at the top right. |cffffd100Expect:|r the spell's \"fire damage\" reads \"Fire Damage\" in the game's Fire colour (orange); \"Magic\" at the top right is in the Magic colour (blue); other words are unchanged. Untick the switch, hover again. |cffffd100Expect:|r the text is exactly as the game writes it. With every Enhanced Tooltips section off (IDs, Item level, Enemy forces, Formulas, Type colours), nothing of XayaUI runs on a hovered tooltip. English game client only." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-h-1", { title = "5. H. Import / Export and backups", order = 506.01, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "H1", text = "[H1] Right-click a rule > Export. Copy the text. Press |cffffd100Import|r (top bar), paste. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Readable rules\", then Import adds it as a new folder \"Imported: ...\"." },
    { key = "H2", text = "[H2] Settings > UI Options > Theme: export the theme. Paste that theme text into the |cffffd100Import|r button's window. |cffffd100Expect:|r \"Readable: a theme\"; Import applies it. Paste the same theme text into Import / Export > Import rules. |cffffd100Expect:|r a message that this text holds a theme and where themes are imported." },
    { key = "H3", text = "[H3] Paste an export you made with 0.5.x (if you kept one). |cffffd100Expect:|r it still imports." },
    { key = "H4", text = "[H4] Start an import in combat (training dummy). |cffffd100Expect:|r a line that it will be imported when combat ends; after combat it is there." },
    { key = "H5", text = "[H5] Import / Export > Backups: name one, |cffffd100Save a backup|r, change a rule, |cffffd100Load (replace)|r the backup. |cffffd100Expect:|r the rule is back as it was." },
} })
