QA.Register("chk-j-1", { title = "5. J. Dev Assist (1 of 2)", order = 508.01, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "J7", text = "[J7] (GameDump 0.6.0) |cff88ccff/combatlog|r (chat says logging is on), then |cff88ccff/xuidev probe on|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r |cff88ccffprobe: ON.|r and a line with how many spells were checked; no Lua error. |cff88ccff/xuidev probe status|r prints a header line and 12 numbered lines (11 before Dev Assist 0.7.1); line |cff88ccff1 context|r says |cff88ccffcombat log true|r." },
    { key = "J8", text = "[J8] (GameDump 0.6.0) On a training dummy, get a proc that lights a button (for example Boiling Point on Blood Boil) 3 times, then pull an open-world mob group with nameplates shown. |cffffd100Expect:|r no Lua error. |cff88ccff/xuidev probe status|r: line 2 shows a glow show count of 3 or more; line 5 shows enemy cast counts above 0; line 6 shows plates added above 0." },
    { key = "J9", text = "[J9] (GameDump 0.6.0) |cff88ccff/reload|r while the probe is on. |cffffd100Expect:|r chat says |cff88ccffprobe: ON (resumed after a reload)|r. Then |cff88ccff/xuidev probe off|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r |cff88ccffprobe: OFF|r with an entry count. Fight the dummy again, then |cff88ccff/xuidev probe status|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the first status line reads |cff88ccffprobe: off:|r and its entry count did not change." },
    { key = "J10", text = "[J10] (GameDump 0.6.0) Solo, target a mob and type |cff88ccff/xuidev probe mark|r out of combat, then once in combat. |cffffd100Expect:|r each time a chat line says whether SetRaidTarget ran or failed, and whether you were in combat. If the game shows a \"blocked\" box, click Ignore and note it in the report. No marker appears unless you typed the command." },
    { key = "J11", text = "[J11] (GameDump 0.6.0) |cff88ccff/xuidev probe spells 59052 abc|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r a chat line for 59052 with its cast and aura secrecy; |cff88ccffabc|r is ignored. Then |cff88ccff/xuidev save|r and upload |cff88ccffXayaUI_DevAssist.lua|r: it holds a |cff88ccffprobe|r table with |cff88ccfflog|r, |cff88ccffanchors|r and |cff88ccffsecrecy|r." },
    { key = "J12", text = "[J12] (Dev Assist 0.7.0) Copy the new |cff88ccffXayaUI_DevAssist|r folder into AddOns and leave the old |cff88ccffXayaUI_GameDump|r folder there. Log in. |cffffd100Expect:|r the AddOns list shows |cffffd100XayaUI Dev Assist 0.7.0|r; at login one chat line says the old copy is switched off from the next /reload, to delete its folder, and that its captures stay in |cff88ccffXayaUI_GameDump.lua|r. |cff88ccff/reload|r: |cffffd100Expect:|r the old one is unticked in the AddOns list and the message does not come back. Type |cff88ccff/xuidev|r and |cff88ccff/xuidump|r: |cffffd100Expect:|r both open the Dev Assist window. Settings > Debugging: |cffffd100Expect:|r a \"Dev Assist (separate tool)\" box whose |cffffd100Open Dev Assist|r button opens the same window, and in \"What to send\" a second box for |cff88ccffXayaUI_DevAssist.lua|r. Note in the QA notes whether the old copy was switched off for this character only or for all (not documented)." },
    { key = "J13", text = "[J13] (Dev Assist 0.7.1) Out of combat in the open world, target a mob with its nameplate shown and type |cff88ccff/xuidev instance|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r |cff88ccffinstance: read N unit(s) you can see now.|r and three summary lines: the first counts at least 1 creature with a name; the third names the zone's instance with its number and a Mythic+ season line (numbers, or |cff88ccffnil|r where the game gives none); no Lua error. |cff88ccff/xuidev instance clear|r, then |cff88ccff/xuidev instance status|r: |cffffd100Expect:|r |cff88ccff0 creatures|r." },
    { key = "J14", text = "[J14] (Dev Assist 0.7.1) In a dungeon (Mythic+ if you can), |cff88ccff/xuidev probe on|r, then before each pull look at the mobs so their nameplates show; pull and play normally; after the run |cff88ccff/xuidev instance status|r, then |cff88ccff/xuidev save|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r no Lua error; the summary counts creatures with names and, in Mythic+, creatures with a Mythic+ count; the second line counts hidden sightings in combat. The file's |cff88ccffinstance|r table holds |cff88ccffcreatures|r (spells cast and auras per creature), |cff88ccffinstances|r with the dungeon's |cff88ccffstep|r and its criteria, and |cff88ccffseason|r. Note in the QA notes whether creature IDs were readable in combat (the second line) and send the file." },
    { key = "J15", text = "[J15] (Dev Assist 0.7.2) |cff88ccff/xuidev probe on|r, then play out of combat for 5 minutes (any class). |cff88ccff/xuidev probe status|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r line 2 ends with |cff88ccffN proc art hides had no spell ID (counted, not logged)|r when the game sent such hides, and the header line's entries-kept number stays well under 6,000 for those 5 minutes (before 0.7.2 those hides filled the log at about two a second)." },
    { key = "J16", text = "[J16] (Dev Assist 0.7.3) Out of combat, type |cff88ccff/xuidev char|r, then |cff88ccff/xuidev save|r (reloads) and open |cff88ccffWTF/Account/<account>/SavedVariables/XayaUI_DevAssist.lua|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r the character record's |cffffd100ilvlEquipped|r holds your equipped item level (before 0.7.3 it was always empty), beside |cffffd100ilvl|r." },
    { key = "J18", text = "[J18] (Dev Assist 0.7.12; REQUEST-LOG A15 P-5; walkthrough: |cff88ccff/xui dev qa|r > \"Performance: send back a recorded run (J18)\", which counts what the record holds) After J17's Confirm, upload |cff88ccffWTF/Account/<account>/SavedVariables/XayaUI.lua|r. On a computer with the repository: |cff88ccffpython3 tools/perf_report.py XayaUI.lua --out report.md|r. |cffffd100Expect:|r a \"Run 1\" section with the dungeon name, one row per fight (bosses named, the rest \"trash\"), a \"Per addon\" table with a line for each loaded XayaUI addon plus \"(all addons)\" and \"(whole game)\", and a \"What to look at first\" list. Values the game hid show \"?\"." },
    { key = "J19", text = "[J19] (Dev Assist 0.7.13; REQUEST-LOG A15 P-7 / P-8; walkthrough: |cff88ccff/xui dev qa|r > \"Performance: settings window memory (J19)\") |cff88ccff/reload|r without opening XayaUI's settings, then follow the walkthrough: a reading after the reload, one with the settings window used for a minute, one 30 s after closing it, one after \"Do it for me\" (a full cleanup). |cffffd100Expect:|r the last step's summary names the settings addon's memory at each reading, how much was leftover garbage and how much it keeps. Send that summary to Xaya. No Lua error." },
} })
QA.Register("chk-j-2", { title = "5. J. Dev Assist (2 of 2)", order = 508.02, generated = true, steps = {
    { key = "J20", text = "[J20] (core 0.6.63, Options 0.6.65, Dev Assist 0.7.14; REQUEST-LOG A15 P-9; walkthrough: |cff88ccff/xui dev qa|r > \"Performance: rule log only while it is read (J20)\") With the console window and the settings window closed (and, with Dev Assist on, \"Rule snapshots in combat\" and \"Rules firing and clearing\" unticked), fight for 15 s. |cffffd100Expect:|r no \"status snapshot\" and no FIRED / cleared lines reach the log (|cff88ccff/xui console|r afterwards shows none from that fight). Open the console and fight again. |cffffd100Expect:|r the snapshot lines at combat start and end are back. |cff88ccff/xui debug status|r still prints every rule. No Lua error." },
    { key = "J21", text = "[J21] (core 0.6.64, Dev Assist 0.7.15; REQUEST-LOG A15 P-10; walkthrough: |cff88ccff/xui dev qa|r > \"Performance: memory growth in combat (J21)\") Mark, fight a training dummy for 30 s, check. |cffffd100Expect:|r the note gives XayaUI core's and all Lua memory growth in KB per second; send it to Xaya (compare with the same fight on core 0.6.62 if you still have it). No Lua error." },
    { key = "J22", text = "[J22] (core 0.6.65, Dev Assist 0.7.16; REQUEST-LOG A15 P-11; walkthrough: |cff88ccff/xui dev qa|r > \"Performance: other addons' errors (J22)\") Play where another addon raises errors (for example the Plater mod in a key), then check. |cffffd100Expect:|r the note counts other addons' errors this session; |cff88ccff/xui report|r lists none of them. The game's own error display still shows them. No Lua error." },
    { key = "J23", text = "[J23] (core 0.6.66, Dev Assist 0.7.17; REQUEST-LOG A15 P-12; walkthrough: |cff88ccff/xui dev qa|r > \"Performance: rules that are not loaded (J23)\") Start the timer, fight a training dummy 30 s, check. |cffffd100Expect:|r the note gives switched-on and loaded rule counts, the engine's ms per step and Lua memory KB/s; send it to Xaya. Then switch on several rules that do not load here (another spec's) and repeat: |cffffd100Expect:|r ms per step and KB/s barely change. Rules that load fire as before. No Lua error." },
    { key = "J24", text = "[J24] (QoL 0.7.41, Dev Assist 0.7.16; REQUEST-LOG A15 P-13; walkthrough: |cff88ccff/xui dev qa|r > \"Performance: a still cursor (J24)\") With the Cursor Highlight or the cursor trail on: keep the mouse still 10 s and check, then move it 10 s and check. |cffffd100Expect:|r XayaUI_QoL's reading while still is close to nothing and lower than while moving; the highlight still follows the cursor at once when it moves (no lag, no jump), and the trail draws and fades as before. No Lua error." },
    { key = "J25", text = "[J25] (Chat 0.6.32, Bonus 0.6.26, Dev Assist 0.7.17; REQUEST-LOG A15 P-14; walkthrough: |cff88ccff/xui dev qa|r > \"Performance: the addon usage tooltip (J25)\") Hover the Chat Bar's frame rate block for 20 s. |cffffd100Expect:|r the tooltip still updates its CPU numbers once a second, ends with the grey line \"Includes the cost of reading these numbers.\", and the walkthrough counts one memory read for the hover. XayaUI_Chat's \"now\" share no longer jumps while hovering (compare with your earlier 9%). Same for a Bonus data panel block. No Lua error." },
    { key = "J27", text = "[J27] (Options 0.6.68, Dev Assist 0.7.18; REQUEST-LOG A15 P-16; walkthrough: |cff88ccff/xui dev qa|r > \"Performance: the settings window (J27)\") Open |cff88ccff/xui|r once, click one switch twice, leave the window open a minute, close it and clean up. |cffffd100Expect:|r one full redraw per open and per click (before: 3 per first open, 2 per click: 1,362 ms), XayaUI_Options grows little while idle, keeps only a few MB after closing (before: about 83 MB). The window looks and behaves as before (Rules sub-tab remembered, rows decorated, dropdowns wide enough). No Lua error." },
    { key = "J30", text = "[J30] (Dev Assist 0.7.30; REQUEST-LOG QR-1; walkthroughs: |cff88ccff/xui dev qa|r > \"Review window and questions (part 1)\", then after the /reload \"Review window and questions (part 2, after the /reload)\", and \"Review window: Open a walkthrough from it (part 3)\" started from the review window; each step pre-filled by the addon's own check) Log in after installing this build. |cffffd100Expect:|r a moment after the loading screen a window \"Review: what's new to test\" lists the QA walkthroughs new or changed since the build you last acknowledged (the first time: all of them), under area headings, each with its key, title, \"new\" / \"changed\", its last result and an |cffffd100Open|r button; a zone change does not open it again. |cffffd100Open|r a row: the runner starts that walkthrough; closing the runner brings the review back. |cffffd100Questions (N)|r: one question per screen with the area, your words in quotes, \"What we did without asking\", \"Keep it\" plus the other choices and a note; Next with nothing picked asks for an answer; Skip moves on; Back shows an earlier answer. |cffffd100Copy answers|r: a selected text box, one line per answer (Ctrl+C copies). Tick |cffffd100Don't show again until the next update|r and /reload: no window. Forget the acknowledged build (part 1's last step), then /reload while in combat with a training dummy: no window until combat ends. |cff88ccff/xui dev review|r and |cff88ccff/xui dev questions|r reopen them. No Lua error at any step." },
    { key = "J26", text = "[J26] (core 0.6.69, Options 0.6.66, Dev Assist 0.7.26; REQUEST-LOG A17 X-1; walkthrough: |cff88ccff/xui dev qa|r > \"Externals and raid defensives in combat (J26)\") Switch on the Externals rules, check out of combat. |cffffd100Expect:|r the note lists each aura rule, its IDs, whether the game's aura container draws it (or why not) and the guard state; send it to Xaya. Then get an external or raid defensive on you in combat and check while it is up. |cffffd100Expect:|r every rule whose aura the game hides is drawn by the container, and its icon with its time shows; the rule's status says \"the game hides this aura now\" in plain words. No Lua error." },
    { key = "J31", text = "[J31] (Options 0.6.69, Dev Assist 0.7.19; REQUEST-LOG A15 P-16; walkthrough: |cff88ccff/xui dev qa|r > \"Performance: a click with a rule open (J28)\") Open |cff88ccff/xui|r, click a rule in the sidebar, click one switch in its editor on and off; click another rule; use the rule's search box and open a result; rename the rule; drag the window to its narrowest. |cffffd100Expect:|r the switch changes at once (the window's own redraw time under 100 ms; before: about 1.4 s per click), every rule shows its own editor straight away (never empty, never the previous rule's), the search result opens its tab, the renamed row updates, the dropdowns still fit at the narrowest width. No Lua error." },
} })
